h the server, so I've queued it rather than risk it today.\n\n**Voice Flares (ADR-0028)**\n- The open model handles it, on our laptop. Ollama 0.40.2 reports audio for gemma4:e4b, and the model hears WAV passed in the `images` field.\n- On the camera screen, \"Say it instead\" records up to 10 s, converts it on the phone to 16 kHz WAV, and sends it to POST /api/v1/drafts/voice. The server passes it to the hub as a new voice-draft job (asyncapi voiceJob). Voice prompt v1 asks for the same {invite, alt} a photo gets, and enforce() runs on both sides.\n- It is hub-only: there is no cloud tier for voices. The audio is zero-filled, and the words heard never come back.\n- Live, through Render to this Mac's hub: \"Meet at the pond bench\" in 3.6 s.\n- The real-stack e2e (npm run e2e:voice) passes. It plays a macOS `say` fixture into the microphone, then runs a real MediaRecorder recording, the phone's WAV conversion, the server, the hub and Gemma.\n- Hub and contract tests are added, and the privacy page has a new line.\n- The live hub is restarted on the new code.\n\n**Crew Atlas (ADR-0029)**\n- Hot spots have OSM ids, so the phone's own map pack places them on an SVG map, with water, woods, streets and benches for context.\n- No tiles and no requests, so the crew's places never leave the phone.\n- It shows facts only, such as \"Met once · Oct 11\", with dot size by count.\n- There's no Gemma caption on purpose: it would mean sending decrypted places to the hub.\n- The sparks e2e on the real stack shows the Atlas. It loads on demand.\n\n**Tests:** unit tests are 678/62/26. e2e (plan, voice, sparks, demo, loop, telegram, field, pwa) passes, and kit a11y has 0 violations.\n\n**Next:** automations, then Sentry depth, the page audit, fresh-eyes round 4, media and the post."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"70332281-bb5d-42b3-bf63-8ae1b750fc0c","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfvxxHYg6BwuZay9Ubait","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"f7e7885c-0dd5-42