{"parentUuid":"852ae756-c7f5-41ca-82f4-5d3b28e2d850","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfw4yhVpFXqq47dm5jhtF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012LHAs3oGM2MsRPhmc8VVgN","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"<project>/flare\" && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='docs/post/draft.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nold='''- **The compass said \"close\" 49 times**'''\nnew='''- **The compass didn't point.** Testers saw rings and a flame, and nothing that read as an arrow. It now has an arrowhead on the dial's edge that turns on a spring and goes gold when you face the right way. On both real iPhone heading streams it moves less than 30° per 100 ms event and never takes the long way round.\n- **The compass said \"close\" 49 times**'''\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new,1); open(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nnode scripts/capture-media.ts 2>&1 | tail -1; node apps/web/test/e2e/demo.ts 2>&1 | tail -1; cp docs/design/redesign/after/demo-4-compass.jpg docs/post/media/04b-demo-compass-ahead.jpg; cp docs/design/redesign/after/demo-2a-friend.jpg docs/post/media/11-demo-friend-view.jpg; S=<tmp>/904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa/scratchpad; cp $S/v7-desk-demo.png docs/post/media/14-desktop-qr-note.png; sed -i '' 's#| 12-site-home-phone.png, 13-site-feature-cards.png | The website on a phone, and the feature cards on desktop | local build |#| 12-site-home-phone.png, 13-site-feature-cards.png | The website on a phone, and the feature cards on desktop | local build |\\n| 14-desktop-qr-note.png | The app on a desktop: the phone column and \"Made for your phone\" with a QR code | local build |#' docs/post/media/README.md; sed -i '' 's#| 04-friend-compass.jpg | Find them: 400 m. A headless browser has no compass, so it asks to hold the phone flat | capture-media.ts |#| 04-friend-compass.jpg | Find them: 400 m. A headless browser has no compass, so it asks to hold the phone flat | capture-media.ts |#' docs/post/media/README.md; git add docs/post && git commit -q -m \"Post and media in sync: the compass arrow, desktop QR note\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && git push -q 2>&1 | tail -1","description":"Post line, recapture media, commit","timeout":1200000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1853,"cache_read_input_tokens":752848,"output_tokens":1180,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":159},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1853,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1180,"cache_read_input_tokens":752848,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1853,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1853},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_012LHAs3oGM2MsRPhmc8VVgN":{"command":"cd \"<project>/flare\" && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='docs/post/draft.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nold='''- **The compass said \"close\" 49 times**'''\nnew='''- **The compass didn't point.** Testers saw rings and a flame, and nothing that read as an arrow. It now has an arrowhead on the dial's edge that turns on a spring and goes gold when you face the right way. On both real iPhone heading streams it moves less than 30° per 100 ms event and never takes the long way round.\n- **The compass said \"close\" 49 times**'''\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new,1); open(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nnode scripts/capture-media.ts 2>&1 | tail -1; node apps/web/test/e2e/demo.ts 2>&1 | tail -1; cp docs/design/redesign/after/demo-4-compass.jpg docs/post/media/04b-demo-compass-ahead.jpg; cp docs/design/redesign/after/demo-2a-friend.jpg docs/post/media/11-demo-friend-view.jpg; S=<tmp>/904c