{"parentUuid":"af630491-75c8-4cca-9b33-e5d2dfdba004","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfw5BDnWay8j72jZfxY9P","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything is live as 376115a. The live demo e2e and smoke both pass. Reporting, and proposing to bring round 5 forward:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":589,"cache_read_input_tokens":756694,"output_tokens":1128,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":205},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":589,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1128,"cache_read_input_tokens":756694,"cache_creation_input_tokens":589,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":589},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"4b5138bf-dca4-4935-80e6-17071a512119","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfw5BCZ797JV12TK6YQKh","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"4ee36084-08a4-46ab-82c7-3d0b34dfc100","timestamp":"2026-10-11T20:22:20.631Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"<project>/flare","sessionId":"904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"wondrous-tumbling-meteor"}
{"parentUuid":"4ee36084-08a4-46ab-82c7-3d0b34dfc100","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfw5BDnWay8j72jZfxY9P","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WCZJX1WeeNDLcwYpFGZJZR","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"uds:<socket>","summary":"Leftovers 1-6 live; propose round 5 now","message":"All six leftovers are done and live as 376115a. The live demo e2e and smoke both pass.\n\n1. **Compass arrow:** an arrowhead on the dial's edge turns with the needle on the same 530 ms spring, against a fixed mark at the top for where the phone points. Facing (lock at 15°, release at 25°) turns both gold.\n   - Tested against both real iPhone heading streams, replayed with a target 300 m away: under 30° per 100 ms event, never the long way round, and facing steady.\n   - The only bigger steps come after sensor gaps (0.5 to 14.5 s, the screen locked), and the spring animates those.\n2. **One mute control:** the sound button mutes tones and the spoken directions together, and stops a line mid-word. \"Mute voice\" is gone.\n3. **Writing your own:** while Gemma writes, \"Write my own\" is one tap away. A late draft never replaces words already chosen.\n4. **Place pre-fill:** this was a race. A position that arrived before the map pack had no name. It now gets named when the pack loads, and a typed place is kept. Two flow tests cover it.\n5. **Menu:** 5 items with no crew yet, 10 with one. \"Your crew\" has its own people icon, and the stray dot in screen-reader names is now a comma pause.\n6. **Desktop note:** \"Made for your phone\" with a QR code for the page, drawn locally by uqr 0.1.3 (MIT, no deps) and loaded only at 1000 px and wider.\n\nChecks: JS 146.8 / 145.9 KB, axe 0 on 88 views, Lighthouse 100. Unit and e2e (demo, sparks, plan, loop, telegram, pwa) all pass. The post and media are in sync: an added compass-arrow line in \"What I got wrong\", a recaptured compass shot and a desktop QR shot.\n\n**Proposal:** run fresh-eyes round 5 now (4:25 PM) instead of 7:30. It takes about 18 minutes, which leaves time to fix what it finds and redeploy before 8 PM, and still report the final score honestly. Then I hold for the founder's review at 9. Say if you'd rather keep 7:30. Until you answer I'll hold, with no changes to live.","type":"message","recipient":"uds:<socket>","recipient_kind":"session","content":"All six leftovers are done and live as 376115a. T…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":589,"cache_read_input_tokens":756694,"output_tokens":1128,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":205},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":589,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1128,"cache_read_input_tokens":756694,"cache_creation_input_tokens":589,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":589},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01WCZJX1WeeNDLcwYpFGZJZR":{"to":"uds:<socket>","summary":"Leftovers 1-6 live; propose round 5 now","message":"All six leftovers are done and live as 376115a. The live demo e2e and smoke both pass.\n\n1. **Compass arrow:** an arrowhead on the dial's edge turns with the needle on the same 530 ms spring, against a fixed mark at the top for where the phone points. Facing (lock at 15°, release at 25°) turns both gold.\n   - Tested against both real iPhone heading streams, replayed with a target 300 m away: under 30° per 100 ms event, never the long way round, and facing steady.\n   - The only bigger steps come after sensor gaps (0.5 to 14.5 s, the screen locked), and the spring animates those.\n2. **One mute control:** the sound button mutes tones and the spoken directions together, and stops a line mid-word. \"Mute voice\" is gone.\n3. **Writing your own:** while Gemma writes, \"Write my own\" is one tap away. A late draft never replaces words already chosen.\n4. **Place pre-fill:** this was a race. A position that arrived before the map pack had no name. It now gets named when the pack loads, and a typed place is kept. Two flow tests cover it.\n5. **Menu:** 5 items with no crew yet, 10 with one. \"Your crew\" has its own people icon, and the stray dot in screen-reader names is now a comma pause.\n6. **Desktop note:** \"Made for your phone\" with a QR code for the page, drawn locally by uqr 0.1.3 (MIT, no deps) and loaded only at 1000 px and wider.\n\nChecks: JS 146.8 / 145.9 KB, axe 0 on 88 views, Lighthouse 100. Unit and e2e (demo, sparks, plan, loop, telegram, pwa) all pass. The post and media are in sync: an added compass-arrow line in \"What I got wrong\", a recaptured compass shot and a desktop QR shot.\n\n**Proposal:** run fresh-eyes round 5 now (4:25 PM) instead of 7:30. It takes about 18 minutes, which leaves time to fix what it finds and redeploy before 8 PM, and still report the final score honestly. Then I hold for the founder's review at 9. Say if you'd rather keep 7:30. Until you answer I'll hold, with no changes to live."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"4b5138bf-dca4-4935-80e6-17071a512119","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cfw5BCZ797JV12TK6YQKh","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"dce030a1-ccfc-4116-b8a3-1b8a29ae9e80","timestamp":"2026-10-11T20:22:27.839Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"<project>/flare","sessionId":"904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"wondrous-tumbling-meteor"}
