{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-11T23:23:10.242Z","sessionId":"904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa","content":"<cross-session-message from=\"uds:<socket>\" from-session=\"local_beb3cc8c-e162-46cc-bd0a-f870e8717ebd\" from-name=\"Flare Manager(founders CTO)\" from-mode=\"prompting\">\nFounder feedback: the site reads as if you need to set up a model to use Flare. Nobody using Flare sets up anything. Please fix that, then push.\n\n1. Website. Change the home link \"Read the setup steps\" to \"Host your own copy\". The /run page title becomes \"Host your own copy\", and its first line says: using Flare needs nothing, you just open the link, and this page is only for people who want their own server. Fix og.run.desc to match.\n\n2. Make the model optional for self-hosting, and say so in three plain levels on /run and in README line 11:\n   - No AI keys: everything works, and you type the six words (place-word chips plus rules).\n   - A free Google AI Studio key: Gemma 4 in the cloud, with no GPU and no laptop.\n   - Ollama on your own machine: the private option, where the photo never leaves your machine.\n   Before you write the Gemini-only level, check that it really works: hub off, only GEMINI_API_KEY set, a full photo Flare via Ask cloud Gemma plus a Plan draft. Add an e2e for it if there isn't one.\n\n3. App, hub-down. \"Couldn't reach our laptop. Write your own?\" reads like it's broken, and judges will see it whenever the Mac sleeps. Rewrite it so it reads as a normal choice: pick a place word, or ask cloud Gemma. Keep the explicit tap for photos to the cloud. Check ai.hubFallback and ai.why.hub_down too.\n\n4. Post: make \"Nothing to install\" plain near the top. Our laptop serves everyone, and it isn't the reader's.\n\nWriting rules as before. Gates: copy key check, svelte-check, CI, axe 0, Lighthouse 100 on the site pages, live smoke after deploy. Don't add a Deploy to Render button unless you can test it without creating anything under the founder's accounts. Report back briefly.\n</cross-session-message>"}
