op.')) or 'laptop' in t.lower() or 'setup' in t.lower():\n    print(k,'|',v['kind'],'|',v.get('fixed',''),'|',t[:160])\nEOF\nsed -n 1,20p README.md; cat \"apps/web/src/routes/(site)/run/+page.svelte\" | head -40","description":"Copy keys, README top, run page"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"5ff0cd36-6540-49e7-8e06-51d73130cd5d","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CfwJyPtHTyK9aRvH1RviX","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"d7c5d81e-276d-434d-a9ee-e0c655cc65a6","timestamp":"2026-10-11T23:23:42.387Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"<project>/flare","sessionId":"904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"wondrous-tumbling-meteor"}
{"parentUuid":"d7c5d81e-276d-434d-a9ee-e0c655cc65a6","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fb97088b-b99e-4d84-9335-c833d3234c27","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011ZoCruR8st4wGnTg8BrsRM","type":"tool_result","content":"app.tier.hub | hint | SRS-AI-4 | Made on our laptop\ndevelop.heading | title |  | Your invite\ndevelop.writing | status |  | Writing a short invite…\ndevelop.editHint | hint |  | Photo not kept. Edit anything.\ndevelop.flameNote | message |  | This is your flame. It grows as friends say yes.\ndevelop.offline | status |  | Offline. Write six words. It sends later.\ndevelop.noSignal | message |  | No signal, so no draft.\ndevelop.hubDown | message |  | Couldn't reach our laptop. Write your own?\ndevelop.fieldLabel | label |  | Six words\ndevelop.template | placeholder | FR-AI-1 template | Outside at {spot}. Come?\ndevelop.tooLong | error |  | Keep it to six words.\ndevelop.empty | error |  | Write up to six words.\ndevelop.use | button |  | Use this\ndevelop.useMine | button |  | Use my words\ndevelop.writeOwn | button |  | Write my own\nladder.madeHub | hint |  | Made on our laptop from OpenStreetMap and today's sunset.\ncheck.tier1 | message |  | Six words come from our laptop.\nmap.drafting | status |  | Drafting tags on our laptop…\nmap.photoAsk | hint |  | A photo lets our laptop draft the tags. It's deleted after.\nmap.drafted | hint |  | Drafted from your photo on our laptop.\nmap.noDraft | hint |  | Our laptop couldn't draft tags. These are the usual ones.\nai.hubHeadline | title |  | Your words come from our laptop.\nai.hubBody | message |  | Our laptop runs Gemma 4 and replies in about 3 seconds.\nai.hubFallback | hint |  | If it can't be reached, you write the six words.\nai.run.photo | message | BR-AI-1 | Our laptop. If it can't answer in 6 s, you type.\nai.run.ladder | message |  | Our laptop. If it can't answer in 8 s, a template.\nai.never.photo | message | ADR-0011 | Your photo is never stored. Our laptop reads it in memory.\nai.why.offline | status |  | You were offline.\nai.why.network | status |  | The connection dropped.\nai.why.timeout | status |  | Our laptop took too long.\nai.why.hub_down | status |  | Our laptop wasn't connected.\nai.why.unusable | status |  | The answer didn't pass our checks.\nai.why.server_error | status |  | Our server had a problem.\nog.run.title | og-title |  | Run Flare yourself\nog.run.desc | og-desc |  | Flare is open source. Host your own copy, with the Gemma 4 model on a laptop with Ollama.\nsite.built.gemma | prose |  | Gemma 4 writes the invite and the Plan steps, on our laptop with Ollama.\nsite.built.google | prose |  | Google AI Studio runs Gemma 4 when our laptop is off.\nsite.home.readRun | prose |  | Read the setup steps.\nsite.privacy.p1 | prose |  | Photos are encrypted on your phone. The key is in the link, after the #, so our server can't open them. To write the invite, the photo goes once to our laptop, \nsite.privacy.l.hub | prose |  | To write the six words, your photo goes to our laptop over an encrypted link. It isn't stored. If the laptop can't be reached, you type them and nothing is sent\nsite.run.title | title |  | Run it yourself\nsite.run.body | prose |  | You don't need to install anything to use Flare. It is open source, so anyone can host a copy: the AI is the open Gemma 4 model, run with Ollama on a laptop.\nsite.run.note | prose |  | The repository link goes live when the repo is public. Setup steps are in the README.\nsite.run.needs | prose |  | You need Node 24.21 or later. For the photo AI, use a Mac or any machine with a GPU, running Ollama.\nsite.run.s1 | prose |  | Install it, set one secret, and start the server and web app.\nsite.run.s2 | prose |  | In a second terminal, on the machine with Ollama, start the AI hub.\nsite.run.s3 | prose |  | Open localhost:8787/hello/ and pick a photo. Six words come back in about 3.5 seconds.\nsite.run.db | prose |  | Postgres is optional for local runs. The tests use an in-memory Postgres.\nsite.run.license | prose |  | License: AGPL-3.0 or later. Map data © OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL. Model: Gemma 4, under the Gemma terms of use.\ndevelop.askCloud | button |  | Ask cloud Gemma\ndevelop.askCloudNote | message |  | Sends this photo to cloud Gemma. Google may review it.\nsite.privacy.l.cloud | prose | ADR-0022 | When our laptop is off, Plan drafts may come from Gemma in the cloud: DigitalOcean first, then Google AI Studio. They get the ask line only. A photo goes there \nsite.privacy.l.voiceFlare | prose |  | You can say your Flare instead of taking a photo. Up to 10 seconds of your voice goes to our laptop once, over the encrypted link. Gemma 4 writes the invite fro\nai.cloud.ladder | prose |  | Plan drafts, only when our laptop is off. It gets the ask line only.\n# Flare\n\nSnap where you are. If enough friends quietly say yes, it's on.\n\nFlare is an installable web app for small groups of friends (2 to 12). A host sends a photo of where they are, or a Plan for later. Friends say yes in private, with conditions if they like (\"after 2\", \"only with Amor\"). It lights only when enough people can come, it shrinks to a smaller plan instead of failing, it works for friends with low vision or limited mobility and with no signal, and it deletes itself within 5 minutes of ending.\n\nBuilt for the DEV Hacktoberfest Open-Source AI Challenge, Week 1 \"Touch Grass\". Field test: Sunday 2026-10-11, near Fairlane Town Center, Dearborn MI, on four iPhones.\n\n## Run it yourself\n\nYou need Node 24.21.0 or later ([.nvmrc](.nvmrc)). For the photo AI you also need a Mac (or any machine with a GPU) running [Ollama](https://ollama.com). Everything else is optional: `DATABASE_URL=pglite:memory` gives an in-memory Postgres, and without the hub the app falls back to typed words.\n\n**1. The server and the app**\n\n```bash\ngit clone https://github.com/Hotragn/flare && cd flare\nnpm ci\ncp .env.example .env        # set HUB_SECRET to any 32+ random characters\nnpm run check-env           # lists every setting as set, missing or default; never prints values\nnpm run build && npm start  # server and web app on http://localhost:8787\n<!-- Run it yourself (W6), the README's setup steps. Commands are code, not copy. -->\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { t } from \"#lib/copy/site.ts\";\n  import Seo from \"../Seo.svelte\";\n\n  const install = `git clone https://github.com/Hotragn/flare-outside && cd flare-outside\nnpm ci\ncp .env.example .env        # then set HUB_SECRET (32+ random characters)\nnpm run check-env           # reports set or missing, never values\nnpm run build && npm start  # server and web app on http://localhost:8787`;\n  const hub = `ollama pull gemma4:e4b-it-q4_K_M\nnpm run hub`;\n</script>\n\n<Seo path=\"/run/\" />\n\n<section class=\"band\">\n  <h1 class=\"t-title\">{t(\"site.run.title\")}</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">{t(\"site.run.body\")}</p>\n  <p>{t(\"site.run.needs\")}</p>\n  <ol class=\"run-steps\">\n    <!-- svelte-ignore a11y_no_noninteractive_tabindex (keyboard scroll, axe scrollable-region-focusable) -->\n    <li><p>{t(\"site.run.s1\")}</p><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>{install}</code></pre></li>\n    <!-- svelte-ignore a11y_no_noninteractive_tabindex (keyboard scroll, axe scrollable-region-focusable) -->\n    <li><p>{t(\"site.run.s2\")}</p><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>{hub}</code></pre></li>\n    <li><p>{t(\"site.run.s3\")}</p></li>\n  </ol>\n  <p>{t(\"site.run.db\")}</p>\n  <p class=\"t-small\">{t(\"site.run.note\")}</p>\n  <p class=\"t-small\">{t(\"site.run.license\")}</p>\n</section>","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"ed8de7d3-8ee9-4866-aa28-32b9a831870c","timestamp":"2026-10-11T23:23:47.135Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"app.tier.hub | hint | SRS-AI-4 | Made on our laptop\ndevelop.heading | title |  | Your invite\ndevelop.writing | status |  | Writing a short invite…\ndevelop.editHint | hint |  | Photo not kept. Edit anything.\ndevelop.flameNote | message |  | This is your flame. It grows as friends say yes.\ndevelop.offline | status |  | Offline. Write six words. It sends later.\ndevelop.noSignal | message |  | No signal, so no draft.\ndevelop.hubDown | message |  | Couldn't reach our laptop. Write your own?\ndevelop.fieldLabel | label |  | Six words\ndevelop.template | placeholder | FR-AI-1 template | Outside at {spot}. Come?\ndevelop.tooLong | error |  | Keep it to six words.\ndevelop.empty | error |  | Write up to six words.\ndevelop.use | button |  | Use this\ndevelop.useMine | button |  | Use my words\ndevelop.writeOwn | button |  | Write my own\nladder.madeHub | hint |  | Made on our laptop from OpenStreetMap and today's sunset.\ncheck.tier1 | message |  | Six words come from our laptop.\nmap.drafting | status |  | Drafting tags on our laptop…\nmap.photoAsk | hint |  | A photo lets our laptop draft the tags. It's deleted after.\nmap.drafted | hint |  | Drafted from your photo on our laptop.\nmap.noDraft | hint |  | Our laptop couldn't draft tags. These are the usual ones.\nai.hubHeadline | title |  | Your words come from our laptop.\nai.hubBody | message |  | Our laptop runs Gemma 4 and replies in about 3 seconds.\nai.hubFallback | hint |  | If it can't be reached, you write the six words.\nai.run.photo | message | BR-AI-1 | Our laptop. If it can't answer in 6 s, you type.\nai.run.ladder | message |  | Our laptop. If it can't answer in 8 s, a template.\nai.never.photo | message | ADR-0011 | Your photo is never stored. Our laptop reads it in memory.\nai.why.offline | status |  | You were offline.\nai.why.network | status |  | The connection dropped.\nai.why.timeout | status |  | Our laptop took too long.\nai.why.hub_down | status |  | Our laptop wasn't connected.\nai.why.unusable | status |  | The answer didn't pass our checks.\nai.why.server_error | status |  | Our server had a problem.\nog.run.title | og-title |  | Run Flare yourself\nog.run.desc | og-desc |  | Flare is open source. Host your own copy, with the Gemma 4 model on a laptop with Ollama.\nsite.built.gemma | prose |  | Gemma 4 writes the invite and the Plan steps, on our laptop with Ollama.\nsite.built.google | prose |  | Google AI Studio runs Gemma 4 when our laptop is off.\nsite.home.readRun | prose |  | Read the setup steps.\nsite.privacy.p1 | prose |  | Photos are encrypted on your phone. The key is in the link, after the #, so our server can't open them. To write the invite, the photo goes once to our laptop, \nsite.privacy.l.hub | prose |  | To write the six words, your photo goes to our laptop over an encrypted link. It isn't stored. If the laptop can't be reached, you type them and nothing is sent\nsite.run.title | title |  | Run it yourself\nsite.run.body | prose |  | You don't need to install anything to use Flare. It is open source, so anyone can host a copy: the AI is the open Gemma 4 model, run with Ollama on a laptop.\nsite.run.note | prose |  | The repository link goes live when the repo is public. Setup steps are in the README.\nsite.run.needs | prose |  | You need Node 24.21 or later. For the photo AI, use a Mac or any machine with a GPU, running Ollama.\nsite.run.s1 | prose |  | Install it, set one secret, and start the server and web app.\nsite.run.s2 | prose |  | In a second terminal, on the machine with Ollama, start the AI hub.\nsite.run.s3 | prose |  | Open localhost:8787/hello/ and pick a photo. Six words come back in about 3.5 seconds.\nsite.run.db | prose |  | Postgres is optional for local runs. The tests use an in-memory Postgres.\nsite.run.license | prose |  | License: AGPL-3.0 or later. Map data © OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL. Model: Gemma 4, under the Gemma terms of use.\ndevelop.askCloud | button |  | Ask cloud Gemma\ndevelop.askCloudNote | message |  | Sends this photo to cloud Gemma. Google may review it.\nsite.privacy.l.cloud | prose | ADR-0022 | When our laptop is off, Plan drafts may come from Gemma in the cloud: DigitalOcean first, then Google AI Studio. They get the ask line only. A photo goes there \nsite.privacy.l.voiceFlare | prose |  | You can say your Flare instead of taking a photo. Up to 10 seconds of your voice goes to our laptop once, over the encrypted link. Gemma 4 writes the invite fro\nai.cloud.ladder | prose |  | Plan drafts, only when our laptop is off. It gets the ask line only.\n# Flare\n\nSnap where you are. If enough friends quietly say yes, it's on.\n\nFlare is an installable web app for small groups of friends (2 to 12). A host sends a photo of where they are, or a Plan for later. Friends say yes in private, with conditions if they like (\"after 2\", \"only with Amor\"). It lights only when enough people can come, it shrinks to a smaller plan instead of failing, it works for friends with low vision or limited mobility and with no signal, and it deletes itself within 5 minutes of ending.\n\nBuilt for the DEV Hacktoberfest Open-Source AI Challenge, Week 1 \"Touch Grass\". Field test: Sunday 2026-10-11, near Fairlane Town Center, Dearborn MI, on four iPhones.\n\n## Run it yourself\n\nYou need Node 24.21.0 or later ([.nvmrc](.nvmrc)). For the photo AI you also need a Mac (or any machine with a GPU) running [Ollama](https://ollama.com). Everything else is optional: `DATABASE_URL=pglite:memory` gives an in-memory Postgres, and without the hub the app falls back to typed words.\n\n**1. The server and the app**\n\n```bash\ngit clone https://github.com/Hotragn/flare && cd flare\nnpm ci\ncp .env.example .env        # set HUB_SECRET to any 32+ random characters\nnpm run check-env           # lists every setting as set, missing or default; never prints values\nnpm run build && npm start  # server and web app on http://localhost:8787\n<!-- Run it yourself (W6), the README's setup steps. Commands are code, not copy. -->\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { t } from \"#lib/copy/site.ts\";\n  import Seo from \"../Seo.svelte\";\n\n  const install = `git clone https://github.com/Hotragn/flare-outside && cd flare-outside\nnpm ci\ncp .env.example .env        # then set HUB_SECRET (32+ random characters)\nnpm run check-env           # reports set or missing, never values\nnpm run build && npm start  # server and web app on http://localhost:8787`;\n  const hub = `ollama pull gemma4:e4b-it-q4_K_M\nnpm run hub`;\n</script>\n\n<Seo path=\"/run/\" />\n\n<section class=\"band\">\n  <h1 class=\"t-title\">{t(\"site.run.title\")}</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">{t(\"site.run.body\")}</p>\n  <p>{t(\"site.run.needs\")}</p>\n  <ol class=\"run-steps\">\n    <!-- svelte-ignore a11y_no_noninteractive_tabindex (keyboard scroll, axe scrollable-region-focusable) -->\n    <li><p>{t(\"site.run.s1\")}</p><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>{install}</code></pre></li>\n    <!-- svelte-ignore a11y_no_noninteractive_tabindex (keyboard scroll, axe scrollable-region-focusable) -->\n    <li><p>{t(\"site.run.s2\")}</p><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>{hub}</code></pre></li>\n    <li><p>{t(\"site.run.s3\")}</p></li>\n  </ol>\n  <p>{t(\"site.run.db\")}</p>\n  <p class=\"t-small\">{t(\"site.run.note\")}</p>\n  <p class=\"t-small\">{t(\"site.run.license\")}</p>\n</section>","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"5ff0cd36-6540-49e7-8e06-51d73130cd5d","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"<project>/flare","root":"<project>/flare","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":25,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":2},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/flare","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/flare","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/flare","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"<project>/flare","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d7c5d81e-276d-434d-a9ee-e0c655cc65a6","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userTy