{"parentUuid":"8dc35903-6e77-491a-a786-1a3cba15cd4c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwKFndhU5mt1Y18PzaD4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0177ji53wXKzmbujtLH3TTVh","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"<project>/flare\" && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='README.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n  global s\n  assert a in s, a\n  s=s.replace(a,b,1)\nrep('''Built for the DEV Hacktoberfest Open-Source AI Challenge, Week 1 \"Touch Grass\". Field test: Sunday 2026-10-11, near Fairlane Town Center, Dearborn MI, on four iPhones.''','''Built for the DEV Hacktoberfest Open-Source AI Challenge, Week 1 \"Touch Grass\". Tested on the real stack end to end, on two iPhones (16 Pro Max, 13) and in a 48-friend simulation; no group meetup with it yet.\n\n**Using Flare needs nothing.** Open https://flare-outside.onrender.com/app/ (or the [demo](https://flare-outside.onrender.com/app/demo/)) and send the link to friends. Gemma runs on our laptop for everyone. The rest of this page is only for hosting your own copy.''')\nrep('''## Run it yourself\n\nYou need Node 24.21.0 or later ([.nvmrc](.nvmrc)). For the photo AI you also need a Mac (or any machine with a GPU) running [Ollama](https://ollama.com). Everything else is optional: `DATABASE_URL=pglite:memory` gives an in-memory Postgres, and without the hub the app falls back to typed words.''','''## Host your own copy\n\nYou need Node 24.21.0 or later ([.nvmrc](.nvmrc)). A model is optional. Pick one of three levels:\n\n1. **No AI keys.** Everything works. The host writes the six words, with place-word chips from the map, and the rules engine does the rest. (`node apps/web/test/e2e/cloud-only.ts --no-keys` checks this: a Flare sent from typed words lights, and Plans get the template steps.)\n2. **A free Google AI Studio key.** Put `GEMINI_API_KEY=` in `.env` (a key from [aistudio.google.com](https://aistudio.google.com)). Gemma 4 runs in the cloud, with no GPU and no laptop. Plan drafts use it automatically, and a photo goes there only when the host taps **Ask cloud Gemma** for that Flare. Google's free tier may review what it receives. (`npm run e2e:cloud-only` checks this: Gemma's words for a photo in about 3.4 s, a Plan draft in 1.3 s.)\n3. **Ollama on your own machine.** The private option: the photo never leaves your machine. Start the hub (step 2 below) on a Mac or any machine with a GPU.\n\n`DATABASE_URL=pglite:memory` gives an in-memory Postgres for a quick run.''')\nrep('''**2. The AI hub** (second terminal, on the machine with Ollama)''','''**2. The AI hub, for level 3 only** (second terminal, on the machine with Ollama)''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='package.json'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('''    \"e2e:cloud-only\": \"node apps/web/test/e2e/cloud-only.ts\",''','''    \"e2e:cloud-only\": \"node apps/web/test/e2e/cloud-only.ts\",\n    \"e2e:no-keys\": \"node apps/web/test/e2e/cloud-only.ts --no-keys\",''',1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nsed -i '' 's#(`node apps/web/test/e2e/cloud-only.ts --no-keys` checks this:#(`npm run e2e:no-keys` checks this:#' README.md; grep -n \"^## Host your own copy\" README.md","description":"README: nothing to install, three levels, honest test line"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1228,"cache_read_input_tokens":815995,"output_tokens":1367,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1228,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1367,"cache_read_input_tokens":815995,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1228,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1228},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"inp