{"parentUuid":"70f2147c-f2fc-4d03-b125-517443cd1f4e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwKruDJuNSwtNA9aVKu9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Every gate passes. Committing and deploying, then the live smoke:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":724,"cache_read_input_tokens":822038,"output_tokens":1197,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":724,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1197,"cache_read_input_tokens":822038,"cache_creation_input_tokens":724,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":724},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"66cdbe56-d3d9-43b7-9387-c3f1aee6ffbd","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfwKrqESXt6pmsCpSJmvj","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"b4028ea4-8364-4f5d-8b9a-c3f4a784cc3e","timestamp":"2026-10-11T23:34:52.421Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"<project>/flare","sessionId":"904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"wondrous-tumbling-meteor"}
{"parentUuid":"b4028ea4-8364-4f5d-8b9a-c3f4a784cc3e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwKruDJuNSwtNA9aVKu9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Uz1Ppa6SowtNev4WL9e1GP","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"<project>/flare\" && git add -A apps/web/src apps/web/test \"apps/web/src/routes/(site)\" design/prototype/src/lib/copy/deck.json docs/content docs/post README.md package.json && git reset -q apps/web/static/scenic apps/web/static/scenery 2>/dev/null; git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nUsing Flare needs nothing; hosting is optional in three levels\n\nFounder feedback: the site read as if you had to set up a model.\n- Site: \"Host your own copy\" (home link, /run title and og), and /run\n  opens with \"Using Flare needs nothing: you open the link, and that's\n  all. This page is only for people who want their own server.\" The\n  clone URL is fixed (Hotragn/flare).\n- Three plain levels on /run and in the README: no AI keys (you write\n  the words with place-word chips); a free Google AI Studio key\n  (Gemma 4 in the cloud, no GPU, no laptop); Ollama on your own\n  machine (the photo never leaves it).\n- Verified on a fresh server with a one-line env file\n  (apps/web/test/e2e/cloud-only.ts): level 2, only GEMINI_API_KEY, no\n  hub: Ask cloud Gemma wrote the invite in 3.4 s, the Flare lit, a\n  Plan draft came from the cloud in 1.3 s (npm run e2e:cloud-only).\n  Level 1, no keys: typed words, it lit, template steps\n  (npm run e2e:no-keys).\n- App, laptop off: \"Tap a place word, or write your own six.\" or,\n  with the cloud on, \"Tap a place word, write your own, or ask cloud\n  Gemma.\" The photo still needs the explicit tap. ai.hubFallback and\n  ai.why.hub_down reworded.\n- README: \"Using Flare needs nothing\" up top; the field-test line now\n  says what was tested and that no group meetup has happened.\n- Post: \"Nothing to install\" near the top; the three levels in Code.\nGates: copy lint 0, svelte-check 0, CI, axe 0 on 88 views,\nLighthouse 100 on 5 pages; e2e demo, sparks, telegram, both levels.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit push -q 2>&1 | tail -1 && npm run deploy:render -- --yes 2>&1 | grep \"deploy started\"; want=$(git rev-parse --short=12 HEAD); for i in $(seq 1 45); do v=$(curl -s https://flare-outside.onrender.com/api/v1/health | python3 -c \"import sys,json;print(json.load(sys.stdin).get('version'))\" 2>/dev/null); [ \"$v\" = \"$want\" ] && break; sleep 20; done; echo live=$v; npm run smoke -- https://flare-outside.onrender.com 2>&1 | tail -1; curl -s https://flare-outside.onrender.com/run/ | grep -o \"Using Flare needs nothing[^<]*\" | head -1","description":"Commit, deploy, live smoke and run page check","timeout":1500000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":724,"cache_read_input_tokens":822038,"output_tokens":1197,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":724,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1197,"cache_read_input_tokens":822038,"cache_creation_input_tokens":724,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":724},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Uz1Ppa6SowtNev4WL9e1GP":{"command":"cd \"<project>/flare\" && git add -A apps/web/src apps/web/test \"apps/web/src/routes/(site)\" design/prototype/src/lib/copy/deck.json docs/content docs/post README.md package.json && git reset -q apps/web/static/scenic apps/web/static/scenery 2>/dev/null; git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nUsing Flare needs nothing; hosting is optional in three levels\n\nFounder feedback: the site read as if you had to set up a model.\n- Site: \"Host your own copy\" (home link, /run title and og), and /run\n  opens with \"Using Flare needs nothing: you open the link, and that's\n  all. This page is only for people who want their own server.\" The\n  clone URL is fixed (Hotragn/flare).\n- Three plain levels on /run and in the README: no AI keys (you write\n  the words with place-word chips); a free Google AI Studio key\n  (Gemma 4 in the cloud, no GPU, no laptop); Ollama on your own\n  machine (the photo never leaves it).\n- Verified on a fresh server with a one-line env file\n  (apps/web/test/e2e/cloud-only.ts): level 2, only GEMINI_API_KEY, no\n  hub: Ask cloud Gemma wrote the invite in 3.4 s, the Flare lit, a\n  Plan draft came from the cloud in 1.3 s (npm run e2e:cloud-only).\n  Level 1, no keys: typed words, it lit, template steps\n  (npm run e2e:no-keys).\n- App, laptop off: \"Tap a place word, or write your own six.\" or,\n  with the cloud on, \"Tap a place word, write your own, or ask cloud\n  Gemma.\" The photo still needs the explicit tap. ai.hubFallback and\n  ai.why.hub_down reworded.\n- README: \"Using Flare needs nothing\" up top; the field-test line now\n  says what was tested and that no group meetup has happened.\n- Post: \"Nothing to install\" near the top; the three levels in Code.\nGates: copy lint 0, svelte-check 0, CI, axe 0 on 88 views,\nLighthouse 100 on 5 pages; e2e demo, sparks, telegram, both levels.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit push -q 2>&1 | tail -1 && npm run deploy:render -- --yes 2>&1 | grep \"deploy started\"; want=$(git rev-parse --short=12 HEAD); for i in $(seq 1 45); do v=$(curl -s https://flare-outside.onrender.com/api/v1/health | python3 -c \"import sys,json;print(json.load(sys.stdin).get('version'))\" 2>/dev/null); [ \"$v\" = \"$want\" ] && break; sleep 20; done; echo live=$v; npm run smoke -- https://flare-outside.onrender.com