{"parentUuid":"c1c5971b-84b7-4226-a492-42927ee12d78","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwLtdk4nDj986UQLahEx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WwR5wEZe8eWME8i7pd8r6b","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"date; cd \"<project>/flare\" && git add apps/web/src apps/web/test \"apps/web/src/routes/(site)\" design/prototype/src/lib/copy/deck.json docs/content && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nClarity: round-5 leftovers, Built with gains Tinker and Entire\n\n- Send: the read-only host line is labelled \"Friends will see\", so\n  your own screen doesn't talk about you in the third person.\n- A spot named from a street reads \"Near West Road\", not a bare\n  street name, so it isn't confused with the suggested park.\n- Demo: a \"Leave the demo\" X on the last screens (You're in, You made\n  it, the Spark, after the outing, the end); the buttons behind the\n  coach card are out of the page (display: none); \"Sent 30 min ago\"\n  follows the demo clock after Skip.\n- Site: no doubled gap above \"What it does\" (the heading wasn't stuck\n  mid-reveal; the old capture had it under the then-translucent\n  header). Built with adds Tinker (the measured failure and the rules\n  it taught, 20/40 to 30/40 blind) and Entire. The nav already reads\n  \"Host your own\".\nGates: unit, e2e (demo with new checks, sparks, telegram, loop, plan,\nfield 27/27, no-keys, flow real), axe 0, Lighthouse 100.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit push -q 2>&1 | tail -1; npm run deploy:render -- --yes 2>&1 | grep \"deploy started\"; git rev-parse --short HEAD","description":"Commit A; push; deploy","timeout":900000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4471,"cache_read_input_tokens":836481,"output_tokens":912,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":196},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4471,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":912,"cache_read_input_tokens":836481,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4471,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4471},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01WwR5wEZe8eWME8i7pd8r6b":{"command":"date; cd \"<project>/flare\" && git add apps/web/src apps/web/test \"apps/web/src/routes/(site)\" design/prototype/src/lib/copy/deck.json docs/content && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nClarity: round-5 leftovers, Built with gains Tinker and Entire\n\n- Send: the read-only host line is labelled \"Friends will see\", so\n  your own screen doesn't talk about you in the third person.\n- A spot named from a street reads \"Near West Road\", not a bare\n  street name, so it isn't confused with the suggested park.\n- Demo: a \"Leave the demo\" X on the last screens (You're in, You made\n  it, the Spark, after the outing, the end); the buttons behind the\n  coach card are out of the page (display: none); \"Sent 30 min ago\"\n  follows the demo clock after Skip.\n- Site: no doubled gap above \"What it does\" (the heading wasn't stuck\n  mid-reveal; the old capture had it under the then-translucent\n  header). Built with adds Tinker (the measured failure and the rules\n  it taught, 20/40 to 30/40 blind) and Entire. The nav already reads\n  \"Host your own\".\nGates: unit, e2e (demo with new checks, sparks, telegram, loop, plan,\nfield 27/27, no-keys, flow real), axe 0, Lighthouse 100.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit push -q 2>&1 | tail -1; npm run deploy:render -- --yes 2>&1 | grep \"deploy started\"; git rev-parse --short HEAD","description":"Commit A; push; deploy","timeout":900000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"c78067b8-473d-4c3e-adbb-99f640d1e2d5","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CfwLtZSM7SWFnfLuwiHKb","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"e806a117-5593-47a1-936f-cd1411ed87aa","timestamp":"2026-10-11T23:48:30.534Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"<project>/flare","sessionId":"904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"wondrous-tumbling-meteor"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-11T23:49:34.469Z","sessionId":"904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa","content":"<cross-session-message from=\"uds:<socket>\" from-session=\"local_beb3cc8c-e162-46cc-bd0a-f870e8717ebd\" from-name=\"Flare Manager(founders CTO)\" from-mode=\"prompting\">\nRevised website brief. It replaces my earlier one, so forward it to the website subagent if it has already started.\n\nEach part of the site has one job:\n- A friend or a curious visitor understands Flare in 5 seconds and starts in a minute.\n- A judge sees within 60 seconds that it's real and how it's built.\n- Motion explains the one idea (it lights only when enough say yes, shrinks instead of dying, then it's gone). It is never decoration.\n\nIn priority order. Cut from the bottom if time runs short, never from the top.\n\n1. The scroll story replaces the static Steps and Shrink sections: fewer sections, not more.\n   - The hero is not taken over. At first paint you see the headline, both buttons and the live sky.\n   - The story plays below the hero: Kindling, Lit, Ember, Gone, with chapter dots, using the Scenery SVG layers.\n2. \"Start in a minute\" and \"Your crew space\", as in the first brief. These are what the founder couldn't find.\n3. A live proof strip called \"Right now\", built from /api/v1/health and /api/v1/audit with no personal data:\n   - Gemma on our laptop: connected, or cloud fallback\n   - Records past their end: 0, checked 12 s ago\n   That makes the privacy promise something you can see live. Link it to the full audit on the privacy page.\n4. \"Try it on your photo\", using the live /hello path:\n   - Pick a photo, it develops like a print, and Gemma's six words come back from our laptop.\n   - The demo uses fixed words, so this is the only place a visitor sees the real model on their own photo.\n   - Same rules as the app: rate limit, nothing stored, never describe faces, typed fallback when the hub is off, and cloud only on an explicit tap.\n5. Real time without asking for location:\n   - Map the browser's time zone to its city coordinates from zone1970.tab, and work out sunset on the page. Example: \"Sunset near Detroit in 38 min. Light a Flare.\"\n   - \"Use my location\" is optional, for an exact time, and sends nothing.\n6. Under the hood, at the bottom of /how, linked from home as \"How it's built\":\n   - An animated diagram of the real path: phone, server, the laptop hub over the relay, Gemma, the cloud fallback (Google, DigitalOcean), and the deletion sweep.\n   - Each partner sits on the line where it actually works, with its one measured number and a link to the code or test that proves it: Mastra, Tinker, Sentry, ElevenLabs, Telegram, Entire.\n   - This is for judges, so the home page stays simple.\n7. Signature taps:\n   - Hear the compass: one ElevenLabs line, while the arrow turns.\n   - The real Telegram card flipping from Waiting to It's lit.\n8. Replace the 10-card grid with a rail called \"At the spot\": compass, walking loop, Sparks, Remember this and Sounds of the spot, each with a short real screen loop. Remember this must show its consent rule visually: every person shows a check before the mic appears. Add the new features as they land.\n9. A small \"Judging? 60-second tour\" link in the hero's fine print, pointing to the demo. Once the founder publishes, add the post link to the footer.\n\nDropped from the first brief:\n- Lenis: native scroll is better for accessibility.\n- The phone-morphs-into-the-app transition: too risky on iOS. Keep View Transitions between site pages only.\n- Feature cards that open into loops: the rail replaces them.\n\nRules and gates are unchanged: no GSAP, no preloader, still with reduced motion, Lighthouse 100, axe 0, JS budget, CSP hashes, LCP under 2.5 s on throttled mobile, and a smooth-scroll trace. Before/after screenshots and a hero GIF for the post.\n</cross-session-message>"}
{"parentUuid":"e806a117-5593-47a1-936f-cd1411ed87aa","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fb97088b-b99e-4d84-9335-c833d3234c27","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WwR5wEZe8eWME8i7pd8r6b","type":"tool_result","content":"Sun Oct 11 19:48:31 EDT 2026\npre-push: secrets, sessions, lint, types, web types and tests ok\nok   deploy started for flare-outside\naee8348","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"2f7de626-faee-4581-be57-bdb9caf2f8c6","timestamp":"2026-10-11T23:50:03.290Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"Sun Oct 11 19:48:31 EDT 2026\npre-push: secrets, sessions, lint, types, web types and tests ok\nok   deploy started for flare-outside\naee8348","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"c78067b8-473d-4c3e-adbb-99f640d1e2d5","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"<project>/flare","root":"<project>/flare","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":38,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":5},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/flare","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/flare","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/flare","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"<project>/flare","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e806a117-5593-47a1-936f-cd1411ed87aa","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"<project>/flare","sessionId":"904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"wondrous-tumbling-meteor"}
{"parentUuid":"2f7de626-faee-4581-be57-bdb9caf2f8c6","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"queued_command","prompt":"<cross-session-message from=\"uds:<socket>\" from-session=\"local_beb3cc8c-e162-46cc-bd0a-f870e8717ebd\" from-name=\"Flare Manager(founders CTO)\" from-mode=\"prompting\">\nRevised website brief. It replaces my earlier one, so forward it to the website subagent if it has already started.\n\nEach part of the site has one job:\n- A friend or a curious visitor understands Flare in 5 seconds and starts in a minute.\n- A judge sees within 60 seconds that it's real and how it's built.\n- Motion explains the one idea (it lights only when enough say yes, shrinks instead of dying, then it's gone). It is never decoration.\n\nIn priority order. Cut from the bottom if time runs short, never from the top.\n\n1. The scroll story replaces the static Steps and Shrink sections: fewer sections, not more.\n   - The hero is not taken over. At first paint you see the headline, both buttons and the live sky.\n   - The story plays below the hero: Kindling, Lit, Ember, Gone, with chapter dots, using the Scenery SVG layers.\n2. \"Start in a minute\" and \"Your crew space\", as in the first brief. These are what the founder couldn't find.\n3. A live proof strip called \"Right now\", built from /api/v1/health and /api/v1/audit with no personal data:\n   - Gemma on our laptop: connected, or cloud fallback\n   - Records past their end: 0, checked 12 s ago\n   That makes the privacy promise something you can see live. Link it to the full audit on the privacy page.\n4. \"Try it on your photo\", using the live /hello path:\n   - Pick a photo, it develops like a print, and Gemma's six words come back from our laptop.\n   - The demo uses fixed words, so this is the only place a visitor sees the real model on their own photo.\n   - Same rules as the app: rate limit, nothing stored, never describe faces, typed fallback when the hub is off, and cloud only on an explicit tap.\n5. Real time without asking for location:\n   - Map the browser's time zone to its city coordinates from zone1970.tab, and work out sunset on the page. Example: \"Sunset near Detroit in 38 min. Light a Flare.\"\n   - \"Use my location\" is optional, for an exact time, and sends nothing.\n6. Under the hood, at the bottom of /how, linked from home as \"How it's built\":\n   - An animated diagram of the real path: phone, server, the laptop hub over the relay, Gemma, the cloud fallback (Google, DigitalOcean), and the deletion sweep.\n   - Each partner sits on the line where it actually works, with its one measured number and a link to the code or test that proves it: Mastra, Tinker, Sentry, ElevenLabs, Telegram, Entire.\n   - This is for judges, so the home page stays simple.\n7. Signature taps:\n   - Hear the compass: one ElevenLabs line, while the arrow turns.\n   - The real Telegram card flipping from Waiting to It's lit.\n8. Replace the 10-card grid with a rail called \"At the spot\": compass, walking loop, Sparks, Remember this and Sounds of the spot, each with a short real screen loop. Remember this must show its consent rule visually: every person shows a check before the mic appears. Add the new features as they land.\n9. A small \"Judging? 60-second tour\" link in the hero's fine print, pointing to the demo. Once the founder publishes, add the post link to the footer.\n\nDropped from the first brief:\n- Lenis: native scroll is better for accessibility.\n- The phone-morphs-into-the-app transition: too risky on iOS. Keep View Transitions between site pages only.\n- Feature cards that open into loops: the rail replaces them.\n\nRules and gates are unchanged: no GSAP, no preloader, still with reduced motion, Lighthouse 100, axe 0, JS budget, CSP hashes, LCP under 2.5 s on throttled mobile, and a smooth-scroll trace. Before/after screenshots and a hero GIF for the post.\n</cross-session-message>","source_uuid":"075c4a46-6ef3-4bb9-a0a7-d062aced9145","delivery_id":"be8be6ef-