eal time without asking for location:\n   - Map the browser's time zone to its city coordinates from zone1970.tab, and work out sunset on the page. Example: \"Sunset near Detroit in 38 min. Light a Flare.\"\n   - \"Use my location\" is optional, for an exact time, and sends nothing.\n6. Under the hood, at the bottom of /how, linked from home as \"How it's built\":\n   - An animated diagram of the real path: phone, server, the laptop hub over the relay, Gemma, the cloud fallback (Google, DigitalOcean), and the deletion sweep.\n   - Each partner sits on the line where it actually works, with its one measured number and a link to the code or test that proves it: Mastra, Tinker, Sentry, ElevenLabs, Telegram, Entire.\n   - This is for judges, so the home page stays simple.\n7. Signature taps:\n   - Hear the compass: one ElevenLabs line, while the arrow turns.\n   - The real Telegram card flipping from Waiting to It's lit.\n8. Replace the 10-card grid with a rail called \"At the spot\": compass, walking loop, Sparks, Remember this and Sounds of the spot, each with a short real screen loop. Remember this must show its consent rule visually: every person shows a check before the mic appears. Add the new features as they land.\n9. A small \"Judging? 60-second tour\" link in the hero's fine print, pointing to the demo. Once the founder publishes, add the post link to the footer.\n\nDropped from the first brief:\n- Lenis: native scroll is better for accessibility.\n- The phone-morphs-into-the-app transition: too risky on iOS. Keep View Transitions between site pages only.\n- Feature cards that open into loops: the rail replaces them.\n\nRules and gates are unchanged: no GSAP, no preloader, still with reduced motion, Lighthouse 100, axe 0, JS budget, CSP hashes, LCP under 2.5 s on throttled mobile, and a smooth-scroll trace. Before/after screenshots and a hero GIF for the post."},"timestamp":"2026-10-11T23:49:34.469Z","isMeta":true,"reminderId":"ef65b9f89f6bc927"},"type":"attac