NEW style files you create there. Do not edit `apps/web/src/routes/(site)/site.css` except to add one `@import` line if you must; put new styles in your own files or component <style> blocks.\n- Copy: every user-facing string goes in the copy deck `design/prototype/src/lib/copy/deck.json` (and the mirror table in `docs/content/02-copy-deck.md`). ADD new keys only, all under a `site.` or `og.` prefix (website lines are split out of the app bundle by `slimDeck` in apps/web/vite.config.ts; site pages import `t` from `#lib/copy/site.ts`). Never change or delete existing keys. Run `node design/prototype/scripts/copy-lint.mjs` (0 problems: buttons ≤3 words, UI messages ≤12 words, no filler words like \"just\").\n- Writing: plain words, a number for every claim, no em dashes. Banned words: seamless, leverage, robust, empower, unlock, elevate, delve, cutting-edge, revolutionize, game-changer, harness, synergy, holistic, paradigm, next-level, supercharge, effortless, ecosystem, tapestry, testament.\n- No GSAP (not open source; we're AGPL), no Lenis, no WebGL, no image sequences, no preloader, no click-to-start gate. Native CSS scroll-driven animations (animation-timeline: view()/scroll()) and View Transitions between site pages, with a fallback where Safari lacks scroll timelines (e.g. IntersectionObserver toggling a class, or a still state). With prefers-reduced-motion everything is still and fully readable.\n- Never send personal data anywhere. No location without a tap.\n\nWhat exists: the home page `apps/web/src/routes/(site)/+page.svelte` (hero with Scenery SVG art + a phone screenshot, Steps.svelte, Features.svelte (10 cards), Shrink.svelte, privacy and access bands, BuiltWith.svelte, run band), `/how/` (Walkthrough.svelte, Shrink), `/privacy/`, `/accessibility/`, `/run/`. Components you can reuse: `#lib/components/Scenery.svelte` (SVG golden-hour scene), `Flame.svelte`, `CountRing.svelte`, `Compass.svelte`, `PhotoPrint.svelte`, sun math in `#lib/map/sun.ts`. Real screen images: `apps/web/static/site/feat/*.webp`, `apps/web/static/site/how/*.webp`, `docs/post/media/*`. Warm-voice clips: `apps/web/static/voice/*.mp3` (e.g. m-150.mp3 + dir-slightLeft.mp3, ahead.mp3). Telegram card renders: `docs/post/media/07-telegram-card-kindling.png`, `07-telegram-card-lit.png` (copy what you need into apps/web/static/site/). APIs: GET /api/v1/health → {ok, version, hub: \"connected\"|\"absent\", db}; GET /api/v1/audit → deletion audit (look at its real shape with curl https://flare-outside.onrender.com/api/v1/audit); POST /api/v1/drafts (image/jpeg body, ≤1.5 MB, returns {invite, alt, tier, ms}; rate-limited per IP; nothing stored) — the /hello page (apps/web/src/routes/hello/) already shows a photo-to-words flow you can learn from. CSP: the server sets a strict CSP with script hashes (apps/server/src/app.ts csp()); keep inline scripts out.\n\nThe brief (from the founder, via the CTO). Each part of the site has one job: a friend or a curious visitor understands Flare in 5 seconds and starts in a minute; a judge sees within 60 seconds that it's real and how it's built; motion explains the one idea (it lights only when enough say yes, shrinks instead of dying, then it's gone) and is never decoration. Do these in priority order and cut from the bottom if time runs short, never from the top:\n\n1. A scroll story replaces the static Steps and Shrink sections on home (fewer sections, not more). The hero is NOT taken over: at first paint the headline, both buttons and the live sky are visible. Below the hero the story plays Kindling → Lit → Ember → Gone with chapter dots, built from Scenery SVG layers: the sky moves to golden hour, a phone lights a Flare at the pond bench, three friend dots walk in, the count goes 1, 2, 3 and it lights; then it shrinks to an Ember at the bench; then the scene empties and leaves fall (Gone). One short line per chapter. Sticky on desktop, shorter on phones.\n2. Two new sections the founder couldn't find:\n   - \"Start in a minute\": three steps with small animated phone screens: open the link; say your name; send a first Flare, or make a crew and share it to Telegram or iMessage.\n   - \"Your crew space\": places, time outside this week, Sparks, the Crew Atlas and Manage crew, with motion (pins drop onto the Atlas, the week bar fills). Use a SAMPLE crew with several places, clearly labelled \"Sample\".\n3. \"Right now\", a live proof strip from /api/v1/health and /api/v1/audit with no personal data: \"Gemma on our laptop: connected\" (or \"cloud fallback\" when hub is absent), and \"Records past their end: 0, checked 12 s ago\" (from the audit). Link to the full audit on /privacy/.\n4. \"Try it on your photo\", using the live drafts path: pick a photo, it develops like a print (PhotoPrint), Gemma's six words come back from our laptop. Same rules as the app: say nothing is stored, never describe faces, typed fallback when the hub is off (tier \"rules\"), cloud only on an explicit tap (POST /api/v1/drafts?cloud=1 only after a tap, and only when /api/v1/config cloud_ai.photo_opt_in is true). Resize to ≤768 px JPEG on the page before sending.\n5. Real time without asking for location: map the browser's time zone (Intl) to its city's coordinates (a small table of IANA zones → lat/lon, e.g. from zone1970.tab, only the zones you need is fine, with a sensible fallback), compute sunset on the page with `#lib/map/sun.ts`: e.g. \"Sunset near Detroit in 38 min. Light a Flare.\" Optional \"Use my location\" for the exact time, computed on the device, sends nothing.\n6. \"Under the hood\" at the bottom of /how/, linked from home as \"How it's built\": an animated diagram of the real path (phone → server → laptop hub over the relay → Gemma; the cloud fallback (Google AI Studio, DigitalOcean paused); the deletion sweep). Each partner sits on the line where it works, with one measured number: Gemma 4 E4B photo 3.0 s median, Voice Flare 3.3 s; Google AI Studio ladder 1.4 s; Mastra agent p95 5.1 s vs 5.5 s, weather 7/7; Tinker 15/40 → LoRA 38/40, rules 20/40 → 30/40 blind; Sentry: allow-list proven by a test; ElevenLabs: 54 compass lines, 698 characters, nothing sent; Telegram: card from the server's renderer; Entire: agent sessions per change. Link each to a repo path (https://github.com/Hotragn/flare/blob/main/...) — the repo may still be private, that's fine.\n7. Signature taps: \"Hear the compass\" (one ElevenLabs line plays while a Compass arrow turns; tap only, never autoplay), and the real Telegram card flipping from Waiting to It's lit.\n8. Replace the 10-card grid with a rail \"At the spot\": compass, walking loop, Sparks, \"Remember this\" and \"Sounds of the spot\" (the last two are being built now: show them with a clear \"Coming in this build\" note only if they aren't live; Remember this must show its consent rule visually: every person shows a check before the mic appears).\n9. A small \"Judging? 60-second tour\" link in the hero fine print, pointing to /app/demo/.\n\nGates you must pass before you report (run them in your worktree after `npm ci` if needed and `npm run build -w apps/web`):\n- `node design/prototype/scripts/copy-lint.mjs` 0 problems; `npx svelte-check` in apps/web 0 errors 0 warnings; `npm run lint` 0; `npm test` passes.\n- `node scripts/lighthouse.ts --min 100` (all five site pages, mobile and desktop, 100 in all four categories); LCP under 2.5 s on throttled mobile (it's in the Lighthouse reports).\n- `node apps/web/test/site/a11y.ts` → 0 findings, 0 targets under 44 px.\n- `npm run budget` (site pages stay modest; /app and /g/[id] must stay under 150 KB, don't touch app code).\n- A smooth-scroll check: a Playwright/Chrome performance trace with 4x CPU throttling (iPhone 13-class) scrolling the home page; report dropped frames / long tasks.\n- Reduced motion: screenshot with reducedMotion \"reduce\" shows every section still and readable.\n- Before/after screenshots (phone 390x844 and desktop 1280x800) and a short hero/scroll-story GIF (≤ 2 MB, via sharp or gifenc, no ffmpeg download) into docs/post/media/site/.\n\nReport back: the branch name and final commit, what you built per item (and what you cut), every gate result with numbers, and the paths of the screenshots and GIF. Be honest about anything that doesn't meet a gate.","outputFile":"<tmp>/904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa/tasks/a1ac31aa2d2a5e6f7.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"dc0c4a0b-7bfd-4ee9-abc1-9b5641cb3160","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"<project>/flare","root":"<project>/flare","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":29,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":5},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/flare","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/flare","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/flare","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"<project>/flare","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3159416d-373b-43ed-aa11-0db4e4a0ba46","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"<project>/flare","sessionId":"904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"wondrous-tumbling-meteor"}
