{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-11T23:52:34.005Z","sessionId":"904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa","content":"<cross-session-message from=\"uds:<socket>\" from-session=\"local_beb3cc8c-e162-46cc-bd0a-f870e8717ebd\" from-name=\"Flare Manager(founders CTO)\" from-mode=\"prompting\">\nNew stream from the founder: motion in the app and the Crew space, so Flare feels better than a WhatsApp poll. Run it as a second subagent in its own worktree (branch app-motion), in parallel with Remember this and site-motion. You merge all three.\n\nThe test for every moment: a WhatsApp poll can't do this. Each one shows a reason Flare wins.\n\n1. The scene is the real sky. The app's illustrated scene follows the phone's clock (golden hour, dusk, night) and the weather we already fetch: rain falls in the scene when it's raining there, and trees sway when it's windy. Outside right now, not a generic picture.\n2. Yeses arrive as sparks. Each anonymous yes flies in from the edge, feeds the flame, the flame grows a step and the count ticks. No names and no faces; a poll shows names, Flare shows warmth.\n3. It's lit. One ignition moment: a warm flash, the flame catches, lit.m4a plays (it's already there), the scene brightens, and the path to the spot draws itself on the ground before \"Find them\".\n4. The shrink. The big flame folds down into a small ember that travels to the bench in the scene. Not dead, smaller. A poll just dies.\n5. Gone. The ember cools, ash drifts up, and \"You were outside together 1 h 12 min\" counts up. A poll stays in the chat forever.\n6. The Crew space is a living place, not a dashboard.\n   - The crew's scene uses the live sky, and each person stands in it as a figure with their initial, not the egg chips.\n   - A fire grows with this week's time outside together.\n   - Sparks float as small lights you tap to read.\n   - On the Atlas, paths draw in, pins drop, and the last meet pulses softly.\n   - Rewrite the empty state \"No time outside yet this week\" as an invitation: an unlit fire pit and \"Your fire's ready. Light a Flare.\"\n   - No streaks and no guilt. Never who said no.\n7. Polish on the Ember screen. The side \"sun\" circles look cropped. The headline sits on top of the bench drawing.\n\nRules:\n- CSS and SVG first, or the Web Animations API. /app is at about 146.8 of 150 KB of JS, so measure, and lazy-load anything new.\n- Each moment is 1.2 s or less, except the ambient scene, which pauses when offscreen or hidden.\n- With reduced motion, everything is still.\n- A 60 fps trace on an iPhone 13-class profile. axe 0. The demo e2e still passes.\n- Remember this adds its controls in the sheet; app-motion owns the visual layers, so they don't collide.\n\nAlso, two cheap and high-value items:\n- Add a short \"Why not just a WhatsApp poll?\" to the post and to the site:\n  - A poll shows who said no. Flare shows a count.\n  - A poll dies when two can't come. Flare shrinks to a smaller plan.\n  - A poll stays forever. Flare deletes itself.\n  - A poll can't help you find each other. Flare has the compass.\n- In fresh-eyes round 6, add the question \"Would you use this over a WhatsApp poll? Why or why not?\" Report the answers verbatim.\n\nBefore/after screenshots and short GIFs of moments 2 to 5 for the post.\n</cross-session-message>"}
