s and components: `apps/web/src/lib/components/*` (Scenery, Flame, Hearth, CountRing, FlameAvatars, Compass visuals, etc.), `apps/web/src/lib/screens/*.svelte` presentation (H5HostKindling, H6HostLit, I1Invite, I6Lit, I9Ember, I10Gone, I12Outside, H0Home), `apps/web/src/lib/motion/*`, and the Crew page `apps/web/src/routes/app/(more)/crew/+page.svelte` plus `apps/web/src/lib/components/CrewAtlas.svelte`.\n- Do NOT edit: anything under apps/server, packages/*, `apps/web/src/lib/screens/flow/*` (host.svelte.ts, link.svelte.ts), `apps/web/src/lib/screens/HostPage.svelte`, `apps/web/src/lib/screens/LinkPage.svelte`, `apps/web/src/routes/(site)/*`, `apps/web/src/routes/app/demo/+page.svelte` (the demo page; you may change the screens it renders, and the demo e2e must still pass). If you need data a screen doesn't have yet, add an optional prop with a sensible default and note it in your report; the lead wires it.\n- Copy: user-facing strings go in `design/prototype/src/lib/copy/deck.json` and the mirror table `docs/content/02-copy-deck.md`. ADD new keys only, with a `motion.` or `crew.` prefix you invent; never change or delete existing keys, except `crew.empty*`/the crew empty-state keys which you may reword. Run `node design/prototype/scripts/copy-lint.mjs` (0 problems; buttons ≤ 3 words, UI messages ≤ 12 words, no filler like \"just\"). Plain words, no em dashes; banned: seamless, leverage, robust, empower, unlock, elevate, delve, cutting-edge, revolutionize, game-changer, harness, synergy, holistic, paradigm, next-level, supercharge, effortless, ecosystem, tapestry, testament.\n\nThe brief (from the founder): make Flare feel better than a WhatsApp poll. The test for every moment: a WhatsApp poll can't do this.\n1. The scene is the real sky: the app's illustrated Scenery follows the phone's clock (golden hour, dusk, night; use `#lib/map/sun.ts` with the phone's rough position if the screen has it, else the time zone/clock) and the weather we already fetch (Home has `weather` {temp_f, rain_likely}; add optional props, e.g. `rain`, `wind`, `hour`): rain falls in the scene when raining, trees sway when windy.\n2. Yeses arrive as sparks: each anonymous yes flies in from the edge, feeds the flame, the flame grows a step, the count ticks (H5HostKindling + I1Invite count ring). No names, no faces.\n3. It's lit: one ignition moment: warm flash, flame catches, play `apps/web/static/sounds/lit.m4a` (it exists; respect `#lib/motion/sound.ts` mute), the scene brightens, the path to the spot draws itself on the ground before \"Find them\" (I6Lit / H6HostLit).\n4. The shrink: the big flame folds down into a small ember that travels to the bench in the scene (I9Ember / the Ember state). Not dead, smaller.\n5. Gone: the ember cools, ash drifts up, \"You were outside together 1 h 12 min\" counts up (I12Outside / I10Gone; the minutes are already a prop).\n6. Crew space as a living place, not a dashboard: the crew's scene uses the live sky; each person stands in it as a figure with their initial (not the egg chips); a fire grows with this week's minutes outside together; Sparks float as small lights you tap to read; on the Atlas paths draw in, pins drop, the last meet pulses softly. Empty state becomes an invitation: an unlit fire pit and \"Your fire's ready. Light a Flare.\" No streaks, no guilt, never who said no.\n7. Ember screen polish: the side \"sun\" circles look cropped; the headline sits on top of the bench drawing. Fix both.\n\nRules: CSS and SVG first, or the Web Animations API. No GSAP, no WebGL. /app is at about 146.8 KB of 150 KB JS (gzipped, `npm run budget` after `npm run build -w apps/web`): measure, and lazy-load anything new (dynamic import, as the codebase already does for Plan screens and SaySpark). Each moment ≤ 1.2 s, except the ambient scene, which pauses when offscreen or the page is hidden. With prefers-reduced-motion (and `[data-reduce-motion]`), everything is still and readable.\n\nGates before you report (in your worktree; `npm ci` if needed):\n- `npx svelte-check` in apps/web: 0 errors, 0 warnings; `npm run lint` 0; `npm test` passes; copy-lint 0 problems.\n- `npm run build -w apps/web && npm run budget`: /app and /g/[id] under 150 KB.\n- `node apps/web/test/site/a11y.ts` → 0 findings; `npm run e2e:demo`, `npm run e2e:sparks`, `npm run e2e:loop` pass.\n- A Chrome performance trace (Playwright, 4x CPU throttle, iPhone-13-class 390x844) through the demo's lit and shrink moments: report fps / dropped frames / long tasks.\n- Reduced-motion screenshots show every screen still.\n- Before/after screenshots (390x844) and short GIFs (≤ 2 MB each, via sharp or gifenc; no ffmpeg download) of moments 2 to 5 into docs/post/media/app-motion/.\n\nReport: branch and final commit, what you built per item and what you cut, every gate with numbers, any new optional props the lead must wire (with where the data comes from), and file paths of screenshots/GIFs. Be honest about gaps.","outputFile":"<tmp>/904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa/tasks/a5311b695b3086d89.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"39ec286d-8f05-4f6b-8a8d-fa0d2e63101e","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"<project>/flare","root":"<project>/flare","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":29,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":5},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/flare","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/flare","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/flare","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"<project>/flare","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"eadde57f-b74b-4f19-8cea-b6fbdb3ecd65","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"<proje