{"parentUuid":"e58f4ba4-95bc-47ef-a084-d7494f416ca7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwND2XsypWdVhVUgCLUm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011FkjZ9Nvwf1eDK6ZUX8pMP","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"<project>/flare\" && cat > <tmp>/904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa/scratchpad/c25.json <<'EOF'\n{\"site.privacy.l.voice\":\"The warm compass voice is recorded once from fixed lines and ships with the app; nothing of yours reaches ElevenLabs for it. Say it for a Spark sends up to 10 seconds of your own voice to ElevenLabs once, only after you tap. We keep no audio. ElevenLabs may keep it under its own terms.\"}\nEOF\npython3 <tmp>/904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa/scratchpad/setcopy.py <tmp>/904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa/scratchpad/c25.json && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\nitems=[\n(\"site.privacy.l.remember\",\"Remember this records a conversation only with everyone's consent. It is off unless the host turns it on for one Flare or Plan. Each person who said yes agrees on their own phone; if anyone doesn't, or someone joins later without agreeing, it stays off for everyone, and nobody sees who. Anyone can stop a recording for everyone, and every phone shows when it's on. Up to 60 seconds goes once to ElevenLabs, which turns it into words with speaker numbers, not names. We keep no audio; ElevenLabs may keep it under its own terms. The words are sealed on your phones with the Flare key, Gemma on our laptop writes one line (never the cloud), and all of it is deleted with the Flare.\",\"prose\",\"site W4 (ADR-0031)\"),\n(\"ai.remember\",\"Remember this: with everyone's OK, ElevenLabs writes down up to 60 s and our laptop sums it up in one line.\",\"prose\",\"/ai/ (ADR-0031)\"),\n]\np='design/prototype/src/lib/copy/deck.json'\ns=open(p).read()\nadd=''.join(f'    {json.dumps(k)}: {{\\n      \"text\": {json.dumps(v)},\\n      \"kind\": \"{kind}\",\\n      \"where\": \"{w}\"\