{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-12T00:10:33.219Z","sessionId":"904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa","content":"<cross-session-message from=\"uds:<socket>\" from-session=\"local_beb3cc8c-e162-46cc-bd0a-f870e8717ebd\" from-name=\"Flare Manager(founders CTO)\" from-mode=\"prompting\">\nRe-plan for tonight from the founder. It replaces every earlier order.\n\nHow judges score: writing quality counts most, then relevance, creativity and technical execution. Partner tools are optional. Winners had:\n- a real person's words near the top\n- measured numbers\n- an honest \"what went wrong\"\n- one line per partner\n- a live demo\nFeature count and length didn't matter, and a bug on live hurts more than a missing feature.\n\nRULES\n- Code freeze at 1:00 AM ET. Anything not finished and tested by then is switched off on live (flag off) and left out of the post. Nothing half-working ships.\n- Every feature that ships needs a measured number or a test, or it isn't mentioned.\n- iPhone 13 smooth, Lighthouse 100, axe 0, JS budget. If motion breaks a gate, cut the motion.\n- After each step lands live, send me one status line, and say plainly what got cut.\n\nPRIORITY (cut from the bottom, never the top)\n\n1. Website clarity (site-motion subagent; do this before any scroll story):\n   - Start in a minute\n   - Your crew space, with a sample crew that's labeled\n   - the \"Right now\" live audit strip\n   - Try it on your photo\n   Judges should get it in seconds.\n\n2. Why it matters, right after the hero on the home page (site-motion subagent).\n   - Real-world data on time indoors, loneliness and time with friends, with charts that make the emotional point plain: many people stay in their room and suffer.\n   - Data integrity is absolute:\n     - Every number is checked against its primary source, with the exact figure, year and a link under the chart.\n     - Any number that can't be verified is dropped.\n     - Nothing from memory.\n   - Candidates to verify:\n     - EPA NHAPS (Klepeis et al. 2001): share of time spent indoors\n     - the 2023 US Surgeon General advisory on loneliness: share of adults reporting loneliness, and in-person time with friends 2003 vs 2020 from the American Time Use Survey\n     - BLS ATUS tables for socializing time by year: a real chart from primary data\n     - White et al. 2019, Scientific Reports: 120 minutes a week in nature\n     - the Meta-Gallup Global State of Social Connections, 2023\n   - Charts: inline SVG with no chart library, direct labels, one accent colour, and a text or table alternative for screen readers. They draw in only when motion is allowed.\n   - Tone: plain and human, not doom. End on the action: 15 minutes outside with people you like.\n\n3. App motion (app-motion subagent): yes sparks feed the flame, the lit moment, the shrink to an Ember, Gone. iPhone 13 smooth or cut. The Crew scene comes after these four.\n\n4. Small automations that make a poll pointless (you, on main):\n   a. One-tap \"Again\" on Home and Crew: the last crew, group size and nearest favourite spot are pre-chosen, and the photo is optional. You can use place-word chips or typed words.\n   b. If the crew is linked to Telegram, Send posts the card straight to the group, with no share sheet. If that needs a lasting crew-to-chat link, make it opt-in and delete it with Forget, and update the deletion audit.\n   c. Automatic \"I'm here\" when the compass is within about 30 m and GPS accuracy is good, on two readings in a row, with a 10 s Undo toast. Only while the page is open. Test it on the recorded iPhone streams.\n\n5. Sounds of the spot. Ship only the labels that pass the lab's eval. Ship only if every speech clip is dropped (speech-drop recall 100% on at least 10 clips); report the number.\n\n6. Remember this. Park it now behind a flag that's off, on its branch, and come back after 5. It ships only if the consent tests pass by 1 AM:\n   - any no or a late joiner means off\n   - nobody sees who said no\n   - the recording sign shows live on every phone\n   - the audio is deleted\n   If it isn't solid, it stays off live, and the post gets one honest next-step line.\n\n7. Fresh-eyes round 6, including \"Why not just a WhatsApp poll?\", with answers quoted word for word.\n\nNot tonight, but in the post as next steps: \"my usual\" conditions, repeating Plans, in-app golden-hour nudges.\n\nONE-LINE FIX in apps/server/src/preview/index.ts:2. Telegram fetches the link on its own servers, but iMessage and WhatsApp build the preview on the sender's phone. Make the comment say that; either way, the preview sits in the chat where our deletion can't reach. The rule itself stays.\n\nPOST: I'll send the post plan separately in a few minutes. Don't restructure the draft before it arrives.\n</cross-session-message>"}
{"parentUuid":"fbdc2cc2-5fac-46b2-91d7-ad4abf4afa1f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwNaFc2GaP6nz1nUAsGt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015sgzyrHf5AJVR6Mk4bQDCL","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"<project>/flare\" && git add docs/frontend/evidence/e2e-remember-*.png packages 2>/dev/null; git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nRemember this: a conversation note made only with everyone's consent\n\nADR-0031 (founder decision; replaces \"never record a conversation\").\n- Per Flare or Plan, off by default; the host turns it on. Each person\n  who said yes agrees on their own phone; any no, or a late joiner\n  without consent, keeps it off for everyone, never saying who\n  (rememberState(), flags only).\n- When lit and everyone agreed, anyone records up to 60 s after \"Only\n  your group. Stop if others are close.\"; every phone shows the sign\n  live (SSE remember) and anyone can stop it for everyone; a no stops\n  it at once.\n- ElevenLabs Scribe v2 with speaker labels (Speaker 1, 2), audio\n  zero-filled, none kept; the phone seals the lines with the Flare key\n  (aad r:); Gemma on the hub writes one line (summary prompt v1,\n  enforceSummary; hub only, never the cloud). Two tables cascade with\n  the gathering; deletion audit DS12.\n- Privacy page: the exact rule, and that ElevenLabs may keep audio.\n  AI page line. openapi (7 routes), asyncapi summaryJob.\nMeasured: Scribe 720 ms on a 10 s two-voice clip; stop to the sealed\nnote on the other phone 5.3 s. Tests: consent properties (fast-check),\ncontract scenario, real-stack 2-phone e2e (npm run e2e:remember) with\na real Scribe call and the real hub. Unit 696/67/26; e2e demo, sparks,\nplan, telegram, field 27/27; axe 0; JS 147.5 / 146.5 KB.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit push -q 2>&1 | tail -1 && npm run deploy:render -- --yes 2>&1 | grep \"deploy started\"; date","description":"Commit Remember t