 ElevenLabs may keep audio.\n  AI page line. openapi (7 routes), asyncapi summaryJob.\nMeasured: Scribe 720 ms on a 10 s two-voice clip; stop to the sealed\nnote on the other phone 5.3 s. Tests: consent properties (fast-check),\ncontract scenario, real-stack 2-phone e2e (npm run e2e:remember) with\na real Scribe call and the real hub. Unit 696/67/26; e2e demo, sparks,\nplan, telegram, field 27/27; axe 0; JS 147.5 / 146.5 KB.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit push -q 2>&1 | tail -1 && npm run deploy:render -- --yes 2>&1 | grep \"deploy started\"; date","description":"Commit Remember this; push; deploy","timeout":900000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"ffd73343-989f-4350-9d50-ced16692d4eb","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfwNaEYXHwbjGJ981zy75","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"fe65f23e-c575-4c02-8662-962ba04d59c7","timestamp":"2026-10-12T00:10:51.325Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"<project>/flare","sessionId":"904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"wondrous-tumbling-meteor"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-12T00:11:46.541Z","sessionId":"904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa","content":"<cross-session-message from=\"uds:<socket>\" from-session=\"local_beb3cc8c-e162-46cc-bd0a-f870e8717ebd\" from-name=\"Flare Manager(founders CTO)\" from-mode=\"prompting\">\nPost plan. The full file is at <project>/orchestration/POST-PLAN.md; read it there, it's outside the repo on purpose. In short:\n\n- Budget: at most 1,900 words of prose (the draft is 2,860) and at most 8 images. Cut, don't add.\n- Angle: almost every entry is one person on one walk. Flare gets a group out. Lead with that.\n- The opening:\n  - Keep the 4 PM scene.\n  - Then the founder's own why, which they write tonight. Delete the \"Suggested:\" quote now: it's invented and can't ship.\n  - Then the friend's real reply and screenshot from tonight's live test.\n  - Then a hero GIF of the four app moments.\n- New: \"Why it matters\", one sourced chart from the site in 120 words. \"Method\", 150 words: roles and handoffs, the ICD frozen first, ADRs and the traced SRS, gated pushes, fresh-eyes rounds as sprint reviews. Plus two images: an architecture diagram and a 4-frame storyboard (Kindling, Lit, Ember, Gone) as the use case.\n- Merge the six partner ### sections into one \"The rest of the stack\", at most 60 words each, keeping the numbers.\n- Tonight's features get one \"New tonight\" section of 150 words, with only what shipped with a test. Remember this opens with the consent rule.\n- Keep \"What I got wrong\", with concrete items. Merge \"What I didn't do\" into \"Honest limits\": no background location or mic, no server pushes, no group meetup yet, and small groups can guess.\n- Prize lines: one each, only with live proof. No DigitalOcean claim unless billing is fixed.\n- First person in the founder's voice, and never words for a real person.\n\nTiming: restructure the post after the freeze at 1:00 AM, when we know what shipped. Until then, only delete the invented quote. A fresh-eyes review session will read the post, the site, the app and the code after the freeze.\n</cross-session-message>"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-12T00:11:55.082Z","sessionId":"904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa","content":"<cross-session-message from=\"uds:<socket>\" from-session=\"local_beb3cc8c-e162-46cc-bd0a-f870e8717ebd\" from-name=\"Flare Manager(founders CTO)\" from-mode=\"prompting\">\nA change to the post timing: writing counts most, and 1:00 to 2:59 is too tight. Start a third subagent now that owns only docs/post. It restructures the draft to the plan using what's already true, and leaves three marked holes:\n- [NEW TONIGHT], filled after the freeze\n- [ROUND 6]\n- the founder's why and the friend quote\nIt also makes the two images (architecture and storyboard). It touches no code. After the freeze, you fill the holes and cut anything that didn't ship.\n</cross-session-message>"}
