{"parentUuid":"9ebfcf52-c6a3-4d03-94bd-2d0004da56d1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwP62aXmyWotHSSAJRJ7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Rj6jDbfN7LUbeh7jSNWVg3","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Restructure the DEV post","subagent_type":"general-purpose","isolation":"worktree","run_in_background":true,"prompt":"You are the writer for Flare's DEV challenge post. Your worktree is the repo at main e6824af. Work on a new branch `post-rework`; commit there; do NOT push to main, do NOT deploy. You own ONLY files under `docs/post/` (the draft is `docs/post/draft.md`; images go in `docs/post/media/`). Touch no code.\n\nRead the plan first: <project>/orchestration/POST-PLAN.md (outside the repo on purpose; read it by that absolute path). Also read `docs/post/draft.md`, `docs/post/REVIEW.md`, `docs/post/media/README.md`, `docs/research/00-challenge-and-field.md` (what judges reward), `docs/research/fresh-eyes-2026-10-11.md`, and the ADRs in `docs/architecture/adr/` (0021 Sentry, 0025 Mastra, 0026 Google cloud tier, 0027 ElevenLabs, 0028 Voice Flares, 0029 Crew Atlas, 0030 automations, 0031 Remember this) for facts and numbers. Every number you keep must already be in the draft or an ADR/handoff/test in the repo; invent nothing.\n\nThe plan, in short (POST-PLAN.md is authoritative where it says more):\n- Budget: at most 1,900 words of prose (tables don't count toward prose but keep them lean) and at most 8 images. Cut, don't add.\n- Angle: almost every entry is one person on one walk; Flare gets a GROUP out. Lead with that.\n- Opening: keep the 4 PM group-chat scene. Then a hole for the founder's own why: `[FOUNDER WHY: the founder writes this tonight, in their own words]`. Then a hole for a friend's real reply from tonight's live test: `[FRIEND QUOTE: the friend's real words and screenshot, with their OK]`. Then a hero GIF of the four app moments: `[HERO GIF: Kindling, Lit, Ember, Gone]`. Never write words for a real person.\n- New \"Why it matters\": one sourced chart from the site in 120 words: leave `[WHY IT MATTERS: one chart and its sources, from the site's verified section]` with a short framing sentence you may write without numbers.\n- New \"Method\", 150 words: roles and handoffs, the ICD (interface contracts) frozen first, ADRs and the traced SRS (requirements traceability), gated pushes (secret scan, lint, types, tests on every push), fresh-eyes rounds as sprint reviews. Plus two images you make: an architecture diagram (phone → server on Render → WebSocket relay → laptop hub with Gemma 4 on Ollama; cloud fallback Google AI Studio (DigitalOcean wired, paused); deletion sweep; ElevenLabs Scribe; Sentry) and a 4-frame storyboard (Kindling, Lit, Ember, Gone) as the use case. Make them as SVG (hand-written, plain shapes, system fonts) and render PNGs with sharp (`node` + `sharp` is installed in the repo) into docs/post/media/ (e.g. 20-architecture.png, 21-storyboard.png); you may compose the storyboard from existing screenshots in docs/post/media/ and docs/design/redesign/after/ (demo-2-kindling.jpg, demo-3-ember-lit.jpg, etc.).\n- Merge the six partner ### sections into one \"The rest of the stack\", at most 60 words each, keeping the numbers.\n- Tonight's features: one section with only a hole `[NEW TONIGHT: ≤150 words, only what shipped with a test; Remember this, if shipped, opens with its consent rule]`.\n- Keep \"What I got wrong\" with concrete items. Merge \"What I didn't do\" into \"Honest limits\": no background location or mic, no server pushes, no group meetup yet, and small groups can guess who said yes from the count.\n- Prize lines: one each, only with live proof. No DigitalOcean claim (billing is still blocked) — remove its prize line.\n- A hole `[ROUND 6: the final fresh-eyes score and the WhatsApp-poll answers, quoted word for word]` in \"How I tested it\".\n- First person, in the founder's voice. Plain words, a number for every claim, no em dashes. Banned words: seamless, leverage, robust, empower, unlock, elevate, delve, cutting-edge, revolutionize, game-changer, harness, synergy, holistic, paradigm, next-level, supercharge, effortless, ecosystem, tapestry, testament.\n- Keep the official opening line exactly: `*This is a submission for the [Hacktoberfest Open-Source AI Challenge Week 1: Touch Grass](https://dev.to/challenges/hacktoberfest-week1-2026-10-05).*` and the front matter tags `devchallenge, hf26challenge, gemma, opensource`. Keep \"Nothing to install\" near the top. Keep the template section order from the research doc (What I Built, Demo, Code, How I Built It, Why Does Open Innovation Matter?, My Agent Session, Prize Categories).\n\nWhen done: report the branch and commit, the prose word count (count words outside tables, code and HTML comments), the image list (≤ 8), every hole you left, and anything from the old draft you cut that the lead might want back."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":765,"cache_read_input_tokens":943978,"output_tokens":2857,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":765,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2857,"cache_read_input_tokens":943978,"cache_creation_input_tokens":765,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":765},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Rj6jDbfN7LUbeh7jSNWVg3":{"description":"Restructure the DEV post","subagent_type":"general-purpose","isolation":"worktree","run_in_background":true,"prompt":"You are the writer for Flare's DEV 