{"parentUuid":"d39dd9e5-cc77-4475-80fa-697c0695e14e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwP62aXmyWotHSSAJRJ7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PVVbJZVD2HCcm1bjVfyPZR","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"a1ac31aa2d2a5e6f7","summary":"Re-plan: new site priorities and data rules","message":"Re-plan from the founder, which replaces the earlier order. Cut from the bottom, never the top.\n\n1. **Clarity first,** before any scroll story: \"Start in a minute\", \"Your crew space\" with a labelled sample crew, the \"Right now\" live audit strip, and \"Try it on your photo\". Judges should get it in seconds.\n\n2. **\"Why it matters\"**, right after the hero on home. Real data on time indoors, loneliness and time with friends, with charts that make the emotional point plain: many people stay in their room and suffer. Data integrity is absolute:\n   - Check every number against its primary source, and put the exact figure, the year and a link under the chart.\n   - Drop any number you can't verify. Nothing from memory: fetch and read the primary source.\n   - Candidates to verify:\n     - EPA NHAPS (Klepeis et al. 2001): share of time spent indoors\n     - the 2023 US Surgeon General advisory on loneliness: share of adults reporting loneliness, and in-person time with friends in 2003 vs 2020 from the American Time Use Survey\n     - BLS ATUS tables for socializing time by year: a real chart from primary data\n     - White et al. 2019, Scientific Reports: 120 minutes a week in nature\n     - the Meta-Gallup Global State of Social Connections, 2023\n   - Charts: inline SVG, no chart library, direct labels, one accent colour, and a text or table alternative for screen readers. They draw in only when motion is allowed.\n   - Tone: plain and human, not doom. End on the action: 15 minutes outside with people you like.\n   - Record every source and the exact figure in a file such as docs/research/why-it-matters-sources.md.\n\n3. **Only then** the scroll story, the \"Under the hood\" diagram, the signature taps and the \"At the spot\" rail, in that order. Drop the rail's \"Remember this\" and \"Sounds of the spot\" cards unless I tell you they shipped.\n\n**Gates and rules (unchanged):** Lighthouse 100, axe 0, iPhone 13 smooth. If motion breaks a gate, cut the motion.\n\n**Code freeze is 1:00 AM ET.** Please send me a progress note by about 11:30 PM with what's committed on site-motion and what passes, so I can merge in time.","type":"message","recipient":"a1ac31aa2d2a5e6f7","recipient_kind":"agent","content":"Re-plan from the founder, which replaces the earl…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":765,"cache_read_input_tokens":943978,"output_tokens":2857,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":765,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2857,"cache_read_input_tokens":943978,"cache_creation_input_tokens":765,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":765},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01PVVbJZVD2HCcm1bjVfyPZR":{"to":"a1ac31aa2d2a5e6f7","summary":"Re-plan: new site priorities and data rules","message":"Re-plan from the founder, which replaces the earlier order. Cut from the bottom, never the top.\n\n1. **Clarity first,** before any scroll story: \"Start in a minute\", \"Your crew space\" with a labelled sample crew, the \"Right now\" live audit strip, and \"Try it on your photo\". Judges should get it in seconds.\n\n2. **\"Why it matters\"**, right after the hero on home. Real data on time indoors, loneliness and time with friends, with charts that make the emotional point plain: many people stay in their room and suffer. Data integrity is absolute:\n   - Check every number against its primary source, and put the exact figure, the year and a link under the chart.\n   - Drop any number you can't verify. Nothing from memory: fetch and read the primary source.\n   - Candidates to verify:\n     - EPA NHAPS (Klepeis et al. 2001): share of time spent indoors\n     - the 2023 US Surgeon General advisory on loneliness: share of adults reporting loneliness, and in-person time with friends in 2003 vs 2020 from the American Time Use Survey\n     - BLS ATUS tables for socializing time by year: a real chart from primary data\n     - White et al. 2019, Scientific Reports: 120 minutes a week in nature\n     - the Meta-Gallup Global State of Social Connections, 2023\n   - Charts: inline SVG, no chart library, direct labels, one accent colour, and a text or table alternative for screen readers. They draw in only when motion is allowed.\n   - Tone: plain and human, not doom. End on the action: 15 minutes outside with people you like.\n   - Record every source and the exact figure in a file such as docs/research/why-it-matters-sources.md.\n\n3. **Only then** the scroll story, the \"Under the hood\" diagram, the signature taps and the \"At the spot\" rail, in that order. Drop the rail's \"Remember this\" and \"Sounds of the spot\" cards unless I tell you they shipped.\n\n**Gates and rules (unchanged):** Lighthouse 100, axe 0, iPhone 13 smooth. If motion breaks a gate, cut the motion.\n\n**Code freeze is 1:00 AM ET.** Please send me a progress note by about 11:30 PM with what's committed on site-motion and what passes, so I can merge in time."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"94c849cd-c146-4bef-8f80-4a0ee0b81b3b","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfwP61LdGRDwnAYdPtG5S","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"3c282dc4-941d-47a3-9ff0