{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-12T00:21:42.164Z","sessionId":"904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa","content":"<cross-session-message from=\"uds:<socket>\" from-session=\"local_beb3cc8c-e162-46cc-bd0a-f870e8717ebd\" from-name=\"Flare Manager(founders CTO)\" from-mode=\"prompting\">\nA live bug from the founder's real Flare tonight, sent by WhatsApp and opened in Brave on an iPhone. This goes ahead of the automations, because a live bug hurts more than a missing feature. Tell app-motion if it's touching I1Invite or H2/H3.\n\nWhat the founder saw:\n- The invite: a dim indoor photo, where only the top third of the screen shows the photo, the six-word headline sits right on it, and the sheet covers the rest. You can't see the place, which is the whole point of the photo. The same thing happens on the send screens (Develop and Send).\n- The copy: \"Fuego is at Near [street].\" The round-5 \"Near {street}\" spot name flows into every \"{host} is at {spot}\" template: invite.where, invite.whereWalk, lit.notice, push.lit and sms.lit.\n\nWhy we missed it: every screenshot, e2e test and fresh-eyes round used our bright daylight demo photos on a full Safari viewport. No test checked that the photo stays visible; contrast and axe only check the text. The new fixes must close that gap.\n\nFixes:\n1. The photo is the content. Text and the sheet never cover the main part of the image.\n   - Show the photo at its natural shape in the top area.\n   - Put the six words below it, or on a short gradient band at the photo's bottom edge only.\n   - The sheet starts collapsed below the photo.\n   - Tap the photo to see it full screen.\n   - Same rule on Develop and Send.\n2. Dark photos. On the phone, measure the average brightness of the decoded photo on a small canvas. If it's dark, brighten it for display only with a CSS filter. Never change the sealed photo.\n3. Make the \"Your yes is private\" chip one line, and stay dismissed once closed.\n4. Copy: when the spot is a \"Near X\" name, every template reads \"{host} is near [street].\" Add a test that renders each of the 5 templates with a street spot, a park spot and a bench spot, and checks the grammar.\n5. New gates, so this can't come back:\n   - Visual tests with a real dark indoor photo and a tall portrait photo.\n   - Viewports: 390×664 (Brave or a WhatsApp in-app browser with a bottom bar) and 375×667 (iPhone SE size), as well as the current ones.\n   - An overlap check that fails if text or the sheet covers more than 25% of the photo's area at first paint.\n   - In round 6, testers use their own dark photo.\n\nSend me the before/after screenshots at 390×664 when it's live.\n</cross-session-message>"}
