{"parentUuid":"7d960140-0f9f-461a-bfd6-910f76637c2b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fb97088b-b99e-4d84-9335-c833d3234c27","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. **Primary request and intent**\n\n   **Project**\n   - Flare is a DEV Hacktoberfest Week 1 \"Touch Grass\" challenge entry.\n   - Deadline: Mon Oct 12, 06:59 UTC (2:59 AM ET). Code freeze: 1:00 AM ET.\n   - Work runs \"like a real software company\": docs, proof, handoffs, frequent commits.\n   - Messages from the manager session \"Flare Manager(founders CTO)\" are treated as the founder's instructions. The socket path changes; use ListAgents and address by name \"Flare Manager(founders CTO)\".\n   - Report to the manager after each step lands live.\n\n   **Security and constraints, verbatim, still in force:**\n   - \"Secrets are already in .env, at <project>/flare/.env (if you're running in a worktree copy, read them from that path). … Never print, log or commit them. .gitignore already protects .env.\"\n   - \"Anything public waits for my yes: deploying under my accounts, making the repo public, publishing, posting, uploading, or messaging people.\"\n   - \"Already approved, no need to ask: npm installs; installing Ollama with Homebrew and pulling gemma4:e4b; downloading the Gemma 4 E2B ONNX model (~3.2 GB) for browser tests; creating a private GitHub repo named flare on my account and pushing to it; keeping the Mac awake (caffeinate) during long work.\"\n   - \"A separate lab session is running technical spikes in lab/ (git-ignored). Don't edit or commit lab/.\"\n   - The founder gave YES (via the manager) for the Render free-tier deploy and redeploys of the same service, and for the Telegram setWebhook.\n   - Do not claim the DigitalOcean signature moment; mark it [PENDING DO BILLING]. No DigitalOcean prize claim unless billing is fixed.\n   - Leave the untracked folders `apps/web/static/scenic/` and the `-640`/`-1280` files in `apps/web/static/scenery/` for the founder. Don't work around the rm block, and never stage them.\n   - Don't add a Deploy to Render button unless it can be tested without creating anything under the founder's accounts.\n   - Don't start anything that listens to conversations. Remember this, which is consented and per-Flare, is the founder-approved exception.\n   - Never write words for a real person. The invented suggested quote was deleted.\n\n   **Writing rules**\n   - Plain words, a number for every claim, no em dashes.\n   - Banned words: seamless, leverage, robust, empower, unlock, elevate, delve, cutting-edge, revolutionize, game-changer, harness, synergy, holistic, paradigm, next-level, supercharge, effortless, ecosystem, tapestry, testament.\n   - Buttons ≤3 words, UI messages ≤12 words, no filler (\"just\"). copy-lint must pass.\n   - Fixed requirement strings can't change: SRS-AI-4 \"Made on our laptop\"; SRS-COND-8 cond.didntCatch; SRS-CMP-5 compass.disclaimer.\n\n   **Gates:** Lighthouse 100 on the site pages, axe 0, JS budget (/app and /g/ under 150 KB), CSP, iPhone 13 smooth (cut motion if it breaks a gate), live smoke after deploy.\n\n   **Current re-plan (latest; replaces earlier orders).** Priority, cut from the bottom:\n   1. Website clarity (site-motion subagent): Start in a minute, Your crew space with a labelled sample crew, the \"Right now\" audit strip, Try it on your photo.\n   2. \"Why it matters\" right after the hero. Real data, verified against primary sources (exact figure, year and link under each chart), drop anything unverifiable, nothing from memory. Candidates: EPA NHAPS (Klepeis 2001), the 2023 Surgeon General loneliness advisory with ATUS 2003 vs 2020, BLS ATUS socializing by year, White et al. 2019 (120 min/week in nature), Meta-Gallup 2023. Inline SVG charts with a text alternative, no library. End on \"15 minutes outside with people you like.\"\n   3. App motion (app-motion subagent): yes sparks, lit, shrink, Gone; iPhone 13 smooth or cut. The Crew scene comes after these.\n   4. Small automations on main:\n      - a. One-tap \"Again\" on Home and Crew: last crew, group size and nearest favourite spot pre-chosen; photo optional; place-word chips or typed words.\n      - b. Telegram-linked crew: Send posts the card directly, no share sheet.\n      - c. Automatic \"I'm here\" within about 30 m with good GPS, on two readings in a row, with a 10 s Undo, only while the page is open, tested on the recorded iPhone streams.\n   5. Sounds of the spot:\n      - At the spot, a tap records 10 s; hub Gemma names a fixed label list (birds, geese, water, wind, leaves, rain, insects, dog, traffic, people).\n      - enforce() rejects anything else. If \"people\" is detected, show \"Heard voices, so nothing was kept\" and drop the result.\n      - Hub only, audio zero-filled; the result is one line on the Ember.\n      - Ship only labels that pass the lab's eval, and only if speech-drop recall is 100% on ≥10 clips; report the number.\n      - The lab will send the numbers.\n   6. Remember this: parked behind a flag (off). It ships only if the consent tests pass by 1 AM; otherwise it stays off and the post gets one honest next-step line.\n   7. Fresh-eyes round 6. Add \"Would you use this over a WhatsApp poll? Why or why not?\" and report the answers verbatim. Do NOT add a WhatsApp comparison section to the site or post.\n   - Not tonight, but in the post as next steps: \"my usual\" conditions, repeating Plans, in-app golden-hour nudges.\n\n   **Post plan:** see <project>/orchestration/POST-PLAN.md.\n   - At most 1,900 words of prose and at most 8 images.\n   - Lead with \"Flare gets a group out\".\n   - Holes: the founder's why, the friend quote, the hero GIF, why-it-matters, [NEW TONIGHT], [ROUND 6].\n   - Method section; architecture diagram and storyboard images.\n   - \"The rest of the stack\": at most 60 words per partner.\n   - \"Honest limits\".\n   - The post subagent restructures now. After the freeze I fill the holes and cut anything that didn't ship.\n\n2. **Key technical concepts**\n\n   **Stack**\n   - npm-workspaces monorepo: packages/shared, packages/engine, apps/server (Hono, ws, PGlite/pg), apps/hub (Ollama gemma4:e4b-it-q4_K_M), apps/web (SvelteKit / Svelte 5, adapter-static).\n   - Node 24 runs `.ts` directly.\n\n   **Deploy and runtime**\n   - Render free tier; deploy with `npm run deploy:render -- --yes`. Live at https://flare-outside.onrender.com.\n   - The hub runs on this Mac: `FLARE_SERVER_URL=wss://flare-outside.onrender.com nohup npm run hub > scratchpad/hub-live.log &`. Restart it after hub changes with `pkill -f apps/hub/src/main.ts`.\n\n   **Cloud tier and voice**\n   - Cloud tier (ADR-0026): DigitalOcean first (402 blocked), then Google AI Studio gemma-4-26b-a4b-it with `thinkingLevel: \"minimal\"`, one retry on 5xx, a 1 h skip on 401/402/403.\n   - Gemma 4 hears audio via Ollama's `images` field (WAV).\n   - ElevenLabs: 54 pre-recorded compass clips (static/voice), and Scribe v2 for Voice Spark. Remember this uses diarize=true.\n   - Copy deck: design/prototype/src/lib/copy/deck.json, mirrored in docs/content/02-copy-deck.md. slimDeck strips site.*/og.* from the app bundle; site pages import from `#lib/copy/site.ts`.\n\n   **Tests and tools**\n   - Copy edits: scratchpad/setcopy.py (by key).\n   - Contract coverage: contract.test.ts needs a `describe(\"<operationId>\"` for every openapi operation. The harness uses a TestClock; the per-IP limit of 60 is shared across that test file.\n   - fast-check is available (hoisted).\n   - Pre-push gate: secrets, sessions, lint, types, web types, tests.\n\n   **Subagents running in worktrees**\n   - site-motion (agent a1ac31aa2d2a5e6f7)\n   - app-motion (a5311b695b3086d89)\n   - post-rework (a0e24f31091a79c08)\n   - I merge all three. Progress notes are due about 11:30 PM.\n\n3. **Files and code sections (this stretch)**\n\n   **Setup copy and hub-down copy (committed b6fd014)**\n   - deck: site.home.readRun \"Host your own copy.\", site.run.title, site.run.body \"Using Flare needs nothing: you open the link, and that's all. This page is only for people who want their own server.\", og.run.*, site.run.levels.title, level1–3.\n   - develop.hubDown \"Tap a place word, or write your own six.\"; new develop.hubDownCloud \"Tap a place word, write your own, or ask cloud Gemma.\"\n   - ai.hubFallback; ai.why.hub_down \"Our laptop was off at that moment.\"\n   - H2Develop uses hubDownCloud when `cloud`.\n   - run/+page.svelte: three levels, clone URL fixed to Hotragn/flare.\n   - README: \"Using Flare needs nothing\", \"Host your own copy\" with three levels; the fake field-test line was replaced with an honest one.\n   - New e2e `apps/web/test/e2e/cloud-only.ts` (npm run e2e:cloud-only, and with `--no-keys` npm run e2e:no-keys). It runs a temp env file with only GEMINI_API_KEY (or none). Results: level 2 photo via Ask cloud Gemma in 3.4 s, a ladder from the cloud in 1.3 s; level 1 template.\n   - tier.test.ts expectation updated.\n\n   **A items (committed aee8348)**\n   - H3Send read-only row label is send.hostLineSeen \"Friends will see\".\n   - host.svelte.ts setPosition: a street-named spot becomes spot.nearStreet \"Near {street}\" (via packPlaces kind street).\n   - Demo: a \"Leave the demo\" X (demo.leave) on the friendIn/here/spark/outside/done steps; `.demo.coach .actions { display:none }`; sentMin from the demo clock (sentAt).\n   - site.css `.site .band.feat { padding-top: 8px }`.\n   - BuiltWith: Tinker and Entire (site.built.tinker, site.built.entire).\n   - demo e2e checks added.\n\n   **Remember this (committed after aee8348; then flagged off)**\n   - migration 0006_remember.sql: tables `remember` (gathering_id pk, on_by_host, recording_until, note_ct bytea) and `remember_consent` (gathering_id, member_id, ok), both cascading.\n   - apps/server/src/core/remember.ts: `rememberState({on, lit, yes, consent, recordingUntil, now})` returns {on, ready, recording, recording_until}; ready = on && lit && every yes agreed. Also `loadRemember`, and RECORD_MAX_MS = 60000.\n   - apps/server/src/routes/remember.ts, mountRemember:\n     - GET/PUT `/api/v1/gatherings/:id/remember`\n     - PUT `/consent`\n     - POST `/record {action}`\n     - POST `/transcribe` (audio ≤1.2 MB, Scribe diarize, zero-fill)\n     - POST `/summary` (hub only)\n     - PUT `/note {note_ct}`\n     - Each change publishes an SSE `{type:\"remember\"}`.\n     - Rate limits are per member and per gathering.\n     - The flag guard throws a 404 when `!ctx.rememberThis`, plus app.use middleware on `/remember/*`.\n   - Supporting changes:\n     - voice.ts: `conversation()` and `toLines()`.\n     - shared prompts/summary.ts: SUMMARY_SYSTEM, summaryUserPrompt, enforceSummary.\n     - hub-protocol SummaryJob; JobResult.summary.\n     - hub ollama `summaryFromTranscript` and client runSummary.\n     - relay `summary()`.\n     - events.ts LiveMessage \"remember\"; gatherings SSE branch.\n     - sweep.ts audit stores DS12 and auditGathering tables.\n     - errors: not_audio, not_ready.\n     - openapi: 7 operations plus RememberState and config.remember. asyncapi: summaryJob.\n   - Web side:\n     - RememberPanel.svelte: chip, sheet, recording banner with \"Stop for everyone\", seal with aad `r:${id}`.\n     - Aad `r:` added in the shared ICD.\n     - `rememberCtx()` in link.svelte.ts and host.svelte.ts.\n     - The panel is lazy-loaded in LinkPage and HostPage.\n   - Copy and docs:\n     - remember.* keys.\n     - Privacy: site.privacy.l.remember (exact rule); site.privacy.l.voice no longer says \"never record a conversation\".\n     - AI page: ai.remember.\n     - ADR-0031.\n   - Tests:\n     - remember.test.ts: fast-check properties, plus a flag-off test where all 7 routes return 404.\n     - contract scenario tests (harness rememberThis: true).\n     - e2e remember.ts (REMEMBER_THIS=1): 2 phones, real Scribe 720 ms, stop to note 5.3 s, Gemma line \"Friends enjoyed the beautiful view of the pond and geese together.\"\n   - Flag: env `rememberThis: str(\"REMEMBER_THIS\") === \"1\"`, wired through deps, app, main. /config `remember: !!ctx.rememberThis`. Committed \"Park Remember this behind REMEMBER_THIS (off)\" and deployed.\n   - preview/index.ts comment fixed (Telegram fetches on its servers; iMessage and WhatsApp build the preview on the sender's phone).\n   - The post draft's \"Suggested:\" quote was replaced with \"[FIELD: the founder's own why, in their own words. Not written by anyone else.]\". Committed e6824af.\n\n   **Automations in progress, uncommitted on main**\n   - New apps/web/src/lib/compass/arrive.ts:\n     ```ts\n     export const ARRIVE_M = 30; export const ARRIVE_ACCURACY_M = 20; export const ARRIVE_FIXES = 2; export const UNDO_MS = 10_000;\n     export function createArrival(o = {}): { fix(d: number|null, acc: number|null): boolean; reset(): void } // fires once after N consecutive good fixes\n     ```\n   - New apps/web/test/flow/arrive.test.ts, 5 pass: both real iPhone streams fire by fix 1–3; a 300 m walk fires only inside 30 m; 40 m accuracy never fires; alternating fixes never fire.\n   - LinkPage.svelte:\n     - find() creates guide + arrival.\n     - The onFix wrapper calls `queueMicrotask(() => { const s = guide.state(); if (arrival.fix(s.distance_m, s.accuracy_m) && flow.screen === \"compass\") offerHere(); })`.\n     - offerHere runs a 10 s countdown toast `.auto` (here.auto \"You're at the spot. Marking you here in {s} s.\", button here.undo \"Undo\") and then calls flow.here().\n     - cancelAuto runs on leaveCompass.\n   - (b) host.svelte.ts: `postedToTelegram = $state(false)`, set from `!!tg` in send().\n   - HostPage: `if (ok && !flow.postedToTelegram) void flow.share();`, plus a `.posted` note with sent.telegram \"Posted to your Telegram group.\" on screen \"sent\".\n   - telegram.ts e2e: a navigator.share counter in the init script, and the check \"linked to Telegram: Send posts the card, no share sheet\" PASSES.\n   - svelte-check is 0/0 and copy-lint is 0.\n\n4. **Errors and fixes**\n   - **Tier test expected the old hub-down copy** → updated with sed.\n   - **The cloud-only e2e words check read the heading \"Your invite\"** → it now reads `.tier`'s previous sibling and checks the tier text contains \"cloud\". The python assert failed once because biome had reformatted the file; I replaced the section by index.\n   - **SendMessage failed on a stale socket** → ListAgents, then addressed by name.\n   - **SayFlare `state` variable collided with the $state rune** → renamed to `phase` (earlier).\n   - **Remember routes used the per-IP rate limit** → 429s in contract tests, so I switched to member and gathering keys. Extra group creations hit the per-IP group limit → the small describes share one gathering (`remLit`). The transcribeSpark test got an `x-forwarded-for: 203.0.113.9` header.\n   - **Type errors:**\n     - fc.RecordValue generic → a local World type.\n     - Buffer typing → `Buffer<ArrayBuffer>` / `Uint8Array<ArrayBuffer>`.\n     - not_ready was missing from ErrorCode → added.\n   - **asyncapi placement:**\n     - The summaryJob block was inserted into the channel list, which left duplicate keys → moved.\n     - The voiceBytes line then had the wrong indent → fixed with sed.\n   - **Hub client import** didn't match the biome-formatted multi-line import → rebuilt it with a regex.\n   - **Python heredoc SyntaxError** from a `\\\\'` escape (score update) → rewrote it as a script file.\n   - **`$state` proxy on the group record** → `$state.raw` to avoid structuredClone issues.\n   - **Fixed requirement strings** (cond.didntCatch, compass.disclaimer, app.tier.hub) must stay unchanged; I restored and kept them.\n   - **Demo X named \"Close\"** collided with the I12 \"Close\" → named \"Leave the demo\".\n   - **Earlier:** a site.css leak into the app was fixed by scoping site.css under `.site`.\n\n5. **Problem solving**\n\n   **Live:**\n   - Deploys: b6fd014 (setup copy), aee8348 (A), Remember this, then the flag-off commit.\n   - Smoke passes on live and the hub is connected.\n\n   **Fresh-eyes scores:** 5, 6, 5, 6, 6 across 5 rounds. Round 5's leftovers are fixed. Round 6 is pending.\n\n   **Pre-review pass done earlier:**\n   - CI passes.\n   - Every e2e passes.\n   - check-env: no secrets in the repo or build.\n   - scan-sessions --public: 1,539 email and 22 phone matches in 101/166 checkpoints, 0 secrets.\n   - docs/post/REVIEW.md written.\n\n   **JS budget:** /app 147.5 KB, /g/ 146.5 KB before the automations.\n\n6. **All user messages**\n   - The only direct user-role message this stretch was the session continuation instruction. All other instructions came via manager cross-session messages (the founder via the CTO), in order:\n     - round 5 now, then the pre-review pass (CI, every e2e, smoke, check-env, scan-sessions dry run, REVIEW.md), then hold;\n     - the usage limit reset, continue;\n     - the setup-copy founder feedback, items 1–4 (Host your own copy, three levels verified by e2e, hub-down copy as a choice, \"Nothing to install\" in the post), report briefly;\n     - next: A (6 leftovers, the faded heading, Run it → Host your own, Built with Tinker+Entire, round 6 targeting 8/10) and B (learns your words);\n     - the website motion brief \"One evening, scrolled\" (later replaced);\n     - founder decisions: the new order, Remember this full spec, Sounds of the spot spec, TabPFN out, code freeze 1 AM;\n     - start the website subagent now in its own worktree (site-motion), new site.* keys only;\n     - the revised website brief (9 priorities: the hero not taken over, the scroll story replaces Steps/Shrink, Start in a minute, Crew space, \"Right now\", Try it on your photo, time-zone sunset, Under the hood on /how, signature taps, the \"At the spot\" rail, the \"Judging? 60-second tour\" link; Lenis and the phone morph dropped);\n     - the app motion stream as a second subagent (app-motion), 7 items, plus the WhatsApp poll section and the round-6 question;\n     - correction: do NOT add the WhatsApp poll section to the site or post; keep the round-6 question;\n     - the re-plan (priorities 1–7, rules, the preview comment one-liner, post plan coming);\n     - the post plan (POST-PLAN.md; only delete the invented quote until the freeze);\n     - start a third subagent for docs/post now with three marked holes and two images.\n\n7. **Pending tasks**\n   - Finish automation (a) \"Again\" on Home (and Crew if feasible without colliding with app-motion). Then commit the automations (a, b, c) with tests, deploy, smoke, and send a one-line status to the manager stating what was cut.\n   - Sounds of the spot once the lab sends numbers: fixed labels, an enforce guard, the people-drop rule, hub only, 100% speech-drop recall on ≥10 clips, report the number.\n   - Revisit Remember this after step 5. Turn REMEMBER_THIS on live only if solid (the consent tests pass; the e2e passes). Otherwise it stays off, with one next-step line in the post.\n   - Merge the site-motion, app-motion and post-rework branches when they report (notes due about 11:30 PM). Run the gates (Lighthouse 100, axe 0, JS budget, iPhone 13 smooth, CSP), deploy.\n   - Fresh-eyes round 6 (same method, no priming, plus the WhatsApp-poll question with answers quoted verbatim), fix what it finds, report the score honestly.\n   - After the freeze at 1 AM: fill the post holes ([NEW TONIGHT] with only shipped and tested features; [ROUND 6]), cut anything that didn't ship, switch off any unfinished feature, recapture media and the hero GIF.\n   - B (learns your words) only if time is left.\n   - Keep RESUME.md, the backlog and REVIEW.md current.\n\n8. **Current work**\n\n   I was implementing automation (a), one-tap \"Again\" on Home, under the re-plan's priority 4. Automations (c), automatic I'm here, and (b), Telegram direct send, are implemented and tested but not yet committed.\n   - (c): arrive.ts, arrive.test.ts with 5 passing, and the LinkPage wiring with the toast.\n   - (b): host.svelte.ts postedToTelegram, the HostPage skip-share plus the `.posted` note, sent.telegram copy, and the telegram e2e check passing.\n   - The last command (8:21 PM ET) inspected H0Home's actions and props, to decide how to add \"Again\" without colliding with the app-motion subagent, which owns H0Home's presentation:\n     ```\n     69:  {#snippet actions()}\n     70-    <Button icon=\"camera\" haptic=\"tap\" onclick={onlight}>{t(\"home.light\")}</Button>\n     71-    <div class=\"row\">\n     72-      <Button variant=\"text\" onclick={onplan}>{t(\"home.plan\")}</Button>\n     73-      {#if !located}<Button variant=\"text\" onclick={onnear}>{t(\"home.near\")}</Button>{/if}\n     74-      <a class=\"demo\" href=\"/app/demo/\">{t(\"demo.try\")}</a>\n     ```\n     The props are golden, weather, green, located, onlight, onplan, onnear and onmenu.\n\n9. **Optional next step**\n\n   Continue automation (a) from the re-plan: \"One-tap \"Again\" on Home and Crew: the last crew, group size and nearest favourite spot are pre-chosen, and the photo is optional. You can use place-word chips or typed words.\"\n   - Implementation idea:\n     - Add an optional `onagain` prop and a small text button to H0Home. This is a minimal edit; note it for the app-motion merge.\n     - Wire it in HostPage to a new `flow.again()`. It should:\n       - store the last quorum in localStorage at send;\n       - go to the develop typing view with chips and no photo;\n       - pre-set the quorum;\n       - use the current or top Hot spot place.\n     - Add a flow test.\n   - Then:\n     - commit (a), (b) and (c) together;\n     - run the gates: svelte-check, lint, tests, e2e demo/sparks/telegram, budget, axe;\n     - deploy and smoke;\n     - send the manager one status line saying plainly what got cut.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: ~/.claude/projects/-project-flare/904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"57dcf16c-2c6e-4382-a429-a545fe3f5052","timestamp":"2026-10-12T00:22:53.895Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":1,"turnIndex":42},"turnOrigin":"peer","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"<project>/flare","sessionId":"904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"wondrous-tumbling-meteor"}
{"parentUuid":"57dcf16c-2c6e-4382-a429-a545fe3f5052","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"<project>/flare/apps/web/src/lib/components/RememberPanel.svelte","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"<project>/flare/apps/web/src/lib/components/RememberPanel.svelte","content":"<!-- Remember this (ADR-0031): a conversation note made only with everyone's consent.\n     Off by default; the host turns it on for this Flare; each person agrees on their own phone;\n     any no or late joiner keeps it off for everyone, and the screen never says who. When lit and\n     everyone agreed, anyone records up to 60 s; every phone shows the sign live and anyone can\n     stop it. The words come back from ElevenLabs Scribe with speaker labels only, Gemma on our\n     laptop writes one line (none when it's off; never the cloud), and the note is sealed here with\n     the Flare key before it is stored. Deleted with the Flare. -->\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { onMount } from \"svelte\";\n  import Button from \"./Button.svelte\";\n  import Sheet from \"./Sheet.svelte\";\n  import Icon from \"./Icon.svelte\";\n  import { t } from \"#lib/copy/index.ts\";\n  import { startSpark, type Recording } from \"#lib/voice/spark.ts\";\n  type Ctx = { id: string; auth: string; key: CryptoKey; crypto: { sealJson(k: CryptoKey, aad: `r:${string}`, v: unknown): Promise<string>; open(k: CryptoKey, aad: `r:${string}`, s: string): Promise<Uint8Array> } };\n  type State = { on: boolean; ready: boolean; recording: boolean; recording_until: string | null; has_note: boolean; my_ok?: boolean | null; is_host?: boolean; note_ct?: string | null };\n  type Note = { v: 1; lines: { speaker: string; text: string }[]; summary: string | null };\n  let { ctx, lit = false, onspark }: { ctx: Ctx; lit?: boolean; onspark?: (line: string) => void } = $props();\n\n  const base = $derived(`/api/v1/gatherings/${ctx.id}/remember`);\n  let st = $state<State | null>(null);\n  let open = $state(false);\n  let error = $state(\"\");\n  let working = $state(false);\n  let note = $state<Note | null>(null);\n  let now = $state(Date.now());\n  let rec: Recording | null = null;\n  let mine = false; // this phone is the one recording\n\n  const call = async (path: string, method: string, body?: unknown, type = \"application/json\") => {\n    const r = await fetch(`${base}${path}`, {\n      method,\n      headers: { authorization: ctx.auth, ...(body !== undefined ? { \"content-type\": type } : {}) },\n      body: body === undefined ? undefined : body instanceof Blob ? body : JSON.stringify(body),\n    });\n    if (!r.ok) throw new Error(String(r.status));\n    return r.json();\n  };\n  async function load() {\n    try {\n      const s = (await call(\"\", \"GET\")) as State;\n      st = s;\n      if (s.note_ct) note = JSON.parse(new TextDecoder().decode(await ctx.crypto.open(ctx.key, `r:${ctx.id}`, s.note_ct))) as Note;\n    } catch {\n      // gone or offline: the panel stays quiet\n    }\n  }\n  function apply(s: State) {\n    const hadNote = st?.has_note;\n    st = { ...st, ...s };\n    if (!s.recording && mine) rec?.stop(); // someone stopped it for everyone, or a no came in\n    if (s.has_note && !hadNote) void load();\n  }\n  onMount(() => {\n    void load();\n    const es = new EventSource(`/api/v1/gatherings/${ctx.id}/events`);\n    es.addEventListener(\"remember\", (e) => apply(JSON.parse((e as MessageEvent).data) as State));\n    const tick = setInterval(() => (now = Date.now()), 1000);\n    return () => {\n      es.close();\n      clearInterval(tick);\n      rec?.stop();\n    };\n  });\n\n  const left = $derived(st?.recording_until ? Math.max(0, Math.ceil((Date.parse(st.recording_until) - now) / 1000)) : 0);\n  async function setOn(on: boolean) {\n    error = \"\";\n    st = { ...(st as State), ...((await call(\"\", \"PUT\", { on })) as State), my_ok: on };\n  }\n  async function consent(ok: boolean) {\n    st = { ...(st as State), ...((await call(\"/consent\", \"PUT\", { ok })) as State), my_ok: ok };\n  }\n  async function record() {\n    error = \"\";\n    try {\n      rec = await startSpark(60_000);\n    } catch {\n      error = t(\"remember.failed\");\n      return;\n    }\n    mine = true;\n    try {\n      apply((await call(\"/record\", \"POST\", { action: \"start\" })) as State);\n    } catch {\n      rec.stop();\n      mine = false;\n      error = t(\"remember.off\");\n      return;\n    }\n    open = false;\n    const clip = await rec.done;\n    rec = null;\n    mine = false;\n    await call(\"/record\", \"POST\", { action: \"stop\" }).catch(() => {});\n    if (!clip) return;\n    working = true;\n    try {\n      const { lines } = (await call(\"/transcribe\", \"POST\", clip, clip.type)) as { lines: Note[\"lines\"] | null };\n      if (!lines?.length) throw new Error(\"empty\");\n      const text = lines.map((l) => `${l.speaker}: ${l.text}`).join(\"\\n\");\n      const { line } = (await call(\"/summary\", \"POST\", { text }).catch(() => ({ line: null }))) as { line: string | null };\n      const n: Note = { v: 1, lines, summary: line };\n      await call(\"/note\", \"PUT\", { note_ct: await ctx.crypto.sealJson(ctx.key, `r:${ctx.id}`, n) });\n      note = n;\n    } catch {\n      error = t(\"remember.failed\");\n    } finally {\n      working = false;\n    }\n  }\n  const stop = () => void call(\"/record\", \"POST\", { action: \"stop\" }).then((s) => apply(s as State)).catch(() => {});\n</script>\n\n{#if st?.recording}\n  <!-- On every phone, live: the sign and a stop anyone can tap. -->\n  <div class=\"rec\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"assertive\">\n    <span class=\"dot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><b>{t(\"remember.recording\", { s: left })}</b>\n    <button class=\"stop\" onclick={stop}>{t(\"remember.stop\")}</button>\n  </div>\n{/if}\n\n{#if st && (st.is_host || st.on || note)}\n  <button class=\"chip\" onclick={() => (open = true)} aria-haspopup=\"dialog\">\n    <Icon name=\"mic\" size={18} /><span>{working ? t(\"remember.working\") : t(\"remember.chip\")}</span>\n  </button>\n{/if}\n\n<Sheet bind:open title={note ? t(\"remember.noteTitle\") : t(\"remember.title\")}>\n  {#if note}\n    {#if note.summary}<p class=\"summary\">{note.summary}</p>{:else}<p class=\"t-small t-muted\">{t(\"remember.noSummary\")}</p>{/if}\n    <!-- svelte-ignore a11y_no_noninteractive_tabindex (keyboard scroll, axe scrollable-region-focusable) -->\n    <ul class=\"lines\" tabindex=\"0\">{#each note.lines as l}<li><b>{l.speaker}</b> {l.text}</li>{/each}</ul>\n    {#if note.summary && onspark}<Button variant=\"secondary\" icon=\"spark\" onclick={() => onspark?.(note?.summary ?? \"\")}>{t(\"remember.saveSpark\")}</Button>{/if}\n    <p class=\"t-small t-muted\">{t(\"remember.privacy\")}</p>\n  {:else if st?.is_host && !st.on}\n    <p>{t(\"remember.hostBody\")}</p>\n    <Button onclick={() => void setOn(true)}>{t(\"remember.turnOn\")}</Button>\n  {:else if st && !st.is_host && st.on && st.my_ok == null}\n    <p>{t(\"remember.askBody\")}</p>\n    <Button onclick={() => void consent(true)}>{t(\"remember.agree\")}</Button>\n    <Button variant=\"text\" onclick={() => void consent(false)}>{t(\"remember.decline\")}</Button>\n  {:else if st?.ready && lit}\n    <p class=\"warn\"><Icon name=\"info\" size={20} /><span>{t(\"remember.warn\")}</span></p>\n    <Button icon=\"mic\" onclick={() => void record()}>{t(\"remember.record\")}</Button>\n  {:else if st?.on}\n    <p role=\"status\">{st.my_ok === false ? t(\"remember.off\") : lit ? t(\"remember.waiting\") : t(\"remember.notLit\")}</p>\n    {#if st.is_host}<Button variant=\"text\" onclick={() => void setOn(false)}>{t(\"remember.turnOff\")}</Button>{/if}\n  {/if}\n  {#if error}<p class=\"err\" role=\"alert\">{error}</p>{/if}\n</Sheet>\n\n<style>\n  .chip { position: fixed; z-index: 35; left: 12px; top: calc(env(safe-area-inset-top, 0) + 64px); min-height: 44px; display: inline-flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center; padding: 0 14px; border: 0; border-radius: 999px; background: rgb(0 0 0 / 0.55); color: #fff; font-weight: 700; }\n  .rec { position: fixed; z-index: 60; left: 0; right: 0; top: 0; display: flex; gap: 10px; align-items: center; padding: calc(env(safe-area-inset-top, 0) + 10px) 14px 10px; background: #b3261e; color: #fff; }\n  .dot { width: 12px; height: 12px; border-radius: 50%; background: #fff; animation: blink 1s steps(2, start) infinite; }\n  .stop { margin-left: auto; min-height: 44px; padding: 0 14px; border: 2px solid #fff; border-radius: 999px; background: transparent; color: #fff; font-weight: 800; }\n  .summary { margin: 0; font-weight: 700; font-size: 1.125rem; }\n  .lines { margin: 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; display: grid; gap: 6px; max-height: 40vh; overflow: auto; }\n  .warn { display: flex; gap: 8px; align-items: center; margin: 0; font-weight: 700; }\n  .err { margin: 0; font-weight: 700; }\n  p { margin: 0; }\n  @keyframes blink { to { visibility: hidden; } }\n  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .dot { animation: none; } }\n</style>\n","numLines":166,"startLine":1,"totalLines":166}},"displayPath":"apps/web/src/lib/components/RememberPanel.svelte"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"dfb9390d-1e6e-4c56-be17-feca5d154cb5","timestamp":"2026-10-12T00:22:54.122Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"<project>/flare/apps/web/src/lib/components/RememberPanel.svelte\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t<!-- Remember this (ADR-0031): a conversation note made only with everyone's consent.\n2\t     Off by default; the host turns it on for this Flare; each person agrees on their own phone;\n3\t     any no or late joiner keeps it off for everyone, and the screen never says who. When lit and\n4\t     everyone agreed, anyone records up to 60 s; every phone shows the sign live and anyone can\n5\t     stop it. The words come back from ElevenLabs Scribe with speaker labels only, Gemma on our\n6\t     laptop writes one line (none when it's off; never the cloud), and the note is sealed here with\n7\t     the Flare key before it is stored. Deleted with the Flare. -->\n8\t<script lang=\"ts\">\n9\t  import { onMount } from \"svelte\";\n10\t  import Button from \"./Button.svelte\";\n11\t  import Sheet from \"./Sheet.svelte\";\n12\t  import Icon from \"./Icon.svelte\";\n13\t  import { t } from \"#lib/copy/index.ts\";\n14\t  import { startSpark, type Recording } from \"#lib/voice/spark.ts\";\n15\t  type Ctx = { id: string; auth: string; key: CryptoKey; crypto: { sealJson(k: CryptoKey, aad: `r:${string}`, v: unknown): Promise<string>; open(k: CryptoKey, aad: `r:${string}`, s: string): Promise<Uint8Array> } };\n16\t  type State = { on: boolean; ready: boolean; recording: boolean; recording_until: string | null; has_note: boolean; my_ok?: boolean | null; is_host?: boolean; note_ct?: string | null };\n17\t  type Note = { v: 1; lines: { speaker: string; text: string }[]; summary: string | null };\n18\t  let { ctx, lit = false, onspark }: { ctx: Ctx; lit?: boolean; onspark?: (line: string) => void } = $props();\n19\t\n20\t  const base = $derived(`/api/v1/gatherings/${ctx.id}/remember`);\n21\t  let st = $state<State | null>(null);\n22\t  let open = $state(false);\n23\t  let error = $state(\"\");\n24\t  let working = $state(false);\n25\t  let note = $state<Note | null>(null);\n26\t  let now = $state(Date.now());\n27\t  let rec: Recording | null = null;\n28\t  let mine = false; // this phone is the one recording\n29\t\n30\t  const call = async (path: string, method: string, body?: unknown, type = \"application/json\") => {\n31\t    const r = await fetch(`${base}${path}`, {\n32\t      method,\n33\t      headers: { authorization: ctx.auth, ...(body !== undefined ? { \"content-type\": type } : {}) },\n34\t      body: body === undefined ? undefined : body instanceof Blob ? body : JSON.stringify(body),\n35\t    });\n36\t    if (!r.ok) throw new Error(String(r.status));\n37\t    return r.json();\n38\t  };\n39\t  async function load() {\n40\t    try {\n41\t      const s = (await call(\"\", \"GET\")) as State;\n42\t      st = s;\n43\t      if (s.note_ct) note = JSON.parse(new TextDecoder().decode(await ctx.crypto.open(ctx.key, `r:${ctx.id}`, s.note_ct))) as Note;\n44\t    } catch {\n45\t      // gone or offline: the panel stays quiet\n46\t    }\n47\t  }\n48\t  function apply(s: State) {\n49\t    const hadNote = st?.has_note;\n50\t    st = { ...st, ...s };\n51\t    if (!s.recording && mine) rec?.stop(); // someone stopped it for everyone, or a no came in\n52\t    if (s.has_note && !hadNote) void load();\n53\t  }\n54\t  onMount(() => {\n55\t    void load();\n56\t    const es = new EventSource(`/api/v1/gatherings/${ctx.id}/events`);\n57\t    es.addEventListener(\"remember\", (e) => apply(JSON.parse((e as MessageEvent).data) as State));\n58\t    const tick = setInterval(() => (now = Date.now()), 1000);\n59\t    return () => {\n60\t      es.close();\n61\t      clearInterval(tick);\n62\t      rec?.stop();\n63\t    };\n64\t  });\n65\t\n66\t  const left = $derived(st?.recording_until ? Math.max(0, Math.ceil((Date.parse(st.recording_until) - now) / 1000)) : 0);\n67\t  async function setOn(on: boolean) {\n68\t    error = \"\";\n69\t    st = { ...(st as State), ...((await call(\"\", \"PUT\", { on })) as State), my_ok: on };\n70\t  }\n71\t  async function consent(ok: boolean) {\n72\t    st = { ...(st as State), ...((await call(\"/consent\", \"PUT\", { ok })) as State), my_ok: ok };\n73\t  }\n74\t  async function record() {\n75\t    error = \"\";\n76\t    try {\n77\t      rec = await startSpark(60_000);\n78\t    } catch {\n79\t      error = t(\"remember.failed\");\n80\t      return;\n81\t    }\n82\t    mine = true;\n83\t    try {\n84\t      apply((await call(\"/record\", \"POST\", { action: \"start\" })) as State);\n85\t    } catch {\n86\t      rec.stop();\n87\t      mine = false;\n88\t      error = t(\"remember.off\");\n89\t      return;\n90\t    }\n91\t    open = false;\n92\t    const clip = await rec.done;\n93\t    rec = null;\n94\t    mine = false;\n95\t    await call(\"/record\", \"POST\", { action: \"stop\" }).catch(() => {});\n96\t    if (!clip) return;\n97\t    working = true;\n98\t    try {\n99\t      const { lines } = (await call(\"/transcribe\", \"POST\", clip, clip.type)) as { lines: Note[\"lines\"] | null };\n100\t      if (!lines?.length) throw new Error(\"empty\");\n101\t      const text = lines.map((l) => `${l.speaker}: ${l.text}`).join(\"\\n\");\n102\t      const { line } = (await call(\"/summary\", \"POST\", { text }).catch(() => ({ line: null }))) as { line: string | null };\n103\t      const n: Note = { v: 1, lines, summary: line };\n104\t      await call(\"/note\", \"PUT\", { note_ct: await ctx.crypto.sealJson(ctx.key, `r:${ctx.id}`, n) });\n105\t      note = n;\n106\t    } catch {\n107\t      error = t(\"remember.failed\");\n108\t    } finally {\n109\t      working = false;\n110\t    }\n111\t  }\n112\t  const stop = () => void call(\"/record\", \"POST\", { action: \"stop\" }).then((s) => apply(s as State)).catch(() => {});\n113\t</script>\n114\t\n115\t{#if st?.recording}\n116\t  <!-- On every phone, live: the sign and a stop anyone can tap. -->\n117\t  <div class=\"rec\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"assertive\">\n118\t    <span class=\"dot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><b>{t(\"remember.recording\", { s: left })}</b>\n119\t    <button class=\"stop\" onclick={stop}>{t(\"remember.stop\")}</button>\n120\t  </div>\n121\t{/if}\n122\t\n123\t{#if st && (st.is_host || st.on || note)}\n124\t  <button class=\"chip\" onclick={() => (open = true)} aria-haspopup=\"dialog\">\n125\t    <Icon name=\"mic\" size={18} /><span>{working ? t(\"remember.working\") : t(\"remember.chip\")}</span>\n126\t  </button>\n127\t{/if}\n128\t\n129\t<Sheet bind:open title={note ? t(\"remember.noteTitle\") : t(\"remember.title\")}>\n130\t  {#if note}\n131\t    {#if note.summary}<p class=\"summary\">{note.summary}</p>{:else}<p class=\"t-small t-muted\">{t(\"remember.noSummary\")}</p>{/if}\n132\t    <!-- svelte-ignore a11y_no_noninteractive_tabindex (keyboard scroll, axe scrollable-region-focusable) -->\n133\t    <ul class=\"lines\" tabindex=\"0\">{#each note.lines as l}<li><b>{l.speaker}</b> {l.text}</li>{/each}</ul>\n134\t    {#if note.summary && onspark}<Button variant=\"secondary\" icon=\"spark\" onclick={() => onspark?.(note?.summary ?? \"\")}>{t(\"remember.saveSpark\")}</Button>{/if}\n135\t    <p class=\"t-small t-muted\">{t(\"remember.privacy\")}</p>\n136\t  {:else if st?.is_host && !st.on}\n137\t    <p>{t(\"remember.hostBody\")}</p>\n138\t    <Button onclick={() => void setOn(true)}>{t(\"remember.turnOn\")}</Button>\n139\t  {:else if st && !st.is_host && st.on && st.my_ok == null}\n140\t    <p>{t(\"remember.askBody\")}</p>\n141\t    <Button onclick={() => void consent(true)}>{t(\"remember.agree\")}</Button>\n142\t    <Button variant=\"text\" onclick={() => void consent(false)}>{t(\"remember.decline\")}</Button>\n143\t  {:else if st?.ready && lit}\n144\t    <p class=\"warn\"><Icon name=\"info\" size={20} /><span>{t(\"remember.warn\")}</span></p>\n145\t    <Button icon=\"mic\" onclick={() => void record()}>{t(\"remember.record\")}</Button>\n146\t  {:else if st?.on}\n147\t    <p role=\"status\">{st.my_ok === false ? t(\"remember.off\") : lit ? t(\"remember.waiting\") : t(\"remember.notLit\")}</p>\n148\t    {#if st.is_host}<Button variant=\"text\" onclick={() => void setOn(false)}>{t(\"remember.turnOff\")}</Button>{/if}\n149\t  {/if}\n150\t  {#if error}<p class=\"err\" role=\"alert\">{error}</p>{/if}\n151\t</Sheet>\n152\t\n153\t<style>\n154\t  .chip { position: fixed; z-index: 35; left: 12px; top: calc(env(safe-area-inset-top, 0) + 64px); min-height: 44px; display: inline-flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center; padding: 0 14px; border: 0; border-radius: 999px; background: rgb(0 0 0 / 0.55); color: #fff; font-weight: 700; }\n155\t  .rec { position: fixed; z-index: 60; left: 0; right: 0; top: 0; display: flex; gap: 10px; align-items: center; padding: calc(env(safe-area-inset-top, 0) + 10px) 14px 10px; background: #b3261e; color: #fff; }\n156\t  .dot { width: 12px; height: 12px; border-radius: 50%; background: #fff; animation: blink 1s steps(2, start) infinite; }\n157\t  .stop { margin-left: auto; min-height: 44px; padding: 0 14px; border: 2px solid #fff; border-radius: 999px; background: transparent; color: #fff; font-weight: 800; }\n158\t  .summary { margin: 0; font-weight: 700; font-size: 1.125rem; }\n159\t  .lines { margin: 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; display: grid; gap: 6px; max-height: 40vh; overflow: auto; }\n160\t  .warn { display: flex; gap: 8px; align-items: center; margin: 0; font-weight: 700; }\n161\t  .err { margin: 0; font-weight: 700; }\n162\t  p { margin: 0; }\n163\t  @keyframes blink { to { visibility: hidden; } }\n164\t  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .dot { animation: none; } }\n165\t</style>\n166\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"<project>/flare","sessionId":"904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"wondrous-tumbling-meteor"}
{"parentUuid":"dfb9390d-1e6e-4c56-be17-feca5d154cb5","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"<project>/flare/docs/post/REVIEW.md","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"<project>/flare/docs/post/REVIEW.md","content":"# Founder review: what's left before you publish\n\n**Deadline:** Mon Oct 12, 06:59 UTC (Sun 11:59 PM PDT, Mon 2:59 AM ET).\n**The post:** [draft.md](draft.md)\n**Live:** https://flare-outside.onrender.com (main, all checks green)\n**State at hand-off (Sun Oct 11, about 5:30 PM ET):**\n- CI passes: secret scan, lint, types, 775 unit and contract tests, contracts, build, budget, 38 diagrams.\n- Every e2e suite passes: hello, pwa, field 27/27, sparks, loop, telegram, kit a11y, demo, plan, voice, flow on the real stack.\n- axe finds 0 issues on 88 page views.\n- Smoke passes on live.\n- check-env: every setting is set, and no secret value is in the repo or the web build (12 values checked in 1,335 tracked files and 374 build files).\n- Fresh-eyes testers scored 5, 6, 5, 6 and 6 (five rounds, a new tester with no context each time). The post states this. Round 5's fixes shipped after its score, so they have no score of their own.\n\n## 1. Decisions only you can make\n\n| Decision | Why it matters | Where |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **Make the repo public** | The post embeds it (`{% github Hotragn/flare %}`) and the site links to it. Judges expect to read the code | GitHub → Settings → Change visibility |\n| **The agent sessions: scrub, then share** | The `--public` dry run of `npm run scan-sessions -- --public` found **1,539 email addresses and 22 phone-number matches in 101 of 166 checkpoints**, and 0 secrets. Most are likely your account email in session metadata, and some phone matches are probably long numbers. Scrub them before any session goes public | Decide: scrub and share one session, or skip the Entire and DevRelay session parts |\n| **DigitalOcean** | The account answers 402 (blocked for billing). The post marks it **[PENDING DO BILLING]** (lines 98 and 178). If billing is fixed, re-run `npm run smoke -- https://flare-outside.onrender.com --hub-off` and look for `cloud tier: digitalocean`, then remove the markers. If not, delete the DigitalOcean prize line and leave the paragraph as \"wired in, paused\" | DigitalOcean billing |\n| **Google AI Studio billing** | On the free tier, Google may use what it receives to improve its products, and people there may review it. Plan asks always go there when the laptop is off; photos only when the host taps. Paid terms stop that use. Today it's disclosed in the app and on the privacy page | Google Cloud console, project billing |\n| **Stale image folders** | `apps/web/static/scenic/` and the `-640` and `-1280` files in `apps/web/static/scenery/` are untracked leftovers. Delete them | `rm -r` them yourself |\n\n## 2. Fill in the post\n\nEvery `[FIELD]` in [draft.md](draft.md), top to bottom:\n\n1. **Line 22, your quote.** A suggested version is there; accept or rewrite it in your own words.\n2. **Line 40, the video.** 60 to 90 s, following [shot-list.md](shot-list.md). Upload it to YouTube or DEV, then paste the link or embed.\n3. **Line 42, the images.** Upload the four images below it in DEV's editor (\"Upload image\"), and replace each `docs/post/media/...` path with the URL DEV gives you. Optional extras are in [media/README.md](media/README.md), e.g. 03-friend-lit, 09-crew-atlas, 04b-demo-compass-ahead, and sim/fairlane-sim-42.gif.\n4. **Line 51, the meetup line.** If you go outside with friends before posting, replace it with what happened, using real numbers. If not, delete only the `[FIELD: ...]` part.\n5. **Line 65, the repo.** Delete the `[FIELD: make the repo public.]` text once it is public.\n6. **Line 127, a Sentry trace.** In Sentry, open the project's traces view and pick an `invoke_agent flare-ladder` trace whose chat span has `gen_ai.provider.name: google`. Screenshot the waterfall and upload it.\n   - To make one: stop the hub on the Mac and send a Plan draft from the live app.\n7. **Lines 170 and 172, the agent session.** See section 4. If you skip sessions, delete both lines and the Entire prize line (182).\n8. **Line 184, thanks.** Name anyone who tried it, with their OK, or delete the line.\n9. **Line 7 to 11, the HTML comment.** Delete it.\n\nAlso check:\n- the title;\n- the tags (`devchallenge, hf26challenge` are required; `gemma, opensource` are ours);\n- the cover image: `brand/export/social/dev-cover-1000x420.png`.\n\n## 3. Publish on DEV (your yes)\n\n1. On dev.to, click Create Post, switch to the Markdown editor, and paste all of [draft.md](draft.md), front matter included. Keep `published: false` for now.\n2. Upload the cover (`brand/export/social/dev-cover-1000x420.png`) and the images, and replace the paths (section 2).\n3. Click Preview. Check that:\n   - the first line links the Week 1 challenge;\n   - the GitHub embed renders, which only works once the repo is public;\n   - the \"Details\" anchor links jump to their sections.\n4. Set `published: true` and Publish. Do this by Mon 06:59 UTC.\n\nA Claude session can do steps 1 and 2 for you through DevRelay (`create_article` with `published: false`). It would only stage a draft in your account, and it needs your yes first. Publishing stays your tap.\n\n## 4. Agent session through DevRelay (optional; it helps the Entire category)\n\n1. Pick the session. Suggested: the Voice Flare build, where Gemma first heard audio, or the round-3 fresh-eyes fix, which found the CSS leak.\n2. Scrub it. Run `npm run scan-sessions -- --public` and remove or redact every email and phone match it lists for that session's checkpoint, then re-run until it reports 0.\n3. Save it with DevRelay. In a Claude session, ask: \"Save this session with DevRelay.\" It uploads unlisted by default.\n4. Make it public in DevRelay, then paste its embed (or link) at line 170 of the post.\n5. Add the Entire checkpoint links for the same session at line 172, and one line at 182.\n\n## 5. After publishing\n\n- Open the live post and click every link and anchor.\n- Optional: enter the post in the challenge through DevRelay (`enter_challenge`), if the challenge page asks for it. The template line and the `hf26challenge` tag are what the challenge requires.\n- Keep the hub running on the Mac (`FLARE_SERVER_URL=wss://flare-outside.onrender.com npm run hub`), so judges trying the live app get Gemma on the laptop and not only the cloud fallback.\n","numLines":69,"startLine":1,"totalLines":69}},"displayPath":"docs/post/REVIEW.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"37dd81af-4cbb-43c9-9af5-4e64ba4dda1f","timestamp":"2026-10-12T00:22:54.122Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"<project>/flare/docs/post/REVIEW.md\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t# Founder review: what's left before you publish\n2\t\n3\t**Deadline:** Mon Oct 12, 06:59 UTC (Sun 11:59 PM PDT, Mon 2:59 AM ET).\n4\t**The post:** [draft.md](draft.md)\n5\t**Live:** https://flare-outside.onrender.com (main, all checks green)\n6\t**State at hand-off (Sun Oct 11, about 5:30 PM ET):**\n7\t- CI passes: secret scan, lint, types, 775 unit and contract tests, contracts, build, budget, 38 diagrams.\n8\t- Every e2e suite passes: hello, pwa, field 27/27, sparks, loop, telegram, kit a11y, demo, plan, voice, flow on the real stack.\n9\t- axe finds 0 issues on 88 page views.\n10\t- Smoke passes on live.\n11\t- check-env: every setting is set, and no secret value is in the repo or the web build (12 values checked in 1,335 tracked files and 374 build files).\n12\t- Fresh-eyes testers scored 5, 6, 5, 6 and 6 (five rounds, a new tester with no context each time). The post states this. Round 5's fixes shipped after its score, so they have no score of their own.\n13\t\n14\t## 1. Decisions only you can make\n15\t\n16\t| Decision | Why it matters | Where |\n17\t| --- | --- | --- |\n18\t| **Make the repo public** | The post embeds it (`{% github Hotragn/flare %}`) and the site links to it. Judges expect to read the code | GitHub → Settings → Change visibility |\n19\t| **The agent sessions: scrub, then share** | The `--public` dry run of `npm run scan-sessions -- --public` found **1,539 email addresses and 22 phone-number matches in 101 of 166 checkpoints**, and 0 secrets. Most are likely your account email in session metadata, and some phone matches are probably long numbers. Scrub them before any session goes public | Decide: scrub and share one session, or skip the Entire and DevRelay session parts |\n20\t| **DigitalOcean** | The account answers 402 (blocked for billing). The post marks it **[PENDING DO BILLING]** (lines 98 and 178). If billing is fixed, re-run `npm run smoke -- https://flare-outside.onrender.com --hub-off` and look for `cloud tier: digitalocean`, then remove the markers. If not, delete the DigitalOcean prize line and leave the paragraph as \"wired in, paused\" | DigitalOcean billing |\n21\t| **Google AI Studio billing** | On the free tier, Google may use what it receives to improve its products, and people there may review it. Plan asks always go there when the laptop is off; photos only when the host taps. Paid terms stop that use. Today it's disclosed in the app and on the privacy page | Google Cloud console, project billing |\n22\t| **Stale image folders** | `apps/web/static/scenic/` and the `-640` and `-1280` files in `apps/web/static/scenery/` are untracked leftovers. Delete them | `rm -r` them yourself |\n23\t\n24\t## 2. Fill in the post\n25\t\n26\tEvery `[FIELD]` in [draft.md](draft.md), top to bottom:\n27\t\n28\t1. **Line 22, your quote.** A suggested version is there; accept or rewrite it in your own words.\n29\t2. **Line 40, the video.** 60 to 90 s, following [shot-list.md](shot-list.md). Upload it to YouTube or DEV, then paste the link or embed.\n30\t3. **Line 42, the images.** Upload the four images below 