steps 1 and 2 for you through DevRelay (`create_article` with `published: false`). It would only stage a draft in your account, and it needs your yes first. Publishing stays your tap.\n55\t\n56\t## 4. Agent session through DevRelay (optional; it helps the Entire category)\n57\t\n58\t1. Pick the session. Suggested: the Voice Flare build, where Gemma first heard audio, or the round-3 fresh-eyes fix, which found the CSS leak.\n59\t2. Scrub it. Run `npm run scan-sessions -- --public` and remove or redact every email and phone match it lists for that session's checkpoint, then re-run until it reports 0.\n60\t3. Save it with DevRelay. In a Claude session, ask: \"Save this session with DevRelay.\" It uploads unlisted by default.\n61\t4. Make it public in DevRelay, then paste its embed (or link) at line 170 of the post.\n62\t5. Add the Entire checkpoint links for the same session at line 172, and one line at 182.\n63\t\n64\t## 5. After publishing\n65\t\n66\t- Open the live post and click every link and anchor.\n67\t- Optional: enter the post in the challenge through DevRelay (`enter_challenge`), if the challenge page asks for it. The template line and the `hf26challenge` tag are what the challenge requires.\n68\t- Keep the hub running on the Mac (`FLARE_SERVER_URL=wss://flare-outside.onrender.com npm run hub`), so judges trying the live app get Gemma on the laptop and not only the cloud fallback.\n69\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"<project>/flare","sessionId":"904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"wondrous-tumbling-meteor"}
{"parentUuid":"37dd81af-4cbb-43c9-9af5-4e64ba4dda1f","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"<tmp>/904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa/tasks/btmre5jwp.output","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"<tmp>/904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa/tasks/btmre5jwp.output","content":"1539 email-address\n  22 phone-number\n     101\nsession scan: 166 checkpoints, 778 files, 10 local values checked, 0 findings\n\n[exited with code 0]\n","numLines":7,"startLine":1,"totalLines":7}},"displayPath":"../../../../../..<tmp>/904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa/tasks/btmre5jwp.output"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"2b6f6923-5eda-4568-a8e3-d64cbabc9515","timestamp":"2026-10-12T00:22:54.122Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"<tmp>/904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa/tasks/btmre5jwp.output\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t1539 email-address\n2\t  22 phone-number\n3\t     101\n4\tsession scan: 166 checkpoints, 778 files, 10 local values checked, 0 findings\n5\t\n6\t[exited with code 0]\n7\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"<project>/flare","sessionId":"904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"wondrous-tumbling-meteor"}
{"parentUuid":"2b6f6923-5eda-4568-a8e3-d64cbabc9515","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"<project>/flare/docs/post/media/README.md","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"<project>/flare/docs/post/media/README.md","content":"# Post media\n\nThese are real screenshots from the real app on the real stack: the server, the hub running Gemma 4 E4B on this Mac, the engine and PGlite. They were taken in Chrome at iPhone size (390x844 @2x), JPEG quality 78, on Sun 2026-10-11 at about 15:45 ET, by `scripts/capture-media.ts`. Re-run it with `npm run build && node scripts/capture-media.ts`.\n\nThe host picks a real photo through the app's own \"Pick a photo\": Eagle Lake, Acadia National Park, public domain (NPS, see [docs/credits/photos.md](../../credits/photos.md)). The fake camera's test pattern isn't used. The Ember shot jumps 31 minutes with the e2e test clock, which only exists with an in-memory database. Nothing else is staged.\n\n| File | Moment | From |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 00-home.jpg | Home: golden hour, the weather, the nearest green spot, Light a Flare | capture-media.ts |\n| 01-host-words.jpg | The photo developed, with the invite Gemma 4 wrote from it (\"Meet by the quiet water's edge\") | capture-media.ts |\n| 01-host-send.jpg | Send it: how many it needs, where you'll be | capture-media.ts |\n| 01-host-sent.jpg | Sent | capture-media.ts |\n| 02-friend-invite.jpg | The friend's invite: photo, words, walk time, the count, I'm in | capture-media.ts |\n| 03-friend-lit.jpg, 03-host-lit.jpg | It's lit, on both phones, with Tell the chat on the host's | capture-media.ts |\n| 04-friend-compass.jpg | Find them: 400 m. A headless browser has no compass, so it asks to hold the phone flat | capture-media.ts |\n| 04b-demo-compass-ahead.jpg | Find them with a heading: \"The bench by the willow is straight ahead\" | e2e demo |\n| 05-friend-spark.jpg | Leaving a Spark, with Say it (Voice Spark) | capture-media.ts |\n| 06-friend-ember.jpg | Needs 3, one yes, 31 minutes later: the smaller plan at West Road | capture-media.ts |\n| 07-telegram-card-kindling.png, 07-telegram-card-lit.png | The Telegram card, Kindling and Lit, from the server's own renderer | earlier capture; the renderer is unchanged |\n| 08-voice-flare-send.png | A Voice Flare: \"Meet at the pond bench\", written by Gemma 4 from what was said, with no photo | e2e voice-flare (real hub) |\n| 09-crew-atlas.png | The Crew Atlas, drawn on the phone from the sealed Hot spots | e2e sparks (real stack) |\n| 10-plan-lit.png | A Plan solved at the deadline: step 3, the biggest step all three can do | e2e plan (real stack) |\n| 11-demo-friend-view.jpg | The demo's friend view | e2e demo |\n| 12-site-home-phone.png, 13-site-feature-cards.png | The website on a phone, and the feature cards on desktop | local build |\n| 14-desktop-qr-note.png | The app on a desktop: the phone column and \"Made for your phone\" with a QR code | local build |\n| sim/fairlane-sim-42.gif | \"A Saturday in Fairlane, played by 48 friends\": the simulation (labelled Simulation) | tools/sim |\n\nStill to add: the founder's iPhone screen recording from [shot-list.md](../shot-list.md), and a Sentry trace screenshot from the live project (it needs the founder's Sentry login).\n","numLines":29,"startLine":1,"totalLines":29}},"displayPath":"docs/post/media/README.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"a411be16-d96a-4baf-823d-6744bc7b7a69","timestamp":"2026-10-12T00:22:54.122Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"<project>/flare/docs/post/media/README.md\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t# Post media\n2\t\n3\tThese are real screenshots from the real app on the real stack: the server, the hub running Gemma 4 E4B on this Mac, the engine and PGlite. They were taken in Chrome at iPhone size (390x844 @2x), JPEG quality 78, on Sun 2026-10-11 at about 15:45 ET, by `scripts/capture-media.ts`. Re-run it with `npm run build && node scripts/capture-media.ts`.\n4\t\n5\tThe host picks a real photo through the app's own \"Pick a photo\": Eagle Lake, Acadia National Park, public domain (NPS, see [docs/credits/photos.md](../../credits/photos.md)). The fake camera's test pattern isn't used. The Ember shot jumps 31 minutes with the e2e test clock, which only exists with an in-memory database. Nothing else is staged.\n6\t\n7\t| File | Moment | From |\n8\t| --- | --- | --- |\n9\t| 00-home.jpg | Home: golden hour, the weather, the nearest green spot, Light a Flare | capture-media.ts |\n10\t| 01-host-words.jpg | The photo developed, with the invite Gemma 4 wrote from it (\"Meet by the quiet water's edge\") | capture-media.ts |\n11\t| 01-host-send.jpg | Send it: how many it needs, where you'll be | capture-media.ts |\n12\t| 01-host-sent.jpg | Sent | capture-media.ts |\n13\t| 02-friend-invite.jpg | The friend's invite: photo, words, walk time, the count, I'm in | capture-media.ts |\n14\t| 03-friend-lit.jpg, 03-host-lit.jpg | It's lit, on both phones, with Tell the chat on the host's | capture-media.ts |\n15\t| 04-friend-compass.jpg | Find them: 400 m. A headless browser has no compass, so it asks to hold the phone flat | capture-media.ts |\n16\t| 04b-demo-compass-ahead.jpg | Find them with a heading: \"The bench by the willow is straight ahead\" | e2e demo |\n17\t| 05-friend-spark.jpg | Leaving a Spark, with Say it (Voice Spark) | capture-media.ts |\n18\t| 06-friend-ember.jpg | Needs 3, one yes, 31 minutes later: the smaller plan at West Road | capture-media.ts |\n19\t| 07-telegram-card-kindling.png, 07-telegram-card-lit.png | The Telegram card, Kindling and Lit, from the server's own renderer | earlier capture; the renderer is unchanged |\n20\t| 08-voice-flare-send.png | A Voice Flare: \"Meet at the pond bench\", written by Gemma 4 from what was said, with no photo | e2e voice-flare (real hub) |\n21\t| 09-crew-atlas.png | The Crew Atlas, drawn on the phone from the sealed Hot spots | e2e sparks (real stack) |\n22\t| 10-plan-lit.png | A Plan solved at the deadline: step 3, the biggest step all three can do | e2e plan (real stack) |\n23\t| 11-demo-friend-view.jpg | The demo's friend view | e2e demo |\n24\t| 12-site-home-phone.png, 13-site-feature-cards.png | The website on a phone, and the feature cards on desktop | local build |\n25\t| 14-desktop-qr-note.png | The app on a desktop: the phone column and \"Made for your phone\" with a QR code | local build |\n26\t| sim/fairlane-sim-42.gif | \"A Saturday in Fairlane, played by 48 friends\": the simulation (labelled Simulation) | tools/sim |\n27\t\n28\tStill to add: the founder's iPhone screen recording from [shot-list.md](../shot-list.md), and a Sentry trace screenshot from the live project (it needs the founder's Sentry login).\n29\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"<project>/flare","sessionId":"904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"wondrous-tumbling-meteor"}
