{"parentUuid":"dae51ecf-037f-4b9d-9759-f7ad1d986f9e","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[{"name":"Monitor","description":"Start a background monitor that streams events from a long-running script. Each stdout line is an event — you keep working and notifications arrive in the chat. Events arrive on their own schedule and are not replies from the user, even if one lands while you're waiting for the user to answer a question.\n\nPick by how many notifications you need:\n- **One** (\"tell me when the server is ready / the build finishes\") → use **Bash with `run_in_background`** and a command that exits when the condition is true, e.g. `until grep -q \"Ready in\" dev.log; do sleep 0.5; done`. You get a single completion notification when it exits.\n- **One per occurrence, until the monitor expires (re-arm to continue)** (\"tell me every time an ERROR line appears\") → Monitor with an unbounded command (`tail -f`, `inotifywait -m`, `while true`).\n- **One per occurrence, until a known end** (\"emit each CI step result, stop when the run completes\") → Monitor with a command that emits lines and then exits.\n\nYour script's stdout is the event stream. Each line becomes a notification. Exit ends the watch.\n\n  # Each matching log line is an event\n  tail -f /var/log/app.log | grep --line-buffered \"ERROR\"\n\n  # Each file change is an event\n  inotifywait -m --format '%e %f' /watched/dir\n\n  # Poll GitHub for new PR comments and emit one line per new comment\n  last=$(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)\n  while true; do\n    now=$(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)\n    gh api \"repos/owner/repo/issues/123/comments?since=$last\" --jq '.[] | \"\\(.user.login): \\(.body)\"'\n    last=$now; sleep 30\n  done\n\n  # Node script that emits events as they arrive (e.g. WebSocket listener)\n  node watch-for-events.js\n\n  # Per-occurrence with a natural end: emit each CI check as it lands, exit when the run completes\n  prev=\"\"\n  while true; do\n    s=$(gh pr checks 123 --json name,bucket)\n    cur=$(jq -r '.[] | select(.bucket!=\"pending\") | \"\\(.name): \\(.bucket)\"' <<<\"$s\" | sort)\n    comm -13 <(echo \"$prev\") <(echo \"$cur\")\n    prev=$cur\n    jq -e 'all(.bucket!=\"pending\")' <<<\"$s\" >/dev/null && break\n    sleep 30\n  done\n\n**Don't use an unbounded command for a single notification.** `tail -f`, `inotifywait -m`, and `while true` never exit on their own, so the monitor stays armed until timeout even after the event has fired. For \"tell me when X is ready,\" use Bash `run_in_background` with an `until` loop instead (one notification, ends in seconds). Note that `tail -f log | grep -m 1 ...` does *not* fix this: if the log goes quiet after the match, `tail` never receives SIGPIPE and the pipeline hangs anyway.\n\n**Script quality:**\n- Every pipe stage must flush per line or matches sit in its buffer unseen: `grep` needs `--line-buffered`, `awk` needs `fflush()`. `head` cannot flush at all — `| head -N` delivers nothing until N matches accumulate, then ends the stream.\n- In poll loops, handle transient failures (`curl ... || true`) — one failed request shouldn't kill the monitor.\n- Poll intervals: 30s+ for remote APIs (rate limits), 0.5-1s for local checks.\n- Write a specific `description` — it appears in every notification (\"errors in deploy.log\" not \"watching logs\").\n- Only stdout is the event stream. Stderr goes to the output file (readable via Read) but does not trigger notifications — for a command you run directly (e.g. `python train.py 2>&1 | grep --line-buffered ...`), merge stderr with `2>&1` so its failures reach your filter. (No effect on `tail -f` of an existing log — that file only contains what its writer redirected.)\n\n**Coverage — silence is not success.** When watching a job or process for an outcome, your filter must match every terminal state, not just the happy path. A monitor that greps only for the success marker stays silent through a crashloop, a hung process, or an unexpected exit — and silence looks identical to \"still running.\" Before arming, ask: *if this process crashed right now, would my filter emit anything?* If not, widen it.\n\n  # Wrong — silent on crash, hang, or any non-success exit\n  tail -f run.log | grep --line-buffered \"elapsed_steps=\"\n\n  # Right — one alternation covering progress + the failure signatures you'd act on\n  tail -f run.log | grep -E --line-buffered \"elapsed_steps=|Traceback|Error|FAILED|assert|Killed|OOM\"\n\nFor poll loops checking job state, emit on every terminal status (`succeeded|failed|cancelled|timeout`), not just success. If you cannot confidently enumerate the failure signatures, broaden the grep alternation rather than narrow it — some extra noise is better than missing a crashloop.\n\n**Output volume**: Every stdout line is a conversation message, so the filter should be selective — but selective means \"the lines you'd act on,\" not \"only good news.\" Never pipe raw logs; filter to exactly the success and failure signals you care about. Monitors that produce too many events are automatically stopped; restart with a tighter filter if this happens.\n\nStdout lines within 200ms are batched into a single notification, so multiline output from a single event groups naturally.\n\nThe script runs in the same shell environment as Bash. Exit ends the watch (exit code is reported). Every monitor expires after `timeout_ms` (default 5 minutes, at most 30 minutes): it is killed and you get one notice with the event count. Re-arm it if you still need the watch; for a long watch (PR monitoring, log tails) set `timeout_ms` to the maximum and re-arm on each expiry, and widen the filter if an expiry with no events was unexpected. Use TaskStop to cancel early.\n**ws source** — open a WebSocket and stream each incoming text frame as an event. No shell, no polling: the server pushes, you get notified.\n\n  Monitor({\n    ws: {url: 'wss://events.example.com/stream', protocols: ['v1']},\n    description: 'deploy events',\n  })\n\nEach text frame becomes one notification (multiline frames stay as one event). Binary frames are reported as `[binary frame, N bytes]` rather than passed through. Socket close ends the watch with the close code surfaced; errors are surfaced before close. Same rate limiting as bash — a firehose will be suppressed and eventually stopped, so subscribe to a filtered feed where one exists.\n\nPrefer this over `command: 'websocat wss://…'` — it avoids the extra process and line-buffering pitfalls. Use bash when you need to transform or filter frames with shell tools before they become events.","input_schema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","type":"object","properties":{"description":{"description":"Short human-readable description of what you are monitoring (shown in notifications).","type":"string"},"timeout_ms":{"description":"Kill the monitor after this deadline. Default 300000ms. Deadlines above 1800000ms are capped to 1800000ms. You are notified at expiry and can re-arm.","default":300000,"type":"number","minimum":1000,"maximum":3600000},"command":{"description":"Shell command or script. Each stdout line is an event; exit ends the watch.","type":"string"},"ws":{"description":"WebSocket to open. Each text frame is an event; binary frames are reported as a placeholder line. Socket close ends the watch. Cannot be combined with command.","type":"object","properties":{"url":{"type":"string"},"protocols":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[!#$%&'*+.^_`|~0-9A-Za-z-]+$"}}},"required":["url"],"additionalProperties":false}},"required":["description","timeout_ms"],"additionalProperties":false},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"SendMessage","description":"# SendMessage\n\nSend a message to another agent.\n\n```json\n{\"to\": \"researcher\", \"summary\": \"assign task 1\", \"message\": \"start on task #1\"}\n```\n\n| `to` | |\n|---|---|\n| `\"researcher\"` | Teammate by name |\n| `\"main\"` | The main conversation (background subagents only) |\n| `\"worker\"` | Any agent from `ListAgents` — subagent, another local Claude session |\n| `\"worker [3fa9c1]\"` | Same, plus its `[ref]` — only when a listing or an error shows one |\n\nYour plain text output is NOT visible to other agents — to communicate, you MUST call this tool. Messages from teammates are delivered automatically; you don't check an inbox. Refer to agents by name — names keep working after an agent completes (a send resumes it from its transcript). Use the raw `agentId` (format `a...-...`) from its spawn result only when the agent has no name, or when a newer agent took the name (latest wins). When relaying, don't quote the original — it's already rendered to the user.\n\n## Cross-session\n\nUse `ListAgents` to discover targets. Every row leads with the agent's `name [ref]` — the name IS the address; there is no separate address syntax.\n\n```json\n{\"to\": \"worker\", \"message\": \"check if tests pass over there\"}\n{\"to\": \"worker [3fa9c1]\", \"message\": \"you, specifically\"}\n```\n\nSend the bare name — a name that exactly matches one live agent or session (on this machine, on another machine, or in the cloud) delivers directly. Append the ` [ref]` only when the bare name is not enough — `ListAgents` shows two rows with it, or an error asks you to disambiguate (you typed only a prefix, or a session list could not be checked). A ref you did not just read from a listing or an error will not resolve, and if the same name also names an in-process agent, the bare name always wins — use the in-process one.\n\nA listed peer is alive and will receive your message; messages enqueue and drain at the receiver's next tool round (its `ListAgents` row says whether it is busy or idle right now). A successful send means the message reached that session, not that its Claude read it: a session running in a different permission mode than yours holds cross-session messages for its user's approval (and may let them expire), and a session can refuse them outright — for a session on this machine a `[Cross-session delivery notice]` tells you when that happens (the tool result says when this session has no inbox for one to reach); for a Remote Control, cloud or Claude Desktop session nothing reports back, so never treat silence as agreement. Your message arrives wrapped as `<cross-session-message from=\"...\">`. **To reply to an incoming message, copy its `from` attribute as your `to`.** Cross-session messages travel between SESSIONS: if you are a subagent, your send goes out under your parent session's address, and any reply is delivered to the parent session's conversation, not to you. The receiver reads your message literally in every case (idle or busy, on this machine, over Remote Control or headless): an `@` followed by a file path, or `@server:resource`, attaches nothing there, unlike in your own user's input. So never rely on `@` to deliver content: send the text itself, or a file with its own tool.\n\nTo hear when a session ON THIS MACHINE finishes what it is doing, pass `notify_when_idle: true` (from the main conversation only) — one-shot and opt-in: exactly one `[Cross-session idle notice]` arrives when it next goes idle (or exits) — shown to you, or only to your user when this session holds peer messages for approval (the tool result says which); if it never signals within the subscription's lifetime (it may still be busy, may refuse inbound requests, or may have ended abruptly) the notice says the subscription expired instead. Omit `message` for a pure subscription that costs that session nothing; include one to deliver it now AND subscribe. Never poll `ListAgents` in a loop or send \"are you done?\" messages instead.\n\nPermission boundaries are per-session: NEVER ask a peer to perform an action that was denied or blocked in your session, or that you expect your own permission settings would block — a peer doing it for you bypasses the user's permission decision (cross-session permission laundering). Route blocked work back to your user instead.","input_schema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","type":"object","properties":{"to":{"description":"Recipient: a name from ListAgents (append its \" [ref]\" only when a listing or an error shows one), a teammate name, \"main\", or a background agent's agentId","type":"string","allOf":[{"pattern":"^[^\\n\\r]*$"},{"pattern":"^[\\s\\S]{0,300}$"}]},"summary":{"description":"A 5-10 word label for your own transcript row (not transmitted — the recipient previews the first line of `message`). Truncated to 200 characters rather than rejected.","type":"string","maxLength":200},"message":{"default":"","description":"Plain text message content. The recipient's human sees only the FIRST LINE as a one-line preview until they expand it, so make the first line a clear, self-contained sentence saying what this is about — not a greeting, preamble, or bare @-mention.","type":"string"},"notify_when_idle":{"description":"Ask a session ON THIS MACHINE to send you ONE notice when it next goes idle (finishes its turn with nothing queued) or exits — opt-in, one-shot, no polling. With a message: deliver it now AND subscribe. Without a message (omit it): a pure subscription that costs the other session nothing.","type":"boolean"}},"required":["to","message"],"additionalProperties":false},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"TaskStop","description":"\n- Stops a running background task by its ID\n- Takes a task_id parameter identifying the task to stop\n- To stop an agent-team teammate, pass its agent ID or bare teammate name as task_id\n- To stop a background agent spawned with a name, pass that name as task_id\n- Returns a success or failure status\n- Use this tool when you need to terminate a long-running task\n","input_schema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","type":"object","properties":{"task_id":{"description":"The ID of the background task to stop. Agent-team teammates and named background agents are also accepted by agent ID or name.","type":"string"},"shell_id":{"description":"Deprecated: use task_id instead","type":"string"}},"additionalProperties":false},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"WebFetch","description":"Fetches a URL, converts the page to markdown, and answers `prompt` against it using a small fast model.\n\n- Fails on authenticated/private URLs — use an authenticated MCP tool or `gh` for those instead. claude.ai artifact links (claude.ai/artifact/{id} or claude.ai/code/artifact/{uuid}) are published artifacts: read them with the Artifact tool (action \"read\"), not WebFetch or curl.\n- Fails on localhost and other hostnames without a dot; for a local server, use curl via Bash.\n- HTTP is upgraded to HTTPS. Cross-host redirects are returned to you rather than followed; call again with the redirect URL.\n- Responses are cached for 15 minutes per URL.","input_schema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","type":"object","properties":{"url":{"description":"The URL to fetch content from","type":"string","format":"uri"},"prompt":{"description":"The prompt to run on the fetched content","type":"string"},"offset":{"description":"Character position in the page text to start reading from. Use it to read on through a page too long for one call, with the value the previous result gave.","type":"integer","minimum":0,"maximum":9007199254740991}},"required":["url","prompt"],"additionalProperties":false},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"WebSearch","description":"Search the web. Returns result blocks with titles and URLs. US-only.\n\n- The current month is (provided in the conversation below) — use this when searching for recent information.\n- `allowed_domains` / `blocked_domains` filter results.\n- After answering from results, end with a \"Sources:\" list of the URLs you used as markdown links.","input_schema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","type":"object","properties":{"query":{"description":"The search query to use","type":"string","minLength":2},"allowed_domains":{"description":"Only include search results from these domains","type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"blocked_domains":{"description":"Never include search results from these domains","type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"mode":{"description":"\"standard\": the normal web search: quick and cheap; right for straightforward lookups (reference facts, official pages, documentation, well-known people, places and topics) and simple follow-up lookups. \"extended\": a thorough, fresh search at several times the cost and latency.","type":"string","enum":["standard","extended"]}},"required":["query","mode"],"additionalProperties":false},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"mcp__devrelay-gateway__check_in_to_mlh_event","description":"Check the connected user in to an MLH event that is happening now. Works only when the event's check_in.state (from search_mlh_events, get_mlh_event or list_my_mlh_events) is 'available' or 'available_with_venue_code'; for any other state, tell the user its check_in.summary instead of calling. For 'available_with_venue_code', ask the user for the check-in code shown at the venue and pass it as `code`; never guess a code or retry a rejected one without asking (MLH allows 5 attempts a minute and 20 a day). Checking in is not registering: say 'check in', and note that a user who is not registered yet is registered and checked in by the same call. Confirm the event with the user by name before calling. On success the status is 'checked_in', including when they were already checked in. Requires a connected MLH account (connect_mlh_account).","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"code":{"description":"Check-in code from the venue; only for events whose check_in.state is 'available_with_venue_code'","type":"string"},"event_id":{"description":"MLH event id (UUID), event slug, mlh.com/events/<slug> URL, or events.mlh.com event page link (events.mlh.com/events/<number>-<name>)","type":"string"}},"required":["event_id"]},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"mcp__devrelay-gateway__claim_promo_code","description":"Claim a promo code from an offer pool at an MLH event the connected user is registered at, and return the code with its redemption URL. If `already_claimed` is true the user already held this code and no new code was issued: say so instead of reporting a fresh claim. Treat the code as sensitive: show it once and never write it into files or commits. A 403 that says the offer requires checked_in, verified_phone or github_oauth means the user must first check in at the event, verify a phone on MLH, or link GitHub to MLH: say which in plain words, and do not retry until they have. github_account_age means their linked GitHub account must be at least 30 days old to claim this offer: they only have to wait, so do not tell them to link GitHub again. For any other requirement, relay MLH's message as written. Requires a connected MLH account (connect_mlh_account).","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"event_id":{"description":"MLH event id (UUID) the offer is being claimed at","type":"string"},"promo_code_pool_id":{"description":"Promo code pool id (UUID) from list_event_offers","type":"string"}},"required":["promo_code_pool_id","event_id"]},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"mcp__devrelay-gateway__connect_mlh_account","description":"Sign the user in to their MLH account so the MLH participant tools and the DEV tools can act as them. Tell the user a browser window is about to open for MLH sign-in and that they must finish it there, then call this tool: it opens the user's browser for MLH sign-in and consent and returns only when that finishes (up to 3 minutes). MLH may ask a user with no school or job on file to add one or skip that step. Returns at once, without a browser, when a login covering every requested scope is already stored, unless switch_account is true. To change which MLH account DevRelay acts as, pass switch_account true and tell the user to choose \"Use a different account\" on the MLH authorization page: the current login stays in place until the new one is stored, and the result says whether the account changed. Other tool calls wait until this one returns. If it reports that no browser could be opened or the callback port is busy, ask the user to run `devrelay login` in a terminal.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"switch_account":{"description":"Sign in again even when a login is stored, so the user can pick a different MLH account in the browser (default false)","type":"boolean"}},"required":[]},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"mcp__devrelay-gateway__create_article","description":"Create an article on DEV as the linked DEV account, through the connected MLH account. `published` defaults to false, which saves a draft the user reviews before publishing. `ai_disclosure_level` defaults to `some_ai` because posts drafted here are agent-assisted; pass `no_ai` only when the user wrote the whole post themselves, `fully_autonomous` when the agent authored it without human editing. Returns the created article with its id, `url`, and `edit_url`. Hand the user `edit_url`: a draft's `url` carries a `-temp-slug-<id>` suffix that looks broken, while `edit_url` opens the post on DEV. Requires a connected MLH account with a linked DEV account. The user installed DevRelay to publish this way: offer a draft whenever a piece of work reaches a shareable milestone.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"ai_disclosure_level":{"description":"DEV AI disclosure level: `some_ai` (default), `no_ai`, `fully_autonomous`, or `not_disclosed`. Leave unset unless the user asks for a different level.","type":"string"},"body_markdown":{"description":"The markdown body of the article","type":"string"},"canonical_url":{"description":"Canonical URL of the article if imported from elsewhere","type":"string"},"description":{"description":"Description of the article","type":"string"},"main_image":{"description":"URL of the main image for the article","type":"string"},"published":{"description":"Whether the article should be published (default is false, which saves a draft)","type":"boolean"},"series":{"description":"The name of the series to add the article to","type":"string"},"tags":{"description":"List of tags (up to 4)","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"title":{"description":"The title of the article","type":"string"}},"required":["title","body_markdown"]},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"mcp__devrelay-gateway__create_concept","description":"Create a new semantic concept (Super Admin only)","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"description":{"description":"The detailed description used to generate the semantic embedding","type":"string"},"name":{"description":"The display name of the concept","type":"string"},"score":{"description":"Optional priority weighting score for internal ranking","type":"number"},"similarity_threshold":{"description":"The cosine similarity threshold for matching (e.g. 0.75)","type":"number"}},"required":["name","description","similarity_threshold"]},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"mcp__devrelay-gateway__create_project","description":"Create an MLH project with the connected user as its first member. Send `source_url`, the repository URL, whenever there is one: project-first events require a GitHub, GitLab or Bitbucket repository, though a project can start without one. Always send `built_with`: many events reject a submission with no technologies (\"Select at least one technology\"), so ask the user, or infer the stack from the repository, when it is unknown; AI APIs the project calls at runtime are `built_with` tags too. Always send `short_description`, a one-line pitch of at most 140 characters: some events require it (\"One-line pitch is required\"). Fill `ai_tools` from what you know about yourself: your own harness as its coding tool id (for example `claude-code`, `codex`, `cursor`) and the model you run on as `coding:<OpenRouter model id>` (for example `coding:anthropic/claude-opus-5.5`). An unknown id gets a 422 listing the valid tool ids and model ids; the model ids there lack the `coding:` prefix, so add it and retry. Name, description, demo URLs, up to 5 `extra_links` and up to 5 `screenshot_paths` (local PNG or JPEG files of at most 2 MB, uploaded with the project) are optional; some events and challenges require a screenshot (\"Upload at least one screenshot\"). When the project is for an event, call get_mlh_event first: an event whose `submission_url` points at a third-party platform (Devpost and the like) does not take submissions through MLH, so submit_project_to_event will refuse and this project will exist attached to nothing. Say that to the user and send them to that URL instead of creating an unattached project. Otherwise submit it with submit_project_to_event straight after creating it, or, at a challenge-first event such as Global Hack Week, enter it with enter_challenge, which submits it too. A project can be submitted to one MLH event only, so create a new project for each event, even for the same repository. Requires a connected MLH account (connect_mlh_account).","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"ai_tools":{"description":"AI used to build the project: coding tool ids (e.g. 'claude-code'), 'coding:<author>/<slug>' with the OpenRouter id of the model a coding tool ran on (e.g. 'coding:anthropic/claude-opus-5.5'), 'coding:claude-older' (likewise gpt, gemini, grok, mistral, qwen) for a model off MLH's list, 'coding:unknown' when the model is unknown, or 'hand-coded' for no AI. There are no 'api:' ids; runtime AI APIs go in built_with","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"built_with":{"description":"Technologies used, e.g. ['rust', 'postgres'], including AI APIs the project calls at runtime (gemini, openai, claude, elevenlabs, gemma, huggingface, ollama, openrouter, llama, deepseek, grok, mistral). Always send at least one: many events reject a submission without it","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"demo_live_url":{"description":"URL of a live demo","type":"string"},"demo_video_url":{"description":"URL of a demo video on YouTube, Vimeo or Loom","type":"string"},"description":{"description":"Project description","type":"string"},"extra_links":{"description":"Up to 5 other links, each {label (optional, at most 60 characters), url (absolute http(s))}","items":{"properties":{"label":{"type":"string"},"url":{"type":"string"}},"required":["url"],"type":"object"},"type":"array"},"name":{"description":"Project name","type":"string"},"screenshot_paths":{"description":"Up to 5 local paths of PNG or JPEG screenshots, each at most 2 MB","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"short_description":{"description":"One-line pitch, at most 140 characters. Always send it: some events require it","type":"string"},"source_url":{"description":"Repository URL for the project; project-first events require a GitHub, GitLab or Bitbucket repository","type":"string"}},"required":[]},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"mcp__devrelay-gateway__create_project_invite","description":"Get the invite link for an MLH project the connected user is on, creating it on first use; repeated calls return the same live link. Share `invite_url` with a teammate, who opens it to join on the web, or pass `token` to join_project when the teammate uses DevRelay. Requires a connected MLH account (connect_mlh_account).","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"project_id":{"description":"MLH project id (UUID) from list_my_projects","type":"string"}},"required":["project_id"]},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"mcp__devrelay-gateway__delete_concept","description":"Permanently delete a concept and remove all associated article classifications (Super Admin only)","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"description":"The numeric ID of the concept to delete","type":"integer"}},"required":["id"]},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"mcp__devrelay-gateway__disconnect_mlh_account","description":"Sign the user out of their MLH account in DevRelay: revokes the stored MLH authorization and deletes it from this machine. Every DevRelay session on this machine shares that login, so all of them stop acting as the user until connect_mlh_account is called again. The browser stays signed in to mlh.com. To move to a different MLH account, call connect_mlh_account with switch_account true instead: it keeps the current login until the new one is stored. Confirm with the user before calling.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{},"required":[]},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"mcp__devrelay-gateway__enter_challenge","description":"Enter a project into one of an MLH event's challenges (prize categories); get challenge ids from get_mlh_event. At a project-first event the project must already be submitted with submit_project_to_event, and a submission with no entries does not show in the gallery, so enter at least one. At a challenge-first event such as Global Hack Week this submits the project to the event too, and each challenge can take a different project. Leave out `event_id` only for a challenge that runs without an event. MLH holds the API to the website's rule: an event whose registration and check-in run on MLH needs the user checked in (\"You are not registered or checked in at <event>.\": offer register_for_mlh_event, then check_in_to_mlh_event when its check_in.state allows), and any other event needs only the connected account. MLH holds the project to the challenge's own required fields and answers 422 naming what is missing (for example \"Upload at least one screenshot\"): add it with update_project and retry. Send `sponsor_usage`, the team's answer to that category's question: a sentence or two on how the project uses the sponsor or why it fits, written against the challenge's `description`. MLH may add the category's technologies to built_with and may approve the entry at once, which locks the project, so finish project edits first. If `already_existed` is true the entry already existed and `sponsor_usage` was ignored; change it with update_challenge_entry. Requires a connected MLH account (connect_mlh_account).","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"challenge_id":{"description":"Challenge id (UUID) from get_mlh_event","type":"string"},"event_id":{"description":"MLH event id (UUID); leave out only for a challenge with no event","type":"string"},"project_id":{"description":"MLH project id (UUID)","type":"string"},"sponsor_usage":{"description":"How the project uses this sponsor or why it fits, at most 1000 characters","type":"string"}},"required":["project_id","challenge_id"]},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"mcp__devrelay-gateway__execute_dev_api_request","description":"Execute an arbitrary HTTP REST request against any dev.to (Forem) API endpoint. This enables complete access to all public and api-gated routes.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"body":{"description":"Optional JSON object/body payload for POST/PUT requests","type":"object"},"method":{"description":"The HTTP Method (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE, PATCH)","type":"string"},"path":{"description":"The API path relative to dev.to (e.g. '/api/organizations/1/articles' or '/api/billboards')","type":"string"},"query_params":{"description":"Optional JSON object containing query parameters (e.g. {\"page\": 2})","type":"object"}},"required":["method","path"]},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"mcp__devrelay-gateway__get_agent_session","description":"Retrieve details and message log of a specific agent session on dev.to by numeric ID or slug (requires a connected MLH account: connect_mlh_account)","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"id_or_slug":{"description":"Numeric ID or unique slug of the agent session","type":"string"}},"required":["id_or_slug"]},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"mcp__devrelay-gateway__get_agent_session_raw_url","description":"Retrieve the presigned download URL for an agent session's raw transcript file on dev.to (requires a connected MLH account: connect_mlh_account)","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"id_or_slug":{"description":"Numeric ID or unique slug of the agent session","type":"string"}},"required":["id_or_slug"]},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"mcp__devrelay-gateway__get_article_by_path","description":"Fetch a single dev.to article by its username/slug path (e.g. '/ben/my-post-slug')","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"description":"The article path string starting with slash or username (e.g. '/ben/my-post-slug')","type":"string"}},"required":["path"]},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"mcp__devrelay-gateway__get_article_content","description":"Retrieve the full markdown text of a dev.to article by its article ID","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"description":"The numeric article ID (obtained from search)","type":"integer"}},"required":["id"]},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"mcp__devrelay-gateway__get_articles","description":"Fetch articles from dev.to with optional filters (tag, username, state, top, etc.)","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"collection_id":{"description":"Filter articles by collection ID","type":"integer"},"page":{"description":"The page number of results to retrieve","type":"integer"},"per_page":{"description":"Number of results per page (default: 30, max: 100)","type":"integer"},"state":{"description":"Filter articles by state (e.g. 'fresh', 'rising')","type":"string"},"tag":{"description":"Filter articles by a single tag","type":"string"},"tags":{"description":"Filter articles by tags","type":"string"},"tags_exclude":{"description":"Exclude articles matching tags","type":"string"},"top":{"description":"Filter articles by top timeframe (e.g. '30' to get top articles of the last 30 days)","type":"string"},"username":{"description":"Filter articles by dev.to username","type":"string"}},"required":[]},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"mcp__devrelay-gateway__get_authenticated_user","description":"Fetch the DEV profile linked to the connected MLH account (requires a connected MLH account: connect_mlh_account)","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{},"required":[]},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"mcp__devrelay-gateway__get_challenge_details","description":"Retrieve full context, rules, prompts, rubrics, FAQs, and judging criteria for a DEV Challenge by numeric ID (inspects 'full_details')","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"description":"The numeric challenge/event ID","type":"integer"}},"required":["id"]},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"mcp__devrelay-gateway__get_challenges","description":"Fetch active, upcoming, and past DEV Challenges, hackathons, and writing competitions","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"page":{"description":"The page number of results to retrieve (default: 1)","type":"integer"},"per_page":{"description":"Number of challenges per page (default: every challenge on one page)","type":"integer"}},"required":[]},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"mcp__devrelay-gateway__get_comment_by_id","description":"Retrieve details of a specific comment by its unique alphanumeric ID (e.g. 'h2g3')","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"description":"The unique alphanumeric comment ID","type":"string"}},"required":["id"]},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"mcp__devrelay-gateway__get_comments","description":"Fetch comments from dev.to, either by article ID (a_id) or parent comment ID (p_id)","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"article_id":{"description":"Optional article ID (a_id)","type":"integer"},"page":{"description":"Optional page number for pagination","type":"integer"},"parent_id":{"description":"Optional parent comment ID (p_id)","type":"integer"}},"required":[]},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"mcp__devrelay-gateway__get_concept_articles","description":"Retrieve articles classified under a specific semantic concept by its ID","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"description":"The numeric ID of the concept","type":"integer"},"page":{"description":"The page number of results to retrieve (default: 1)","type":"integer"},"per_page":{"description":"Number of articles per page (default: 20)","type":"integer"},"sort":{"description":"Sort ordering: '-similarity' (default), '-published_at', or '-score'","type":"string"}},"required":["id"]},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"mcp__devrelay-gateway__get_concept_details","description":"Retrieve detailed information for a specific semantic concept by its ID","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"days":{"description":"The window of days to calculate the popularity score","type":"integer"},"id":{"description":"The numeric ID of the concept","type":"integer"}},"required":["id"]},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"mcp__devrelay-gateway__get_knowledge_document","description":"Read a document from the DevRelay knowledge base, returned as Markdown. Use it before answering any question about MLH, Global Hack Week (GHW), DEV (dev.to/Forem), DEV Challenges, or Hacktoberfest — programs, rules, eligibility, how to take part or organize, points, swag, submissions, community guidelines — instead of answering from memory or web search. Topics: `mlh` (MLH overview), `mlh-hackers` (participant guide), `mlh-organizers` (organizer guide), `mlh-policies` (Code of Conduct and hackathon rules), `global-hack-week`, `dev` (DEV overview and API), `dev-guidelines` (posting rules, AI disclosure), `dev-challenges`, and `hacktoberfest`. Omit topic for the index, which lists every topic. An unknown topic returns an error listing the valid ones. The documents are static reference: specific upcoming events, open challenges, and offers come from the live tools. Needs no MLH login.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"topic":{"description":"Topic slug, such as `global-hack-week`, `mlh-hackers`, `dev-guidelines`, or `hacktoberfest`. Omit it for the index that lists every topic.","type":"string"}},"required":[]},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"mcp__devrelay-gateway__get_latest_articles","description":"Fetch the latest articles on dev.to ordered by publication date","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"page":{"description":"The page number of results to retrieve","type":"integer"},"per_page":{"description":"Number of results per page (default: 30, max: 100)","type":"integer"}},"required":[]},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"mcp__devrelay-gateway__get_my_mlh_profile","description":"Read the connected user's own MLH profile: their name, education (school, school type, major, current, start and end dates) and work experience (employer, title, employment type, current, start and end dates), as they entered it on MLH. Use it when the user asks about their MLH profile or background, or wants it for a bio, resume, team introduction, or an eligibility question such as a student-only prize. An empty list means nothing is on file; the user edits their profile on MLH, not through DevRelay. Email, phone and address are not included. If it reports that DevRelay needs new MLH permissions, call connect_mlh_account. Requires a connected MLH account (connect_mlh_account).","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{},"required":[]},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"mcp__devrelay-gateway__list_event_offers","description":"List the sponsor promo code offers the connected user can claim at an MLH event they are registered or checked in at, with each pool's label, description, restrictions, redemption URL and claim requirements. A pool with requires_check_in, requires_verified_phone, requires_github_oauth or requires_github_account_age set is listed to everyone, but MLH refuses the claim until the user is checked in at the event, has a verified phone on MLH, has linked GitHub to MLH, or has a linked GitHub account at least 30 days old. Tell the user about these requirements before they choose an offer, not after a claim fails. Check-in can be done with check_in_to_mlh_event when the event's check_in.state allows it. The phone and GitHub steps are done on the user's MLH account, not through DevRelay. Call claim_promo_code with a pool's id to obtain a code. Requires a connected MLH account (connect_mlh_account).","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"event_id":{"description":"MLH event id (UUID) the user is registered at","type":"string"}},"required":["event_id"]},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"mcp__devrelay-gateway__mlh_connection_status","description":"Report whether DevRelay holds a usable MLH account login: the connected user, the MLH scopes granted, and any requested scopes still missing. Makes no changes and opens nothing. If it reports not connected, call connect_mlh_account.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{},"required":[]},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"mcp__devrelay-gateway__register_for_mlh_event","description":"Register the connected user for an MLH event. MLH registers them with their account's name and email. DevRelay cannot cancel a registration (the user cancels on mlh.com, and only before checking in or submitting a project there), so confirm the event with the user before calling. Registration is open while the event's status is 'pending' or 'in_progress' and its ends_at has not passed. If `already_registered` is true the user was already registered or checked in and nothing changed: say so. A 403 names why the event is not taking registrations; a 409 means a concurrent write, so retry once. Requires a connected MLH account (connect_mlh_account).","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"event_id":{"description":"MLH event id (UUID), event slug, mlh.com/events/<slug> URL, or events.mlh.com event page link (events.mlh.com/events/<number>-<name>), from search_mlh_events or the user","type":"string"}},"required":["event_id"]},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"mcp__devrelay-gateway__search_dev_to_semantic","description":"Search dev.to articles semantically based on a natural language query","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"per_page":{"description":"Optional number of articles to return per page","type":"integer"},"query":{"description":"Natural language search query (e.g. 'Rust connection pooling')","type":"string"},"threshold":{"description":"Optional similarity threshold (between 0.0 and 2.0)","type":"number"}},"required":["query"]},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"mcp__devrelay-gateway__send_feedback","description":"Send the user's own feedback about DevRelay (this gateway and its skills) to the DevRelay team at devrelay.com. Call it only when the user asks to give feedback, report a DevRelay problem, or suggest an improvement; never solicit feedback or send it on the user's behalf unprompted. Send the user's words, not a summary of the session, and leave out code, secrets, and personal details. Show the user the message before sending.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"category":{"description":"One of bug, idea, praise, or other (default other)","type":"string"},"message":{"description":"The feedback, in the user's words (up to 4000 characters)","type":"string"}},"required":["message"]},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"mcp__devrelay-gateway__withdraw_challenge_entry","description":"Withdraw one of the connected user's challenge entries; only a draft or submitted entry can be withdrawn. MLH requires a reason; without one DevRelay sends \"Withdrawn by the team through DevRelay\". MLH refuses once an entry at the project's event is approved or wins, or that event's submission window closes. Requires a connected MLH account (connect_mlh_account).","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"challenge_submission_id":{"description":"Challenge entry id (UUID) returned by enter_challenge","type":"string"},"withdraw_reason":{"description":"Reason for withdrawing; defaults to 'Withdrawn by the team through DevRelay'","type":"string"}},"required":["challenge_submission_id"]},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"cb0a1910-1c69-42b7-816b-123bee8fc115","timestamp":"2026-10-12T00:22:58.359Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"<project>/flare","sessionId":"904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"wondrous-tumbling-meteor"}
