a real Flare by WhatsApp and opened it in Brave on an iPhone. The invite (apps/web/src/lib/screens/I1Invite.svelte) had a dim indoor photo, but only the top third of the screen showed the photo. The six-word headline sat right on it and the sheet covered the rest, so you couldn't see the place, which is the whole point of the photo. The send screens H2Develop.svelte and H3Send.svelte, and the shared apps/web/src/lib/components/PhotoPrint.svelte, have the same problem. No test caught it: every test used bright daylight photos on a full Safari viewport.\n\nFIXES\n1. The photo is the content. Text and the sheet never cover the main part of the image.\n   - Show the photo at its natural aspect ratio in the top area. Cap its height sensibly so the main action (I'm in / Send) still fits on a 375x667 screen without scrolling, or with at most a small scroll.\n   - Put the six words below the photo, or on a short gradient band at the photo's bottom edge only.\n   - The sheet starts collapsed below the photo.\n   - Tapping the photo opens it full screen. Use an accessible dialog with a 44 px close button, Escape closes it, and focus returns to the photo.\n   - Apply the same rule on H2Develop and H3Send.\n2. Dark photos. On the phone, draw the decoded photo onto a tiny canvas (for example 32x32) and measure its average luminance. If it's dark, for example a mean below ~0.35, brighten it FOR DISPLAY ONLY with a CSS filter, for example brightness(1.35) contrast(1.05), scaled to how dark it is. Never touch the sealed or uploaded photo bytes. Photos are blob or object URLs, so the canvas is same-origin. Guard against tainted canvases with try/catch. Put the logic in a small pure module with a unit test (vitest, like apps/web/test/flow/*.test.ts).\n3. The \"Your yes is private\" chip (find it with grep in the deck and the screens): make it a single line at 375 px. Once someone closes it, it stays closed: store that in localStorage with a try/catch.\n4. New gates, so the bug can't come back. Add a Playwright e2e script like the others in apps/web/test/e2e/ (look at how demo.ts or telegram.ts start the stack, and add an npm script e2e:photo-fit in the root package.json).\n   - Test photos: a real dark indoor photo and a tall portrait photo. Look in the repo first (docs/credits/photos.md, apps/web/static, test fixtures). If there is no real indoor photo, make a dark version of a real public-domain photo that is already in the repo (with sharp or a canvas), label it honestly in the test as \"darkened real photo\", and say so in your report. Do NOT download anything from the internet.\n   - Viewports: 390x664 (Brave or a WhatsApp in-app browser with a bottom bar), 375x667 (iPhone SE), and the current ones (390x844).\n   - Overlap check: at first paint, compute the photo's bounding rect and the rects of every text element and of the sheet. Fail if their union covers more than 25% of the photo's area.\n   - Run it on I1Invite (the friend's link page), H2Develop and H3Send.\n   - Also check that the dark photo gets the display filter and that the stored or sent photo is unchanged.\n   - Save before and after screenshots at 390x664 for invite, develop and send to docs/frontend/evidence/photo-fit/ (before = run the check on main's build first, after = yours).\n\nRULES\n- Writing rules for any copy: plain words, a number for every claim, no em dashes, buttons ≤3 words, UI messages ≤12 words, no \"just\". Banned words: seamless, leverage, robust, empower, unlock, elevate, delve, cutting-edge, revolutionize, game-changer, harness, synergy, holistic, paradigm, next-level, supercharge, effortless, ecosystem, tapestry, testament.\n- Copy changes go through the deck JSON plus the md mirror. `node design/prototype/scripts/copy-lint.mjs` must report 0 problems.\n- Don't change these strings: cond.didntCatch, compass.disclaimer, app.tier.hub, and anything about \"Made on our laptop\".\n- Do NOT touch the invite.where, invite.whereWalk, lit.notice, push.lit or sms.lit templates, or the spot-naming code in host.svelte.ts. The lead is fixing \"is at Near X\" grammar there.\n- Do NOT touch lab/, .env, or the untracked apps/web/static/scenic/ or the -640/-1280 files in apps/web/static/scenery/. Never stage them; use explicit git add paths.\n- Never print secrets. .env is at <project>/flare/.env if the e2e needs it; read it only through the existing scripts.\n- Another subagent (app-motion) is adding motion to the app on its own branch. Keep your edits to layout. Don't redo animations.\n- Gates you must pass and report numbers for:\n  - `cd apps/web && npx svelte-check --threshold warning`: 0/0\n  - `npm run lint`\n  - `npm test`\n  - copy-lint 0\n  - the existing e2e suites that cover these screens: at least demo, sparks, telegram and loop (see package.json)\n  - axe 0 (whatever script the repo uses, e.g. the kit a11y e2e)\n  - JS budget: /app and /g/ under 150 KB (the repo has a budget script; /app was 147.5 KB, so keep the additions tiny and lazy-load the full-screen viewer if needed)\n  - Respect prefers-reduced-motion.\n\nREPORT (short): commit hash(es), files changed, the overlap % per screen and viewport before and after, the gate results with numbers, the screenshot paths, and anything you couldn't do. Target: done within about 75 minutes. If time runs short, ship fixes 1 to 3 plus the overlap gate first.","outputFile":"<tmp>/904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa/tasks/a3799e92ab8ab5a63.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"14c2cdb3-ed87-4bb4-8914-7e8d6ca0f90e","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"<project>/flare","root":"<project>/flare","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":28,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":5},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/flare","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com"