{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-12T00:26:28.406Z","sessionId":"904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa","content":"<cross-session-message from=\"uds:<socket>\" from-session=\"local_beb3cc8c-e162-46cc-bd0a-f870e8717ebd\" from-name=\"Flare Manager(founders CTO)\" from-mode=\"prompting\">\nLive bugs 3 and 4 from the same real Flare. Real people found them, so all live bugs come before the automations; cut automations if needed.\n\nBug 3, conditions. The friend's second try was \"10min only with you\", and the result was \"I didn't catch that. Try 'after 2' or 'only with Amor'.\"\n- \"10min\" again. This is covered by bug 2's fix; make sure the no-space forms work inside longer sentences.\n- \"with you\" / \"only with you\" / \"if you're there\" / \"you and me\" / \"only if you come\" mean \"only with the host\". The friend is talking to Fuego.\n- The hint examples are wrong for the moment:\n  - \"after 2\" at 8:24 PM makes no sense. Build examples from the time of day, like \"in 10 min\" or \"after 9\".\n  - \"only with Amor\" may be the reader's own name. Never use the reader's own name; use the host's.\n- The bigger fix: when parsing fails or only partly works, don't stop at an error. Show 3–4 tappable chips built from what it did catch, plus common ones, like \"Come in 10 min\", \"Only if Fuego's there\", \"After 9 PM\", \"15 min max\". One tap fills the rule. Lazy friends shouldn't have to type twice.\n- Add both of the friend's sentences to hard_20, and keep blind_40 with no regression.\n\nBug 4, the WhatsApp share didn't open. The founder tapped share in Brave on an iPhone, and WhatsApp never opened. The founder may have only WhatsApp Business; the first screenshot's back button said \"WA Business\".\n- Check every share path: navigator.share, any whatsapp:// link and any wa.me link.\n- Make the share sheet (navigator.share) the main path, so WA Business, iMessage and Telegram all show up.\n- Any direct WhatsApp button must be a real <a href=\"https://wa.me/?text=…\"> tapped by the user, not a window.open from script. If the page is still visible after 1.5 s, fall back to the share sheet and a \"Copy link\" button with a toast.\n- Test in Safari and Brave on iOS 17/18, with WhatsApp and with WhatsApp Business only, and write down what you could and couldn't test. If you can't test a combination, say so. Don't claim it.\n\nSend me one status line per fix when it's live.\n</cross-session-message>"}
