{"parentUuid":"2167ad75-2f8f-46fb-b0e4-f6d1c90f7974","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>11020053 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"5f3a0913-8846-4801-accb-1220592e6df8","timestamp":"2026-10-12T00:26:51.056Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>11020053 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"<project>/flare","sessionId":"904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"wondrous-tumbling-meteor"}
{"parentUuid":"5f3a0913-8846-4801-accb-1220592e6df8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwPpzJokUteWLcfUTD39","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5642,"cache_read_input_tokens":110329,"output_tokens":1871,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":156},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5642,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1871,"cache_read_input_tokens":110329,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5642,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5642},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":1794,"serverClassifierRequest":"bd212b19-4a84-4620-9998-0d4c3fa1f8a9","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfwPpyLGPKZ8mkPm3MbKb","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c7b782a0-3f1f-421a-ba1b-2e417cd5779e","timestamp":"2026-10-12T00:26:54.400Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"<project>/flare","sessionId":"904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"wondrous-tumbling-meteor"}
{"parentUuid":"c7b782a0-3f1f-421a-ba1b-2e417cd5779e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwPpzJokUteWLcfUTD39","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FxQTyYms2DriZdazYfWMWu","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Fix WhatsApp share live bug","isolation":"worktree","run_in_background":true,"prompt":"You are the frontend engineer fixing a LIVE bug in Flare. Flare is a SvelteKit/Svelte 5 PWA in an npm-workspaces monorepo; the web app is apps/web, and the copy deck is design/prototype/src/lib/copy/deck.json, mirrored in docs/content/02-copy-deck.md. You are in a git worktree branched from main. Commit on your branch. Do NOT push, deploy or merge; the lead merges.\n\nTHE BUG\nThe founder lit a real Flare in Brave on an iPhone and tapped share, and WhatsApp never opened. The founder may have only WhatsApp Business installed (the back button said \"WA Business\").\n\nFIX\n1. Audit every share path in apps/web/src (git grep -n \"navigator.share\\|wa.me\\|whatsapp:\\|window.open\\|share(\" apps/web/src). That includes the host's share after Send (flow.share() in apps/web/src/lib/screens/flow/host.svelte.ts and HostPage.svelte), \"Tell the chat\" on Lit, and any friend-side share. List them in your report.\n2. Make navigator.share the main path, so WA Business, iMessage and Telegram all appear in the sheet.\n   - Call it directly inside the user's tap handler. Make sure no await (no fetch, no image building) runs before it, because iOS drops the user activation.\n   - If you need to prepare a file or a card image, do it ahead of time.\n   - Handle AbortError quietly.\n3. If there is a direct WhatsApp button, it must be a real <a href=\"https://wa.me/?text=...\"> that the user taps, never window.open from script, and never whatsapp://.\n   - After the tap, if the page is still visible 1.5 s later (document.visibilityState === \"visible\"), fall back: open the share sheet if it's available, otherwise show a \"Copy link\" button that copies with navigator.clipboard and shows a short toast.\n4. Everywhere: when navigator.share is missing or throws (other than AbortError), show \"Copy link\" with a toast. Look for existing copy keys first.\n5. Tests:\n   - A unit or flow test for the fallback logic.\n   - An e2e check with Playwright in the style of apps/web/test/e2e/telegram.ts. Stub navigator.share in an init script. Assert that share is called synchronously from the click, before any network request. Assert that with share missing, \"Copy link\" appears and writes to the clipboard. Assert that any WhatsApp control is an <a> with an https://wa.me href.\n   - Run with WebKit too if Playwright's webkit is installed (npx playwright install webkit is pre-approved as an npm-level install). Report whether it ran.\n6. Write docs/frontend/evidence/share-matrix.md. It is a table of Safari and Brave on iOS 17/18, with WhatsApp and with WhatsApp Business only, and says honestly for each cell what you tested (for example Playwright WebKit with a stub) and what you could NOT test on a real device. Never claim a combination you didn't run.\n\nRULES\n- Copy: plain words, buttons ≤3 words, UI messages ≤12 words, no em dashes, no \"just\". `node design/prototype/scripts/copy-lint.mjs` must report 0 problems.\n- Banned words: seamless, leverage, robust, empower, unlock, elevate, delve, cutting-edge, revolutionize, game-changer, harness, synergy, holistic, paradigm, next-level, supercharge, effortless, ecosystem, tapestry, testament.\n- Don't touch I1Invite.svelte, H2Develop.svelte, H3Send.svelte or PhotoPrint.svelte (another worker owns their layout). Don't touch apps/web/src/lib/conditions/ or I2/I3 (the lead is working there).\n- Keep your edits in host.svelte.ts small and limited to share().\n- Do NOT touch lab/, .env, apps/web/static/scenic/, or the -640/-1280 files in apps/web/static/scenery/. Use explicit git add paths.\n- JS budget: /app and /g/ are near 150 KB (another branch brings them to 149.5), so add as little code as you can, ideally under 0.3 KB gzip. Report the delta from the repo's budget script.\n- Gates to pass:\n  - `cd apps/web && npx svelte-check --threshold warning`: 0/0\n  - `npm run lint`\n  - `npm test`\n  - copy-lint 0\n  - the e2e suites telegram, demo and loop\n  - axe 0\n\nREPORT, short: the commit hash, the share paths found and what changed in each, test results with numbers, the matrix file, and what you could not test. Aim to finish in about 45 minutes."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5642,"cache_read_input_tokens":110329,"output_tokens":1871,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":156},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5642,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1871,"cache_read_input_tokens":110329,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5642,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5642},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01FxQTyYms2DriZdazYfWMWu":{"description":"Fix WhatsApp share live bug","isolation":"worktree","run_in_background":true,"prompt":"You are the frontend engineer fixing a LIVE bug in Flare. Flare is a SvelteKit/Svelte 5 PWA in an npm-workspaces monorepo; the web app is apps/web, and the copy deck is design/prototype/src/lib/copy/deck.json, mirrored in docs/content/02-copy-deck.md. You are in a git worktree branched from main. Commit on your branch. Do NOT push, deploy or merge; the lead merges.\n\nTHE BUG\nThe founder lit a real Flare in Brave on an iPhone and tapped share, and WhatsApp never opened. The founder may have only WhatsApp Business installed (the back button said \"WA Business\").\n\nFIX\n1. Audit every share path in apps/web/src (git grep -n \"navigator.share\\|wa.me\\|whatsapp:\\|window.open\\|share(\" apps/web/src). That includes the host's share after Send (flow.share() in apps/web/src/lib/screens/flow/host.svelte.ts and HostPage.svelte), \"Tell the chat\" on Lit, and any friend-side share. List them in your report.\n2. Make navigator.share the main path, so WA Business, iMessage and Telegram all appear in the sheet.\n   - Call it directly inside the user's tap handler. Make sure no await (no fetch, no image building) runs before it, because iOS drops the user activation.\n   - If you need to prepare a file or a card image, do it ahead of time.\n   - Handle AbortError quietly.\n3. If there is a direct WhatsApp button, it must be a real <a href=\"https://wa.me/?text=...\"> that the user taps, never window.open from script, and never whatsapp://.\n   - After the tap, if the page is still visible 1.5 s later (document.visibilityState === \"visible\"), fall back: open the share sheet if it's available, otherwise show a \"Copy link\" button that copies with navigator.clipboard and shows a short toast.\n4. Everywhere: when navigator.share is missing or throws (other than AbortError), show \"Copy link\" with a toast. Look for existing copy keys first.\n5. Tests:\n   - A unit or flow test for the fallback logic.\n   - An e2e check with Playwright in the style of apps/web/test/e2e/telegram.ts. Stub navigator.share in an init script. Assert that share is called synchronously from the click, before any network request. Assert that with share missing, \"Copy link\" appears and writes to the clipboard. Assert that any WhatsApp control is an <a> with an https://wa.me href.\n   - Run with WebKit too if Playwright's webkit is installed (npx playwright install webkit is pre-approved as an npm-level install). Report whether it ran.\n6. Write docs/frontend/evidence/share-matrix.md. It is a table of Safari and Brave on iOS 17/18, with WhatsApp and with WhatsApp Business only, and says honestly for each cell what you tested (for example Playwright WebKit with a stub) and what you could NOT test on a real device. Never claim a combination you didn't run.\n\nRULES\n- Copy: plain words, buttons ≤3 words, UI messages ≤12 words, no em dashes, no \"just\". `node design/prototype/scripts/copy-lint.mjs` must report 0 problems.\n- Banned words: seamless, leverage, robust, empower, unlock, elevate, delve, cutting-edge, revolutionize, game-changer, harness, synergy, holistic, paradigm, next-level, supercharge, effortless, ecosystem, tapestry, testament.\n- Don't touch I1Invite.svelte, H2Develop.svelte, H3Send.svelte or PhotoPrint.svelte (another worker owns their layout). Don't touch apps/web/src/lib/conditions/ or I2/I3 (the lead is working there).\n- Keep your edits in host.svelte.ts small and limited to share().\n- Do NOT touch lab/, .env, apps/web/static/scenic/, or the -640/-1280 files in apps/web/static/scenery/. Use explicit git add paths.\n- JS budget: /app and /g/ are near 150 KB (another branch brings them to 149.5), so add as little code as you can, ideally under 0.3 KB gzip. Report the delta from the repo's budget script.\n- Gates to pass:\n  - `cd apps/web && npx svelte-check --threshold warning`: 0/0\n  - `npm run lint`\n  - `npm test`\n  - copy-lint 0\n  - the e2e suites telegram, demo and loop\n  - axe 0\n\nREPORT, short: the commit hash, the share paths found and what changed in each, test results with numbers, the matrix file, and what you could not test. Aim to finish in about 45 minutes."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"bd212b19-4a84-4620-9998-0d4c3fa1f8a9","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfwPpyLGPKZ8mkPm3MbKb","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"66682497-18da-4dfa-a06a-d99359749348","timestamp":"2026-10-12T00:27:09.211Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint