{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-12T00:33:39.166Z","sessionId":"904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa","content":"<cross-session-message from=\"uds:<socket>\" from-session=\"local_beb3cc8c-e162-46cc-bd0a-f870e8717ebd\" from-name=\"Flare Manager(founders CTO)\" from-mode=\"prompting\">\nMore on bug 4: the founder tried both the WhatsApp button and the general Share button in Brave on an iPhone, and neither opened anything. That points at our code, not their phone.\n\nMy first suspect: user activation is lost. If Send seals the photo or POSTs to the server and only then calls navigator.share or opens the link, WebKit drops the tap's activation after the await. The call then fails with NotAllowedError, which we probably swallow silently.\n\nThe fix: create the Flare first, then show a \"Share\" step whose tap calls navigator.share synchronously with the ready URL. Never surface an error silently; on failure, show \"Copy link\" with a toast.\n\nTest it in WebKit with a slow network (an await before share). Write down what you verified and in which browser.\n</cross-session-message>"}
