{"parentUuid":"2a45627c-15a9-407c-8586-af30e17916f9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwQSnhovAV57vWvt8Jed","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012iZdscYD5H2kVL3iudZjps","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"<project>/flare\" && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='docs/handoffs/RESUME.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nnew='''# Resume note\n\n## Now: Sun 2026-10-11, ~9:15 PM ET, usage-limit pause (resets 9:50 PM ET). Read this first.\nFreeze 1:00 AM ET. Deadline Mon 06:59 UTC. Order: live bugs 1 to 4, then site clarity, then the rest.\n\n**Main (live, deploy started for 2751410 + format fix):**\n- 7792e2c Automations: Again on Home (last crew size, no photo, place words), Telegram-linked Send posts directly with no share sheet, auto I'm here within 30 m on 2 good fixes with a 10 s Undo.\n- 2751410 Live bugs 2 and 3, conditions:\n  - \"10min\" and the other delay phrasings are read as a delay;\n  - a bare hour picks the next one coming;\n  - \"with you\" means the host;\n  - missed words are said back (\"I didn't catch: ...\");\n  - tap-to-fill chips from the time of day and the host;\n  - cond.didntCatchNow replaces the fixed hint on screen. cond.didntCatch (SRS-COND-8) is unchanged and is still what parseError returns.\n  - Tests: apps/web/test/ai/conditions-live.test.ts, 10 tests including a fast-check property. blind_40 30/40 before and after; core 40/40, hard_20 20/20, fresh 40/40 (ml/tinker/out/eval_after_fix.json).\n  - TODO after the reset: live smoke, then a manager status line with the friend's sentence before and after.\n\n**Worktree branches (merge in this order):**\n1. Photo fit, live bug 1 (agent a3799e92ab8ab5a63, worktree-agent-a3799e92ab8ab5a63): I1Invite, H2Develop, H3Send and PhotoPrint, the dark-photo display filter, the private chip on one line and remembered once closed, the e2e:photo-fit overlap gate under 25% at 390x664, 375x667 and 390x844, and before/after shots in docs/frontend/evidence/photo-fit/. The manager wants the 390x664 before/after shots once it's live. \"Fuego is at Near [street]\" grammar (fix 4) is NOT done yet: it's the lead's job, for invite.where, invite.whereWalk, lit.notice, push.lit and sms.lit, with a test over street, park and bench spots.\n2. Share, live bug 4 (agent a26567a1d6d5b923c, worktree-agent-a26567a1d6d5b923c): navigator.share synchronous in the tap after the Flare exists, a real wa.me anchor, Copy link fallback with a toast, WebKit slow-network test, docs/frontend/evidence/share-matrix.md (honest about real devices).\n3. site-motion (agent a1ac31aa2d2a5e6f7, branch site-motion, a3e295f mergeable): Why it matters (4 charts from primary sources; Surgeon General numbers NOT used, hhs.gov 403), Start in a minute, Crew space, Running now (copy-lint bans \"right now\"), Try it on your photo, the scroll story. Lighthouse mobile home perf was 99 and being tuned.\n4. app-motion (paused, worktree-agent-a5311b695b3086d89 at 4119624, rebased on 7792e2c). After merging:\n   - wire H5HostKindling `ember`, H0Home `at` = homeAt, and wind later;\n   - rerun npm test, e2e demo/sparks/loop, axe and perf;\n   - take the after shots and GIFs (tools/motion/).\n   - Budget on its last full build: 146.7 / 146.8 KB.\n5. post-rework (worktree-agent-a0e24f31091a79c08 at 5e2e6a5): docs/post only, about 1,585 words, 6 of 8 images, holes listed in its commit. It's paused; the holes get filled after the freeze.\n\n**Still to do:** the Near-X grammar; Sounds of the spot (waiting on lab numbers); Remember this stays OFF unless the consent tests pass by 1 AM; fresh-eyes round 6 (testers use their own dark photo, plus the WhatsApp-poll question, answers quoted verbatim); gates after the merges (Lighthouse 100, axe 0, budget under 150 KB, CSP, smoke); post holes after the freeze.\n\n'''\ns=s.replace('# Resume note\\n\\n','',1)\nopen(p,'w').write(new+s)\nEOF\ngit add docs/handoffs/RESUME.md && git commit -qm \"RESUME: state before the 9:50 PM usage reset\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && echo ok","description":"Write RESUME.md and commit"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1660,"cache_read_input_tokens":151321,"output_tokens":1807,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":46},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1660,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1807,"cache_read_input_tokens":151321,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1660,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1660},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_012iZdscYD5H2kVL3iudZjps":{"command":"cd \"<project>/flare\" && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='docs/handoffs/RESUME.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nnew='''# Resume note\n\n## Now: Sun 2026-10-11, ~9:15 PM ET, usage-limit pause (resets 9:50 PM ET). Read this first.\nFreeze 1:00 AM ET. Deadline Mon 06:59 UTC. Order: live bugs 1 to 4, then site clarity, then the rest.\n\n**Main (live, deploy started for 2751410 + format fix):**\n- 7792e2c Automations: Again on Home (last crew size, no photo, place words), Telegram-linked Send posts directly with no share sheet, auto I'm here within 30 m on 2 good fixes with a 10 s Undo.\n- 2751410 Live bugs 2 and 3, conditions:\n  - \"10min\" and the other delay phrasings are read as a delay;\n  - a bare hour picks the next one coming;\n  - \"with you\" means the host;\n  - missed words are said back (\"I didn't catch: ...\");\n  - tap-to-fill chips from the time of day and the host;\n  - cond.didntCatchNow replaces the fixed hint on screen. cond.didntCatch (SRS-COND-8) is unchanged and is still what parseError returns.\n  - Tests: apps/web/test/ai/conditions-live.test.ts, 10 tests including a fast-check property. blind_40 30/40 before and after; core 40/40, hard_20 20/20, fresh 40/40 (ml/tinker/out/eval_after_fix.json).\n  - TODO after the reset: live smoke, then a manager status line with the friend's sentence before and after.\n\n**Worktree branches (merge in this order):**\n1. Photo fit, live bug 1 (agent a3799e92ab8ab5a63, worktree-agent-a3799e92ab8ab5a63): I1Invite, H2Develop, H3Send and PhotoPrint, the dark-photo display filter, the private chip on one line and remembered once closed, the e2e:photo-fit overlap gate under 25% at 390x664, 375x667 and 390x844, and before/after shots in docs/frontend/evidence/photo-fit/. The manager wants the 390x664 before/after shots once it's live. \"Fuego is at Near [street]\" grammar (fix 4) is NOT done yet: it's the lead's job, for invite.where, invite.whereWalk, lit.notice, push.lit and sms.lit, with a test over street, park and bench spots.\n2. Share, live bug 4 (agent a26567a1d6d5b923c, worktree-agent-a26567a1d6d5b923c): navigator.share synchronous in the tap after the Flare exists, a real wa.me anchor, Copy link fallback with a toast, WebKit slow-network test, docs/frontend/evidence/share-matrix.md (honest about real devices).\n3. site-motion (agent a1ac31aa2d2a5e6f7, branch site-motion, a3e295f mergeable): Why it matters (4 charts from primary sources; Surgeon General numbers NOT used, hhs.gov 403), Start in a minute, Crew space, Running now (copy-lint bans \"right now\"), Try it on your photo, the scroll story. Lighthouse mobile home perf was 99 and being tuned.\n4. app-motion (paused, worktree-agent-a5311b695b3086d89 at 4119624, rebased on 7792e2c). After merging:\n   - wire H5HostKindling `ember`, H0Home `at` = homeAt, and wind later;\n   - rerun npm test, e2e demo/sparks/loop, axe and perf;\n   - take the after shots and GIFs (tools/motion/).\n   - Budget on its last full build: 146.7 / 146.8 KB.\n5. post-rework (worktree-agent-a0e24f31091a79c08 at 5e2e6a5): docs/post only, about 1,585 words, 6 of 8 images, holes listed in its commit. It's paused; the holes get filled after the freeze.\n\n**Still to do:** the Near-X grammar; Sounds of the spot (waiting on lab numbers); Remember this stays OFF unless the consent tests pass by 1 AM; fresh-eyes round 6 (testers use their own dark photo, plus the WhatsApp-poll question, answers quoted verbatim); gates after the merges (Lighthouse 100, axe 0, budget under 150 KB, CSP, smoke); post holes after the freeze.\n\n'''\ns=s.replace('# Resume note\\n\\n','',1)\nopen(p,'w').write(new+s)\nEOF\ngit add docs/handoffs/RESUME.md && git commit -qm \"RESUME: state before the 9:50 PM usage reset\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && echo ok","description":"Write RESUME.md and commit"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"86079c9e-4241-412c-91e8-498ae856f1dd","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfwQSkDUupxQW74U4HGWy","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"1e1a5fd5-71e8-4937-8ede-01102ef94212","timestamp":"2026-10-12T00:35:14.885Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"<project>/flare","sessionId":"904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"wondrous-tumbling-meteor"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-12T00:35:18.961Z","sessionId":"904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa","content":"<cross-session-message from=\"uds:<socket>\" from-session=\"local_beb3cc8c-e162-46cc-bd0a-f870e8717ebd\" from-name=\"Flare Manager(founders CTO)\" from-mode=\"prompting\">\nLive bug 5: the founder got no buzz when friends said yes. The host was in Brave on an iPhone, not on the Home Screen.\n\nThe cause is our copy: sent.body promises \"Phone in your pocket. We'll buzz you when it's lit.\" An iPhone browser tab can't vibrate, and gets no push unless Flare is added to the Home Screen and alerts are allowed. That's a promise we can't keep.\n\nFix:\n1. Only say \"We'll buzz you\" when this device actually has a live push subscription.\n2. Otherwise, right after Send, show one honest choice:\n   - \"Keep this open and the sound on\"\n   - \"Add Flare to your Home Screen for a buzz\", with the 2-step iOS instructions, then the permission ask\n   - if the crew is linked to Telegram, \"Telegram will ping the group\"\n3. On returning to the page (visibilitychange), show at once what happened while away, with the lit sound if audio was unlocked: \"2 friends said yes. It's lit.\"\n4. Put the state in the tab title (\"It's lit · Flare\"), and call setAppBadge on Home Screen installs.\n5. Add a test that the sent screen never shows the buzz promise without a subscription.\n\nAlso, I see lib/motion/flame-gl.ts on app-motion. WebGL wasn't in the brief, so check it against the JS budget, the iPhone 13 trace and reduced motion. Cut it if it fails any of them.\n</cross-session-message>"}
